window.IH_RACES = [{"id":"prime-mundane-human","name":"Human","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Normal human, plain and featureless. A blank slate full of potential.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":["Queen Eirene (Ryke)","Duke Thaddeus Halgorn Seroria","Count Bartholomew Ironwright","Baron Ludd Garanth","Countess Isolde of Valyra","Emperor Tiberian Valerius (Otenzian Empire (East))"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves into: Exemplar","Titles: Prime (tree), Human (race)","Features: Medium size","Skills: Choose 1:","Two (2) magic skills or affinities","Two (2) martial skills or techniques","Two (2) secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"Exemplar","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-human-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-human-2.webp"],"aliases":["Human","Human (race)","Prime (tree)"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-aerial","name":"Aerial","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"A human with wings capable of flight. It’s unknown if they are descended from avian people or demigods or if the wings are a spontaneous evolution. Many find employment in the Otenzian Empire (East) as couriers, but a larger population exists in Ryke due to the Empire's human supremacy mindset causing less favorable treatment at times. They have also been seen acting as scouts in the northern desert regions of the Ororoot Empire (West) as well. Many more aerials are said to have fallen from the sky at random locations throughout the Second Continent.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Aerials possess the same range of body types as humans, but generally have a leaner build that is crucial for flight, especially over long distances. Muscular aerials typically excel at short bursts of speed, while leaner aerials are better suited for long distance flight. It is possible for an aerial to become too obese to fly. Evolution typically increases wing strength.","coloring":"Aerial wings typically resemble those of birds of prey (hawks, vultures, owls, and falcons), especially in form. Most common colorings are browns and tans, grays, black, whites and creams, reds and rusts, and most rarely blues. There is speculation that wing color hints at various lineages (ex: white wings being angels/divine) and possibly predicts what an aerial could potentially evolve into, but nothing conclusive has been determined.","historicalFigures":["Baron Regula Caelia (Ryke)"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42+ points","Evolves into: Valkyrie","Titles: Prime, Aerial","Features:","Medium size","[Wings] - Paired appendages capable of flight. Requires Flight skill to actually fly.","Stats: Precision - C (21)","Skills:","Flight F (21)","2 Secondary Skill","Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","2 martial skills/techniques","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle"],"evolvesInto":"Valkyrie","totalCost":"42+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-aerial-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-aerial-2.webp"],"aliases":["Aerial"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-draconian","name":"Draconian","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Humans with dragon heritage descended from the dragonborn. The bloodline is heavily diluted, leaving their appearance mostly human, but manifestations of the draconic heritage can still take form. Such manifestations may be superior physical abilities, superhuman healing, magical aptitude, and, more rarely, partial draconic transformation. Draconians are among the longest lived races in the Prime tree, which often causes them to be prideful and arrogant, even when dealing with races from their own tree.","lifespan":"150 years","height":"Male: 5' 5\" to 6' 4\" (165.1--193.04 cm) Female: 5' to 6' (152.4--182.88 cm)","weight":"Male: 180--240 lbs (82--109 kg) Female: 170--220 lbs (77--100 kg)","physique":"Generally, draconians have a strong, athletic build, reflecting their draconic heritage. They are often well-defined with broad shoulders and a strong core. Prominent cheekbones, pronounced jaws. Strong arms and legs, often with claw-like fingers and toes for added grip and combat effectiveness. Many draconians have a tail, which can aid in balance and expressiveness. Some may have vestigial wings or large wings that can be used for gliding or flight, adding to their imposing appearance.","coloring":"Often covered in a layer of scales or tough skin, which can vary in color (greens, reds, blues, etc.) depending on the type of dragon.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly to dragon lineage races","Antagonistic towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49+ points","Titles: Prime, Draconian","Features:","Medium size","[Scales] - Naturally occurring reptilian scales that cover exterior surfaces of the body.","[Partial] - The above feature is only intermittently present.","[Horns] - (optional) - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Tail] (optional) - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","[Type] Affinity - E (14)","Regeneration - F (7)","2 secondary skills","Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","2 martial skills/techniques","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirement will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"49+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-draconian-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-draconian-2.webp"],"aliases":["Draconian"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-marinoid","name":"Marinoid","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Marinoids are a subspecies of human that has adapted to living underwater. Webbing and various fin-like formations assist and strengthen their movement through water. While they are able to come ashore, their home is beneath the waves. The magic they wield is typically frowned upon for its chaotic roots stemming from beings that were cast out of this dimension eons ago. Siren songs and their enchanting nature are an example of this so-called \"deep magic\" that the surface has learned to fear.","lifespan":"130 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Marinoids often have features reminiscent of aquatic creatures, such as webbed fingers, scales, or fins. Overall, their forms are lean, focusing on a hydrodynamic build. Large, expressive eyes that may have nictitating membranes, allowing for excellent underwater vision. Marinoids are usually adept swimmers, able to move quickly in water. They possess gills or the ability to hold their breath for extended periods. Males are generally more muscular and robust, reflecting strength for tasks like hunting or defending territory. They may have larger or more elaborate fins or crests that display dominance or attract females. Females are often leaner and more streamlined in form, which may aid in agility and swimming. Females commonly exhibit magical aptitude, especially with healing and water manipulation magics. Females may develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young.","coloring":"Skin tones range from deep blues and greens to lighter, iridescent shades. Males might have more vibrant colors or patterns to attract mates. Females might have softer, more muted colors, enhancing camouflage in their environment.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect water fae races","Friendly towards water-dwelling races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49+ points","Titles: Prime, Marinoid","Features:","Medium size","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Gills] (7) - Slits typically in the throat region that allow for breathing underwater.","[Nictitating Membrane] (7) (optional) - membrane that forms an inner eyelid that can be drawn across the eye to protect it from dust and keep it moist, possibly granting bonuses to resist blinding effects, avoid blinking, or gain a bonus to vision-based activities underwater.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Swim Speed F (7)","Supersense F [Hydrodynamics] (7)","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","2 martial skills/techniques","2 secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirement will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"49+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-marinoid-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-marinoid-2.webp"],"aliases":["Marinoid"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-moon-blessed-vampire","name":"Moon-blessed Vampire","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"A species of Vampire that has been blessed with vampirism as opposed to being cursed with it. This manner of receiving vampirism allows the recipient to retain their normal human appearance and [Prime] title. Additionally, while it does slightly increase the individual's lifespan compared to normal humans, it does not immediately grant immortality. Unlike their cursed counterparts, Moon-Blessed Vampires feed on the blood of monsters. Even so, Moon-Blessed Vampires are still distrusted and considered outcasts due to their need for blood. Furthermore, Moon-Blessed Vampires cannot control their thirst or bloodlust when around monsters, entering an enraged state where they will lash out at said monsters.","lifespan":"130 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Moon-blessed vampires are virtually indistinguishable from normal humans aside from their fangs. After receiving the blessing, their bodies may experience diminished digestive function, hampering their ability to process normal foods, thereby satisfying thirst and hunger. The inability to satisfy these cravings inflames and instills the need to consume blood, particularly the blood of monsters. Combat skills are bolstered for a short time after feeding.","coloring":"Their eyes turn red when they consume blood, or when they enter a frenzied state from prolonged blood deprivation. Very rarely, the otherwise normal skin might have a slight shimmering or silvery appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect other Moon-blessed, Moon-aligned races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 35/42+ points","Evolves into: Moon-Ordained Vampire","Titles: Prime, Moon-blessed Vampire","Features:","Medium size","[Fangs] (Cosmetic) - Elongated canine teeth used to puncture flesh and draw blood.","[Blood Drinker] (7) - Feature Skill - Creature derives nutrition from drinking the blood of other creatures.","Stats: Strength OR Intelligence E (7)","Skills:","Choose 1:","Fighting Style F (7) + Technique [Vampiric, Blight (Ice/Holy/Bleed)] (21) (21)","Affinity [Vampiric, Blight (Ice/Holy/Bleed)] F (14)","Equipment: Weapon/Catalyst with the prefix of [Moon-Blessed] eg. Moon-blessed Weapon/Catalyst. (7)","“A weapon that has been bathed in moonlight and takes on its subtle glow. A badge","of honor, a partner, and a symbol of the lunar blessing.”","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirement will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"Moon-Ordained Vampire","totalCost":"35/42+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-moon-blessed-vampire-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-moon-blessed-vampire-2.webp"],"aliases":["Moon-blessed Vampire"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-nephilim","name":"Nephilim","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Nephilim are the offspring of a human and a supernatural entity. The story usually goes that the parent met a stranger by happenstance and was bewitched by their unnatural beauty. There may have been a handful of benign encounters with the individual, but, after a night of passion, the stranger disappears without another word. The child born is usually gifted with supernatural sight and suffers visions of things beyond the natural world. It’s common that these children end up in the care of monasteries and various temples in hopes that a divine discipline can give them direction in these matters. If the supernatural entity is the mother, the child is deposited on the doorstep of a temple without ever knowing either parent. Many attempt to gouge out their eyes hoping to end the visions. Others suffer supernatural transplants in which one or both eyes are crudely removed and replaced with inhuman eyes.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 130--190 lbs (59--86 kg) Female: 110--170 lbs (50--77 kg)","physique":"Nephilim are usually quite lean, bordering on malnourished.","coloring":"One or both eyes may be an unnatural color typically on the yellow, orange, or red spectrum. Scarring may be present around the eyes that weeps blood when drawing near to divine/demonic/angelic sources or entities. In the absence of scarring, the eyes are usually sunken and deep shadows or fatigue lines are clearly visible.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect divine races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 28+ points","Titles: Prime, Nephilim","Features: Medium size","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Sixth Sense [type] F (7)","Religion F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"28+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-nephilim-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-nephilim-2.webp"],"aliases":["Nephilim"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-nhevian","name":"Nhevian","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Nhevians are the modern precursor to giants. The diluted bloodline distanced this iteration of giant from the elemental-infusions and upper limits of the large stature common to the purebloods, but Nhevians often evolve into these traits after exposing themselves to the right catalyst. Many Nhevians and other giants are employed by the Otenzian Empire (East), but the largest demographic of Nhevians and giantkin can be found in the middle to northern portions of the mountain range that divides the Empire from the Republic and Ryke. There are a handful in the Kingdom as well. It's not uncommon for Nhevians to join the Adventurer's Guild, so they are seen here and there around the Second Continent.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 7' to 7' 11\" (213.36--241.3 cm) Female: 6' 11\" to 7' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 260--370 lbs (118--168 kg) Female: 240--350 lbs (109--159 kg)","physique":"Nhevians possess a robust and powerful physique, with well-defined muscles that reflect their strength and endurance. Their shoulders are wide, giving them an imposing presence without appearing overly bulky. They have elongated arms and legs, providing them with a graceful yet powerful gait. Their hands and feet are proportionally larger than those of other Prime tree races, aiding in their ability to handle heavy objects and traverse rugged terrain. A prominent jaw and high cheekbones give them a rugged, noble appearance. They have large, expressive eyes that can range in color, often reflecting the natural elements around them, such as greens and browns. Some may have patches of tougher skin or natural armor-like growths that provide additional protection. Their physique allows them to adapt to various environments, making them proficient climbers and swimmers.","coloring":"Hair is thick and coarse, often worn long or in braids.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elemental giant races","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree","Neutral towards Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 56+ points","Titles: Prime, Nhevian","Features: Medium size","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Superstrength F (14)","Athletics F (7)","Climbing F (7)","Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","1 martial skills/techniques","Equipment: (optional) Natural Armor (Heavy)(14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirement will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"56+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-nhevian-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-nhevian-2.webp"],"aliases":["Nhevian"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-ork","name":"Ork","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"A human subspecies that is more primal in nature. Prizing strength over any other trait, the ork tribes are known to be formidable in battle. Despite revering strength, some orcs worship deities and are granted magical power. Orks are primarily found in the northern regions of the Ororoot Empire (West), where they can indulge in their combative tendencies more freely between the Kingdom's border to the north and the more civilized regions south of the Empire's deserts.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 6' to 7' (1.8 to 2.1 m) Female: 5' 6\" to 6' 6\" (1.7 to 2.0 m)","weight":"Male: 250--350 lbs (113--159 kg) Female: 150--250 lbs (68--113 kg)","physique":"Orks have a robust and powerful physique, with broad shoulders and strong limbs. Their bodies are often described as stocky, with a solid frame that emphasizes strength and endurance. Males are typically larger and more muscular, often being larger and bulkier. Strong, angular features with a pronounced jaw. Typically, males have larger tusks protruding from the lower jaw, while females may have smaller or less pronounced tusks. Large, expressive eyes, often in shades of yellow or red, conveying a fierce or cunning demeanor. Females are generally smaller and leaner, though still strong and capable. Males often have more pronounced features, such as larger tusks, brow ridges, and overall ruggedness. Females may have softer facial features, though still retain some of the characteristic orcish traits. Thick and coarse, often worn long or in braids. Hair colors can range from black to dark brown or even gray. Males may have thick beards or sideburns, while females might have less facial hair.","coloring":"Skin tones span the usual human range, but may manifest in various shades of green. The skin may have a rough or tough texture, providing some natural armor against environmental elements.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect warrior races","Neutral towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42+ points","Titles: Prime, Ork","Feature:","Medium size","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Tusks] - Elongated canines on the bottom jaw that may protrude through the lips.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - D (14)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Fighting Style F (7)","Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","1 martial skill/technique","2 secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-ork-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-ork-2.webp"],"aliases":["Ork"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-warbound","name":"Warbound","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"The Warbound, or Heartbound, are one of the three Bound races. This version is tied to the Heart and a red aesthetic as hinted by their naturally deep red hair. They have an obsession with all things red as it is the color of blood, which is life itself. Heartbound loathe fire as it withers the blood. In this Bound race, the women are notably stronger than the males. Even so, Warbound are a hearty race known for their tough skin and aptitude for hand-to-hand combat. Often born during times of war or strife, they possess a natural inclination to fight or be combative. A Warbound's tactics capitalize on their unnatural strength, making them ideal frontline soldiers. For this cause, many militant factions seek them out in order to bolster their ranks.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Despite having mostly normal builds for humans, the females are inexplicably stronger than the males by a grade or two.","coloring":"Skin tone may have a reddish tint. Hair is always a deep shade of red. Some manifest a birthmark that resembles a scar though they never sustained such an injury.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84+ points","Titles: Prime, Warbound","Features:","Medium size","[Red Hair] - Hair is naturally red","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Superstrength F (14)","Fighting Style F (7) - [Warbound Berserker] (Natural Weapons - Martial Arts/Hand to Hand)","2 Tech Cores of choice","Leadership F (7)","Warfare F (7)","Equipment:","Natural Armor F (14)","Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-warbound-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-warbound-2.webp"],"aliases":["Warbound"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-witch","name":"Witch","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"A race of all females, witches possess a strong connection to magic. The oddity of this synergy is only rivaled by their exaggerated features. Witches are reluctant to test their limits and often specialize in specific kinds of magic.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"From hunched old croons to unnaturally elegant and youthful ladies, witches vary greatly in appearance. Most learn and maintain magics that grant a youthful appearance. Even so, most witches are physically weak and die in the same ways as other mortals.","coloring":"Mana veins might visibly glow blue beneath a witch’s skin due to her potent connection to magic.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70+ points","Titles: Prime, Witch","Features: Medium size","Stats: Intelligence - D (14)","Skills:","Componentless magic E (42)","Magic E (14)","2 magic affinities F","1 Secondary skill F","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"70+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-witch-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-witch-2.webp"],"aliases":["Witch"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-wodewise","name":"Wodewise","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"Wodewise are humans with an overly large head. Like the wodewose, wodewise are humans left to survive in the wilderness, however, this brand of feral human adapted to the elements in the forests of the Fae See. Whether they made a genuine connection with an ancient power or went mad from the fungi, these feral humans have awakened their magical ability. Though generally more composed than the wodewose, the wodewise can lash out unexpectedly as the means by which they obtained their magic often comes with aggressive ticks or compulsions.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63+ points","Evolves into: Diwose","Titles: Prime, Wodewise","Features: Medium size","Stats:","Character Grade - E","Intelligence D (14)","Skills:","Magic E (14)","Telepathy F (21)","Sixth Sense [type] F (7)","Focus F (21)","Choose one:","1 magic skills/affinities","2 martial skills/techniques","1 secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"Diwose","totalCost":"63+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-wodewise-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-wodewise-2.webp"],"aliases":["Wodewise"]},{"id":"prime-mundane-wodewose","name":"Wodewose","tree":"Prime","stage":"Mundane","description":"A human left to fend for itself in the wild. More primitive than its city-dwelling kin, this creature has sacrificed social prowess for physical might and rugged endurance. May find it easier to win the approval of races that prize such things. Females are exceedingly rare.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Wodewose adapt to their environment. Cooler climates might see them retain fat, while warmer climates might encourage a leaner build. In any environment, wodewose are covered in unkempt body hair and head and facial hair is kept shaggy. Hands and feet are heavily calloused.","coloring":"There is a healthy radiance to their complexion, marked by a sense of vitality and resilience. The skin may have a slight sheen from sweat or natural oils, and its texture is slightly rougher, with a few visible imperfections such as freckles or sun spots. Additionally, the skin could exhibit fine lines or wrinkles, especially around the eyes and forehead.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49+ points","Evolves into: Diwose","Titles: Prime, Wodewose","Features: [Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Character Grade - E","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Climbing F (7)","Intimidation (7)","Nature (7)","Survival (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on one skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Versatile - choose melee weapons, ranged weapons, or catalyst. Permanently change governing stat to strength, precision, or intelligence instead of normal stat. Fighting style and magic stat requirements will change to match. Ex: Catalyst that uses strength and magic skill that uses strength for a wizard of muscle."],"evolvesInto":"Diwose","totalCost":"49+ points","images":["assets/races/prime-mundane-wodewose-1.webp","assets/races/prime-mundane-wodewose-2.webp"],"aliases":["Wodewose"]},{"id":"prime-intermediate-diwose","name":"Diwose","tree":"Prime","stage":"Intermediate","description":"A fusion occurs between a wodewose and a wodewise, causing the two to share one body with the heads fused together on the innermost side. The resulting creature is called a diwose. The instinct of the wodewose and the higher mind of the wodewise vie for control, causing the creature’s already unstable actions to become even more dangerous and unpredictable. The need for survival can compel the sides to cooperate, like obtaining food or escaping/killing predators, but the conflicting natures are mortal enemies seeking dominance of the form at all cost.","lifespan":"1 year","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Wodewose adapt to their environment. Cooler climates might see them retain fat, while warmer climates might encourage a leaner build. In any environment, wodewose are covered in unkempt body hair and head and facial hair is kept shaggy. Hands and feet are heavily calloused.","coloring":"There is a healthy radiance to their complexion, marked by a sense of vitality and resilience. The skin may have a slight sheen from sweat or natural oils, and its texture is slightly rougher, with a few visible imperfections such as freckles or sun spots. Additionally, the skin could exhibit fine lines or wrinkles, especially around the eyes and forehead.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Wodewose, Wodewise","Evolves into: Fellhuman, Wizern","Titles: Prime, Wodewose/Wodewise, Diwose","Feature:","[Multiple Heads: 2] (7) - Creature has multiple heads. Cannot be blinded except by AOE effects or blinding abilities that hit all heads.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E","Intelligence - C","Skills:","Heightened Sense [Type] E","Magic D","Sixth Sense [type] E","Telepathy D","Climbing","Focus E","Survival","1 Secondary skill","1 C-grade Magic skill","Perk 1: [Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Perk 2: Gain 1 C-grade Asset (common examples: faction standing, real estate, or specifical npc connection of a skilled individual like a veteran mage/solder/merchant/clergy)"],"evolvesInto":"Fellhuman, Wizern","totalCost":"","images":[],"aliases":["Diwose","Wodewise","Wodewose"]},{"id":"prime-intermediate-exemplar","name":"Exemplar","tree":"Prime","stage":"Intermediate","description":"The height of mortal Man is the exemplar. Fast, strong, and intelligent, the exemplar has raised its stats as far as humanly possible. With hands firmly pressed against the evolutionary ceiling, there is but one thing left to do: break through.","lifespan":"180 years","height":"Male: 6' 0\" to 6' 3\" (183–191 cm) Female: 5'6\" to 5'9\" (168–175 cm)","weight":"Male: 180–220 lbs (82–100 kg) Female: 140–180 lbs (64–82 kg)","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Human","Evolves into: Paragon","Titles: Prime, Human, Exemplar","Features: Medium size","Stats:","1 A-grade","1 B-grade","3 C-grade","Skills:","1 C-grade skill","4 secondary skills aside from the C-grade skill","Perk 1: [Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Perk 2: Gain 1 C-grade Asset (common examples: faction standing, real estate, or specific npc connection of a skilled individual like a veteran mage/solder/merchant/clergy)"],"evolvesInto":"Paragon","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-intermediate-exemplar-1.webp","assets/races/prime-intermediate-exemplar-2.webp"],"aliases":["Exemplar","Human"]},{"id":"prime-intermediate-moon-ordained-vampire","name":"Moon-Ordained Vampire","tree":"Prime","stage":"Intermediate","description":"A Moon-Blessed Vampire evolves into a Moon-Ordained Vampire once they reach a certain stage in their growth. Having learned to control their thirst and bloodlust around monsters, this intermediate race is well-suited to the art of demon hunting. Blessed by the moon this race excels at combat focused around the culling of monster species and with their vampirism taking a more firm hold on their being, their appearance is mystifyingly beautiful. A beauty that makes other non-monster races far more accepting of them than before.","lifespan":"150 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Moon-ordained vampires maintain a youthful plumpness to their flesh, which turns increasingly more milky white over time after evolving to the Intermediate tier. Though their bodies do not build muscle mass, they have remarkable strength and agility.","coloring":"Skin grows increasingly pale to milky-white. Dark-skinned races that receive the blessing become a shade of gray. Shimmering or silvery appearance becomes more dramatic, especially in moonlight.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Moon-Blessed Vampire","Evolves into: Lunae Electi","Title: Prime, Moon-Blessed Vampire, Moon-Ordained Vampire","Feature:","[Fangs] (Cosmetic) - Elongated canine teeth used to puncture flesh and draw blood.","[Blood Drinker] (7) - Creature derives nutrition from drinking the blood of other creatures.","Stats:","Character Grade - C","Strength/Precision - C","Intelligence - C","Speed/Vitality - C","Skills:","Heightened Sense - E [Smell, Sight]","Sixth Sense F - [Weakpoint Vision]","Regeneration F","Resilient F [Aging]","Any Movement Skill - F","4 secondary skills of your choice","Equipment: Moon Blessed Weapon - D","Perk 1: [Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Perk 2: Gain 1 C-grade Asset (common examples: faction standing, real estate, or specifical npc connection of a skilled individual like a veteran mage/solder/merchant/clergy)"],"evolvesInto":"Lunae Electi","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-intermediate-moon-ordained-vampire-1.webp","assets/races/prime-intermediate-moon-ordained-vampire-2.webp"],"aliases":["Moon-Blessed Vampire","Moon-Ordained Vampire"]},{"id":"prime-intermediate-valkyrie","name":"Valkyrie","tree":"Prime","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Valkyrie, an all-female race, are humanoids highly adept at flying and aerial combat. Though they are often mistaken for angels, the valkyrie are quite mortal but very specialized as one might expect of a once ascended creature.","lifespan":"150 years","height":"Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Valkyrie possess the same range of body types as humans, but generally are more muscular than aerials. Most notably, their wings are much stronger allowing for burst and endurance flights.","coloring":"Valkyrie wings typically resemble those of birds of prey (hawks, vultures, owls, and falcons), especially in form. Most common colorings are blends of gold, silver, and white, with a minority of earthen tones. Valkyrie wings become more radiant as they near evolution to the Ascended tier.","historicalFigures":["Baron Regula Caelia (Ryke)"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree","Antagonistic towards Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Aerial","Titles: Prime, Aerial, Valkyrie","Feature:","Medium size","[Wings] - Paired appendages capable of flight.","Stats:","Strength - C","Precision - A","Skills:","Flight D","Fighting Style D","1 C-grade skill","4 secondary skills aside from the C-grade skill","Perk 1: [Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Perk 2: Gain 1 C-grade Asset (common examples: faction standing, real estate, or specifical npc connection of a skilled individual like a veteran mage/solder/merchant/clergy)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-intermediate-valkyrie-1.webp","assets/races/prime-intermediate-valkyrie-2.webp"],"aliases":["Aerial","Valkyrie"]},{"id":"prime-ascended-fellhuman","name":"Fellhuman","tree":"Prime","stage":"Ascended","description":"The fellhuman is a legendary being that is the perfect marriage of Man and Beast. The raw strength and instincts of the beast are carefully honed and moderated by the awakened mind of Man, implementing every aspect of their ability with deadly focus and precision. Fellhumans are capable of speech but prefer telepathic communication, believing it to present the speaker in their truest form.","lifespan":"180 years","height":"Male: 6' to 7' (1.8 to 2.1 m) Female: 5' 6\" to 6' 6\" (1.7 to 2.0 m)","weight":"Male: 250--350 lbs (113--159 kg) Female: 150--250 lbs (68--113 kg)","physique":"Male Fellhumans exhibit unnaturally dense musculature for a humanoid, while the females are more sleek and streamlined in form. Even so, both possess great strength as well as other unnatural senses and abilities. Body hair is present over much of the body and commonly grows thicker more like a coat of fur. Horns, claws, tails and other accessory growths may manifest after evolution. It’s unclear if Fellhumans possess more than one pair of arms, are able to grow extra pairs of arms at will, or simply move fast enough to create after images of their appendages.","coloring":"Fellhumans commonly have grayish-brown skin, but color can vary widely depending on various factors, such as what medium the wodewise came into contact with that ignited their magical potential and the form of the bestial persona of wodewose. Similarly, eye color is commonly earthen tones, bright gold, or colorless, but can vary wildly based on the previously mentioned and other factors.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Diwose","Titles: Prime, Wodewose/Wodewise, Diwose, Fellhuman","Feature:","[Third Eye] (7) - A third eye, physical or ethereal, that gives the creature an awareness of its surroundings at all times. Cannot be surprised.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength S or Precision S or Vitality S","Intelligence - A","Speed - C","Skills:","Magic D","Heightened Sense [Type] D","Telepathy A","Sixth Sense [type] E","Focus E","Climbing","Survival","1 C-grade skill","3 secondary skill","Equipment: Natural Weapons C or [weapon] C","Perk 1: [Apex] - gain the title Apex. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","Perk 2: [Queen/King Bee] - gain the Queen/King Bee title. You are at the top of the species pecking order and considered a special existence. You are generally permitted audience with the leaders of factions and heads of state. Nations where your race is the majority tend to look to those of your grade for guidance or alliance.","Perk 3: Gain 1 S-grade Asset (common examples: Tops of faction standing, real estate like palaces and domains, or special npc connection of a god)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-ascended-fellhuman-1.webp","assets/races/prime-ascended-fellhuman-2.webp"],"aliases":["Diwose","Fellhuman","Wodewise","Wodewose"]},{"id":"prime-ascended-lunae-electi","name":"Lunae Electi","tree":"Prime","stage":"Ascended","description":"The final evolution of the Moon-Blessed Vampire. Lunae Electi are the moon's chosen ones. Extremely rare and under-documented this race is considered to be nothing more than fantasy and rumor. Little is known about how a Moon-Ordained Vampire actually goes about evolving into a Lunae Electi, but it goes without saying such a task must be exceptionally dangerous. The Lunae Electi are masters of monster extermination. A holy being that has risen to meet the wishes the moon once bestowed upon them and has made its blessing fully their own.","lifespan":"150 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Moon-ordained vampires maintain a youthful plumpness to their flesh, which turns increasingly more milky white over time after evolving to the Intermediate tier. Though their bodies do not build muscle mass, they have remarkable strength and agility.","coloring":"Skin grows increasingly pale to milky-white. Dark-skinned races that receive the blessing become a shade of gray. Shimmering or silvery appearance becomes more dramatic, especially in moonlight.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Moon-Ordained Vampire","Titles: Prime, Moon-blessed Vampire, Moon-ordained Vampire, Lunae Electi, Apex, Queen/King Bee","Feature:","[Fangs] (Cosmetic) - Elongated canine teeth used to puncture flesh and draw blood.","[Blood Drinker] (7) - Creature derives nutrition from drinking the blood of other creatures.","Stats:","1 S-grade stat","Character Grade - A","Skills:","1 S-grade Skill","Core/Affinity Aura [Holy/Ice/Holy Ice] - B","Weaken [Str/Int/Pre] - B","Selective B","Regeneration B","Resilient E [Aging + Surprise]","Always Outnumbered","6 secondary skills of your choice","Ability - Divine Authority [Aura B (Holy/Ice/Holy Ice), Weaken (Strength/Int/Precision) B, Vorpal, Selective]","“You are Lunae Electi! Let all who face you in battle know your authority! Bolster your allies, weaken your foes, and let all who dare approach you in opposition know pain.”","Equipment: Moon-Blessed Weapon - A","Gain S-grade Asset: Lunae Electi - You are connected to the Moon Gods and can commune with them","Quest - Slay an A-grade Demon Solo","6 secondary skills","Perk 1: [Apex] - gain the title [Apex]. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","Perk 2: [Queen/King Bee] - gain the [Queen/King Bee] title. You are at the top of the species pecking order and considered a special existence. You are generally permitted audience with the leaders of factions and heads of state. Nations where your race is the majority tend to look to those of your grade for guidance or alliance.","Perk 3: Gain 1 S-grade Asset (common examples: Tops of faction standing, real estate like palaces and domains, or special npc connection of a god)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-ascended-lunae-electi-1.webp","assets/races/prime-ascended-lunae-electi-2.webp"],"aliases":["Apex","King Bee","Lunae Electi","Moon-blessed Vampire","Moon-ordained Vampire","Queen"]},{"id":"prime-ascended-paragon","name":"Paragon","tree":"Prime","stage":"Ascended","description":"A legendary variant of human said to be the primary race of the world once upon a time. Very few are left.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 6' to 7' (1.8 to 2.1 m) Female: 5' 6\" to 6' 6\" (1.7 to 2.0 m)","weight":"Male: 250--350 lbs (113--159 kg) Female: 150--250 lbs (68--113 kg)","physique":"Paragons appear to be carved out of marble. Their flesh has been converted into a medium that allows for maximum flow of mana, removing the need for dedicated mana veins. They don't need to exercise to maintain or grow musculature as the medium comprising their form is freely manipulated by the individual. It’s questioned whether they even need to eat or drink.","coloring":"Paragons come in a whitish gray or deep black. Physical injuries appear as gold, blue, or white cracks, which is their mana working to repair the form. Males are typically bald, but females sometimes choose to manifest hair-like tendrils from their scalp.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Exemplar","Titles: Human, Exemplar, Paragon","Stats: 1 S-grade stat","Skills:","One (1) A-grade skill","Six (6) secondary skills.","Perk 1: [Apex] - gain the title Apex. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","Perk 2: [Queen/King Bee] - gain the Queen/King Bee title. You are at the top of the species pecking order and considered a special existence. You are generally permitted audience with the leaders of factions and heads of state. Nations where your race is the majority tend to look to those of your grade for guidance or alliance.","Perk 3: Gain 1 S-grade Asset (common examples: Tops of faction standing, real estate like palaces and domains, or special npc connection of a god)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-ascended-paragon-1.webp","assets/races/prime-ascended-paragon-2.webp"],"aliases":["Exemplar","Human","Paragon"]},{"id":"prime-ascended-wizern","name":"Wizern","tree":"Prime","stage":"Ascended","description":"Wizerns are powerful casters that seem to have a secondary presence, like a shadow, with them at all times. It can take any form but commonly manifests as a bestial humanoid that defends the wizern.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5' 3\" to 6' 2\" (160--188 cm) Female: 4' 10\" to 5' 10\" (147--178 cm)","weight":"Male: 140--300 lbs (63.5--136 kg) Female: 100--250 lbs (45.4--113.4 kg)","physique":"Wizerns are thin and physically underdeveloped.","coloring":"Body may sometimes appear as a shadowed silhouette despite being fully lit up.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Beast tree","Neutral towards Prime tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Diwose","Titles: Prime, Wodewose/Wodewise, Diwose, Wizern","Feature: [Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats: Intelligence - S","Skills:","Heightened Sense [Type] C","Magic S","Sixth Sense [type] C","Telepathy C","Climbing","Focus C","Survival","Companion F","Feature: [Living Shadow]","Perk 1: [Apex] - gain the title [Apex]. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","Perk 2: [Queen/King Bee] - gain the [Queen/King Bee] title. You are at the top of the species pecking order and considered a special existence. You are generally permitted audience with the leaders of factions and heads of state. Nations where your race is the majority tend to look to those of your grade for guidance or alliance.","Perk 3: Gain 1 S-grade Asset (common examples: Tops of faction standing, real estate like palaces and domains, or special npc connection of a god)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/prime-ascended-wizern-1.webp","assets/races/prime-ascended-wizern-2.webp"],"aliases":["Diwose","Wizern","Wodewise","Wodewose"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-lionkin","name":"Lionkin","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Lionkin originally hailed from the Ororoot Empire (West) where they were militant nomads that roamed the borders of the northern deserts. They eventually became enslaved and were sold to a merchant from the The Republic, who brought a handful back to his homeland. While the West Empire natives remained wild and militant, those that were raised in the Republic became more well-mannered and civilized.","lifespan":"77 years","height":"Male: 6' to 6' 10\" (184–208 cm) Female: 5' 3\" to 6' (160–184 cm)","weight":"Male: 411.3–496 lbs (186.55–225 kg) Female: 261–316.4 lb (118.37–143.52 kg)","physique":"Lionkin are the second-largest of the feline beastkin, after tigerkin. They are well-muscled with long bodies and large heads. Males are considerably larger than females. In short, powerful build, short coat, a distinctive mane on males, and a tail with a black tuft.","coloring":"Lionkin have short, tawny coats, typically buff yellow, orange-brown, or silvery gray to dark brown. Their underparts are usually lighter in color. Lionkin cubs have rosette spots that fade as they mature.","historicalFigures":["King Akio (Ryke)"],"relations":["Respect elephantkin","Neutral to lionkin","Equal to tigerkin, leopardkin","Antagonistic towards hyenakin, especially gnoll"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70 points","Titles: Beast, Lionkin","Feature:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Lion] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a lion.","[Muzzle] - The nose and mouth region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Intimidation F or Leadership F (7)","Heightened Sense E [Sight, Smell] (14)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"70 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-lionkin-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-lionkin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Lionkin"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-foxkin","name":"Foxkin","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Foxkin appear to mostly hail from the Republic and the northern territory that eventually became part of Ryke. Their speed and cunning made them enticing trophies for hunters and slavers alike. As a rule, foxkin generally avoid confrontation as they are among the smaller and lighter beastkin and usually lack the strength for a head-on fight. For these reasons, they became adept at stealth and sneak attacks if a fight is forced.","lifespan":"74 years","height":"Male: 3' to 5' 10\" (90–180 cm) Female: 3' to 5' 4\" (90--163 cm)","weight":"Male: 45–155 lbs (20.4--70.3 kg). Female: 40–145 lbs (18.1--65.8 kg)","physique":"Foxkin are generally lightly built, with comparatively long bodies for their mass. Pointed snout with sharp, keen eyes. Upright and triangular head. Slender and agile body type, built for speed and adaptability.","coloring":"Dense and bushy coat, with a mix of reddish-brown fur, white underbelly, and black markings on the legs and ears.","historicalFigures":["Princess Sakura (Ryke)"],"relations":["Respect wolfkin","Friendly with other small beastkin, such as raccoons, tanuki, red pandas, and rabbitkin","Antagonistic towards catkin","Hostile towards large dog races, like coyote, and predatory birdkin races"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70 points","Titles: Beast, Foxkin","Feature:","Small (<4’) or Medium (>4’) size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Fox] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a lion.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Heightened Sense [Sight, Hearing] E (14)","Acrobatics F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"70 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-foxkin-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-foxkin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Foxkin"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-fidoan","name":"Fidoan","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Fidoans are among the densest demographics of beastkin throughout the Second Continent. They are closely followed by wolfkin and other canine type beastkin. It is unclear where the Fidoans originated from, but the name of the race resembles an old pet name for dogs used by humans. Even so, they are commonly found among samurai clans in the Republic. Generally speaking, Fidoans are seen as adaptable, but their true strength lies in the natural sturdiness of their frames. It has been found that they are very efficient at shaking off various effects from techniques used on them. Wolfkin are seen as a higher evolution among Fidoans, so it is common to see Fidoans modify their ears to appear more like those of wolfkin.","lifespan":"89 years","height":"Male: 4'1\" to 7' 11\" (124.46–241.3 cm) Female: 4'1\" to 7'7\" (124.46–231.14 cm)","weight":"Male: 130–350 lbs (59--159 kg) Female: 100–325 lbs (45.36--147.42 kg)","physique":"Fidoans can be lean, muscular, or stocky. They typically have broad and deep chests, allowing for lung capacity. Medium to taller specimens typically have long legs, which allow them to run fast, while shorter specimens have compact proportions built for strength reminiscent of other short races, such as dwarves and gnomes. Head shape can vary from a slender form similar to foxkin to a broad form closer to those of bearkin and lionkin. Fidoan tails are just as varied, coming long, short, curled, or straight, but the fur of the tail and elsewhere on the body is typically not as bushy as that of wolfkin or foxkin. While there is significant variation, the average Fidoan physique is characterized by a balanced proportion of muscle, bone, and fat, reflecting its function and adaptability to different environments.","coloring":"Common base colors include black, brown, white, gray, and cream. Coloring comes in solid, brindle, merle, and sable patterns. Markings creating specific looks are described as piebald, tuxedo, mask, and spotting.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect wolfkin","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards cat races, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree, enemies of friends"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77 points","Titles: Beast, Fidoan","Feature:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Dog] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a dog.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Duration Reduction F OR Resistance [type] F OR Resilience [type] F (7)","Heightened Sense [Smell, Sight] E (14)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-fidoan-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-fidoan-2.webp"],"aliases":["Fidoan"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-lizardkin","name":"Lizardkin","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Lizardkin are the result of what were once three distinct tribes of reptilian beast races: the Iguanids, strong swimmers with sturdy frames, the Gexos, nigh unstoppable climbers with darkvision and the ability to regrow their tails, and the Chamaelian, gifted with adaptable camouflage, incredible vision, long tongues, and prehensile tails that could function as an extra limb. Originally, these tribes existed in pockets near mountains, deserts, and a few islands off the coast of the Second Continent. Upon the slavers of the West and East empires finding them, they were brought together en masse for the first time. It was found that these three races had unheard of compatibility with one another that allowed their offspring to quickly take on new traits and evolutions in as little as the first or second generation. Forced reproduction between carefully selected mates eventually led to the modern day lizardkin which possesses many, if not all, of the traits from their ancestor tribes.","lifespan":"82 years","height":"Male: 5'5\" to 6' 5\" (165–196 cm) Female: 4'1” to 5' (122–152 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–210 lbs (68--95 kg) Female: 100–110 lbs (45--50 kg)","physique":"Males typically have broader, more robust heads compared to the more slender heads of females. Males have larger and more prominent dewlaps (the flap of skin under the throat). Males often have more pronounced spines along their backs. If the lizardkin possesses a tail, it is either thick and powerful for swimming or slender and dextrous for grasping. Overall musculature appears lean compared to other Beast races and even some Prime races. Females may develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young.","coloring":"All lizardkin can have patterns in striped, spotted, or mottled variations. Colors vary depending on what tribe the lizardkin is descended from as follows: Iguanid - Green (Common), Brown (Common), Blue (Uncommon), Orange/Yellow (Rare) Gexos - Brown/Tan (Common), Green (Uncommon), Red/Yellow (Rare), Blue (Very Rare) Chamaelian - Default coloring is most commonly green, but is freely changed","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Larger reptile races, Serpentkin, Birds of Prey (Eagle, Hawk, Falcon, Owl), Big Cat races (Tiger, Lion, Jaguar, Leopard)","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42+ points","Titles: Beast, Lizardman","Feature:","Medium size","[Scales] - Skin is totally covered in reptilian scales.","[Ears: Reptilian] - A thin membrane located at the rear of the head.","[Eyes: Bestial] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Speed or Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Resilient [desert] F (7) or Swim Speed F (7) or Climbing F (7)","Athletics F (7)","2 Sense Skills","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42+ points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-lizardkin-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-lizardkin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Lizardkin","Lizardman"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-animal","name":"[animal]","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Most normal animals found in the world.","lifespan":"","height":"","weight":"","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":[],"relations":[],"requirements":["Titles: Beast, [animal name, e.g. wolf]","Feature skills to mimic the animals senses and appearance","Skills:","2 Sense Skills","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-animal-1.webp"],"aliases":["[animal]","animal name","e.g. wolf"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-anuran","name":"Anuran","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"This humanoid frog race embodies a blend of amphibian agility and human-like strength, making them well-adapted for both terrestrial and aquatic environments. Their physique allows for impressive jumping ability, speed, and dexterity, enabling them to thrive in diverse habitats. They are usually shorter before evolving but can gain a variety of features over time. Believed to have been created on the Dark Continent to serve as protectors for the eggs of an arachne. [Reference Image]","lifespan":"70 years","height":"Male: 4’1” to 5' (124–152 cm) Female: 4'6” to 5'5” (137–165 cm)","weight":"Male: 90–140 lbs (41--64 kg) Female: 115–150 lbs (52--68 kg)","physique":"A wider head with prominent, bulging eyes that provide excellent vision, especially in low light. A flattened snout that allows for efficient breathing and vocalization. A tapered waist that contributes to an agile appearance. Well-defined muscles, particularly in the legs and arms, allowing for powerful movements and agility. Proportionally long, strong legs adapted for jumping and leaping, with powerful thigh muscles. Relatively long arms with a strong grip, allowing for climbing and manipulation of objects. Toes may be slightly webbed, aiding in swimming, with strong pads for grip. Females may develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young.","coloring":"Skin is generally smooth and moist, reflecting typical amphibian characteristics, with a possible glossy sheen. Coloration varies widely, often featuring vibrant greens, yellows, or blues, which may help in camouflage.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Larger reptile races, Serpentkin, Birds of Prey (Eagle, Hawk, Falcon, Owl), Big Cat races (Tiger, Lion, Jaguar, Leopard)","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49+ points","Titles: Beast, Anuran","Feature:","Medium size","[Webbed Appendages] - The body has extra skin flaps that make swimming easier.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Long tongue] - A tongue long enough to be an additional arm for those coordinated enough to use it as such.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Jumping F (7)","Swim Speed F (7)","1 Sense Skills","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"49+ points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-anuran-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-anuran-2.webp"],"aliases":["Anuran"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-bunnykin","name":"Bunnykin","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Race of humanoid rabbit people said to hail from the Ororoot Empire (West). Some see them as stereotypically weak and cowardly, while others see them as peaceful and energetic workers. It is said that some tribes were driven eastward by slavers, raiders, and occasionally conflicts with other tribes. Having a set of powerful legs, bunnykin are well known for their speed and jumping capabilities.","lifespan":"75 years","height":"*Ear length excluded Male: 5’ to 6' (152–182 cm)* Female: 4'10” to 5'4” (147–162 cm)*","weight":"Male: 130–200 lbs (59–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Muscular yet agile, reflecting a balance between human-like musculature and the physical traits of rabbits. The body is well-proportioned with a slight emphasis on strong hindquarters for enhanced jumping ability (pear-shaped forms). Long, strong legs built for powerful leaps and agility. Arms are proportionate but slightly more muscular than a typical human's, allowing for climbing and manipulation of objects. Ears are prominent and upright, typically 6 to 12 inches long, providing exceptional hearing. They can move independently to express emotions or alertness. A small, fluffy tail, about 5 to 8 inches in length. The face may have rabbit-like features but mostly appears human.","coloring":"Soft and dense fur specifically covering the rabbit features, varying in color patterns (solid, spotted, or striped) that can provide camouflage or reflect their environment. Colors range from white to gray to earthen shades.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 35 points","Titles: Beast, Bunnykin","Feature:","Medium size","[Ears: Rabbit] (Cosmetic) - Tall Ears shaped like those of a rabbit, which often turn in different directions to keep track of multiple threats through sound.","[Tail: Rabbit] (Cosmetic) - A stubby and fluffy tail.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Jumping F (7)","Fast F (7)","Supersense [Multidirectional Hearing] F (7) OR Heightened Sense [Hearing] F (7)","Does not qualify for Mundane perks"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"35 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-bunnykin-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-bunnykin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Bunnykin"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-felisian-catfolk","name":"Felisian (Catfolk)","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Felisian are humanoid felines that are believed to have hailed from the west, though some historians insist that they arose from the southern fae country. Smaller and more agile than the wolfkin, the catkin are well-suited for climbing and running through obstacle courses, which might explain where the phrase \"cat burglar\" came from.","lifespan":"98 years","height":"Male: 5'0\" to 5'7\" (152–170 cm) Female: 4'5\" to 5'2\" (135–157 cm)","weight":"Male: 140–180 lbs (64–82 kg) Female: 90–130 lbs (41–59 kg)","physique":"An upright posture resembling humans, but with a more flexible spine, allowing for agility and graceful movement. Muscular yet lean, emphasizing strength and endurance, with well-defined muscles. Arms are proportionate to their height, with strong, muscular arms that allow for dexterity and climbing. Hands have retractable claws, resembling a cat’s paw but adapted for manipulation. Long, powerful hind legs, contributing to impressive jumping ability and agility. The structure supports both running and climbing, with well-developed thigh and calf muscles. A long, expressive tail (about 3 to 4 feet) that aids in balance and emotional expression, tapering to a point. The tail is muscular and flexible, allowing for precise movement in various terrains. Slightly elongated head with a flatter, more defined snout compared to humans. Large, expressive eyes that provide excellent [darkvision], typically in shades of green, gold, or blue. Pointed and tufted ears that can swivel independently, enhancing their hearing abilities and adding to their expressive nature. Posture is upright but slightly crouched, allowing for quick movements and agility. Movement is graceful and fluid, with a natural ability to [jump] and [climb].","coloring":"Soft, dense fur that is both warm and protective, varying in color and pattern based on individual genetics. Patterns may include stripes, spots, or solid colors, offering camouflage in their environment. Color can be black, white, gray (or blue), cream, red (or orange), or more rarely chocolate, lilac, cinnamon, or fawn.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Big Cat races (Tiger, Lion, Jaguar, Leopard)","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Antagonistic towards Fidoans, Rodent races (Mice, Rats, Squirrels, Beavers, Porcupines, Gophers)","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63 points","Titles: Beast, Catkin","Feature:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Cat] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a feline.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Double-jointed] (7) - Greater than average range of mobility in the joints. Does not allow 360 rotation. Dislocation/Injury can still occur.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Heightened Sense [Hearing, Smelling] E (14)","Acrobatics F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-felisian-catfolk-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-felisian-catfolk-2.webp"],"aliases":["Catkin","Felisian (Catfolk)"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-dragonborn","name":"Dragonborn","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Dragonborn resemble bipedal dragons without wings and may or may not have a tail. Originally hatched from dragon eggs, dragonborn are direct descendants of dragons. The draconian humans are a more diluted branch of their bloodline that is more human than dragon. Dragonborn scale colors can vary, with some having vibrant hues matching their dragon kin, while others have more uniform brass or bronze colors. Their scales, coloration, and other features reflect their dragon ancestors. Dragonborn are resistant to the same type of elemental damage as their breath weapon.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 6'2\" to 6'6\" (188–198 cm) Female: 5'8\" to 6'2\" (173–188 cm)","weight":"Male: 250–300 lbs (113–136 kg) Female: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg)","physique":"Dragonborn have a robust and muscular build, standing tall with a strong, upright posture. Their bodies are well-defined, reflecting their physical prowess. Dragonborn have elongated snouts, prominent jaws, and sharp teeth, resembling their dragon ancestors. They possess distinctive frills or ridges along their heads and necks. Females may develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young.","coloring":"They are covered in tough, scaly skin that varies in color depending on their draconic heritage (e.g., red, blue, green, black, white, gold, or silver). Black: Acid breath. Blue: Lightning breath. Green: Poison breath. Red: Fire breath. White: Cold breath. Brass: Fire breath. Bronze: Lightning breath. Copper: Acid breath. Gold: Fire breath. Silver: Cold breath.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect full-blooded Dragons","Friendly towards dragon races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77+ points","Titles: Beast, Dragonborn","Feature:","Medium size","[Scales] - Skin is totally covered in reptilian scales.","[Horns] - optional - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Tail] - optional - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Breath Weapon (Type)] - The ability to exhale or project an elementally charged breath or discharge from the mouth. Element must be selected upon acquisition.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Fighting Style [Natural Weapon] F (7)","Tech: Range F (Free)","Tech: Area F (7)","Resistance [Type] F (7)","1 Sense skill","Equipment: Natural Weapon F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77+ points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-dragonborn-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-dragonborn-2.webp"],"aliases":["Dragonborn"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-drider","name":"Drider","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Driders are a unique and cursed race, characterized by their drow upper body and spider lower body. Typically created as a punishment for failing to meet the expectations of the spider goddess Lolth, they embody both the grace of drow and the predatory nature of spiders. With abilities like climbing and web production, they are formidable foes and often serve as agents of chaos and darkness within their societies. The surface world doesn’t see many of them.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 6'5\" to 7'0\" (196–213 cm) Female: 6'0\" to 6'6\" (183–198 cm)","weight":"Male: 250–350 lbs (113–159 kg) Female: 200–300 lbs (91–136 kg)","physique":"Driders possess a unique and striking physique that combines the features of both drow (dark elves) and spiders. This combination creates a formidable and unsettling presence. Muscular yet agile, their upper bodies are strong and capable of wielding weapons, while their lower bodies provide superior mobility. The upper body resembles that of a drow, retaining the graceful and lithe build typical of elves. Sharp, angular faces with high cheekbones, pointed ears, and expressive features. The lower body transitions into that of a large spider. Eight long, powerful legs provide exceptional agility and speed, allowing them to climb walls and ceilings effortlessly. The legs and abdomen are covered in a tough, chitinous exoskeleton that offers protection and adds to their monstrous appearance. Driders move with a fluid grace, combining the elegance of their drow upper body with the swift, agile motions of a spider.","coloring":"Skin Tone of the upper half is often dark, ranging from deep browns to purples or blacks, similar to their drow heritage. Their eyes may reflect a range of colors, including red, purple, or silver. Long, flowing hair that can be white, silver, or other shades, often styled elaborately, reflecting their drow background.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Darkness, things of the dark","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 119 points","Titles: Beast, Drider","Feature:","Medium size","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Octoped] (21) - Has eight legs.","[Spinneret] (7) - Portion of the lower abdomen that is able to produce silk.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Special Movement F [Wall-crawling] (14) - Can cling to and traverse walls or ceilings as though they were on the ground.","Fighting Style [weapon type] F (7) or Magic F (7)","Resilient F [Poison] (7)","Language [Arachnid] (7 if not taken for free at creation)","Stealth F (7)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"119 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-drider-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-drider-2.webp"],"aliases":["Drider"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-elefante","name":"Elefante","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Elefantes are large, muscular humanoids with a blend of elephantine features, including trunks, tusks, and thick skin. Their impressive height and weight, coupled with their dexterity and grace, make them formidable beings in both combat and social interactions. Their physique reflects their roles as guardians, healers, and community leaders within their societies.","lifespan":"140 years","height":"Male: 7'0\" to 8'0\" (213–244 cm) Female: 6'0\" to 7'0\" (183–213 cm)","weight":"Male: 300–400 lbs (136–181 kg) Female: 250–350 lbs (113–159 kg)","physique":"Elefantes are robust and strong, with a solid, muscular build that allows them to perform heavy physical tasks and engage in combat effectively. Elefantes have prominent trunks, which they use for various tasks, and tusks that can vary in size. Their facial structure is reminiscent of elephants, giving them a distinctive appearance. They possess large, expressive ears that help with temperature regulation and enhance their sensory perception. Elefantes have a generally upright posture, which contributes to their imposing presence. An elefante’s movement is best described as “controlled power”. Despite their size, they can move with surprising grace, particularly in social settings or when performing delicate tasks. Their trunks provide them with a unique form of dexterity, allowing them to manipulate objects with precision and perform tasks that require fine motor skills.","coloring":"Their skin is thick, resembling that of an elephant, providing some natural armor against physical damage. Its color can range from grays to blues to earthen tones bordering on reds. Elefantes in colder climates often grow thick fur.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Compassion","Friendly with Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 91 points","Titles: Beast, Elefante","Feature:","Medium size","[Skin: (color(s))] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Elephant] - Bestial ears shaped like those of an elephant.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Trunk] (7) - The elongated, prehensile nose of an elephant.","[Tusks] - Elongated canines on the bottom jaw that may protrude through the lips.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Superstrength F (14)","Heightened Sense [Hearing, Smell] E (14)","Resistance [Bludgeoning] F (7)","Athletics F (7)","Equipment: Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"91 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-elefante-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-elefante-2.webp"],"aliases":["Elefante"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-gnoll","name":"Gnoll","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Gnolls are hyena-like humanoids, embodying a mix of ferocity and savagery. Their physical appearance includes canine features, such as elongated snouts, sharp teeth, and fur-covered bodies. Gnolls are tribal and nomadic, living in packs led by powerful chieftains or shamans. They are said to have originated from the corruption of humanoid tribes, often linked to the demon lord Yeenoghu, the Gnoll Lord. According to this myth, Yeenoghu transformed these tribes into gnolls to serve him, instilling in them a thirst for blood and chaos. Other accounts claim that gnolls are the result of a pact between humans and hyena spirits, where the spirits granted them strength and survival skills in exchange for servitude. Typically, gnolls roam the desert regions of the Ororoot Empire (West), but have been spotted as far east as Ryke.","lifespan":"40 years","height":"Male: 5'8\" to 6'6\" (173–198 cm) Female: 6'2\" to 7'0\" (188–213 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–250 lbs (68–113 kg) Female: 220–300 lbs (100–136 kg)","physique":"Gnolls are muscular and robust, with a powerful build that reflects their physical prowess. Gnolls have elongated, hyena-like heads with large, pointed ears. Their faces feature sharp, predatory features, including a pronounced snout and sharp teeth. Eyes are often bright and expressive, commonly seen in shades of yellow or red. Areas not covered by fur may show tough, leathery skin, especially around the joints. They have long, powerful limbs, with muscular arms suited for melee combat and agile legs for quick movement. Gnolls possess claw-like fingers and toes, enhancing their ability to grip and climb. Gnolls are known for their brute strength, capable of overpowering foes in combat. Despite their size, they are surprisingly agile, able to move quickly and effectively in various terrains.","coloring":"Gnolls are covered in coarse fur, typically in shades of brown, tan, or gray, often with darker spots or stripes.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile towards all trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77 points","Titles: Beast, Gnoll","Features:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Hyena] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a hyena.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Heightened Sense [Hearing, Smell] E (14)","Stealth F (7)","Survival F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-gnoll-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-gnoll-2.webp"],"aliases":["Gnoll"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-haregon","name":"Haregon","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"A small hare-like beastfolk with powerful legs and good hearing. Known to come from big families more often than not. The top haregons in each family often try to intermingle in the social and political scenes to make up for what they might lack in physical prowess.","lifespan":"75 years","height":"*Ear length excluded Male: 3'2\" to 4'0\" (97–122 cm)* Female: 3'0\" to 4'0\" (91–122 cm)*","weight":"Male: 40–60 lbs (18–27 kg) Female: 30–45 lbs (14–20 kg)","physique":"The harengon race combines the agility and characteristics of hares with a humanoid form, making them distinct and agile. They have a slender, athletic build, emphasizing agility and speed. Their limbs are proportionate, with longer hind legs designed for powerful movement. They stand upright on their hind feet, which are strong and well-developed, enabling quick bursts of speed and agile maneuvers. Their heads are slightly elongated with a rounded shape, maintaining some hare-like features. Large, expressive eyes are prominent, offering excellent peripheral vision and depth perception, typically in shades of brown, green, or hazel. Long, upright ears are sensitive and can swivel independently, enhancing their ability to detect sounds from various directions. Areas not covered by fur may exhibit smooth, slightly padded skin, particularly on the hands and feet. Their arms are slightly shorter than average for their height but are well-muscled, allowing for dexterity and strength in manipulation. The hind legs are powerful and muscular, designed for jumping and sprinting. The front limbs end in dexterous hands with long fingers, suitable for grasping and climbing.","coloring":"They have a soft, dense coat of fur that varies in color from light tan to dark brown, and gray, often with patterns that help them blend into their surroundings.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63(+7) points","Titles: Beast, Haregon, Small","Feature:","[Small] (+7)","Height: 2 to 4 feet tall/long","Weight: 8 to 60 pounds","Character's lift and carry/5 . Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","minus 1 strength action effectiveness","Mundane damage received is increased 1","plus 1 speed action effectiveness","attacks can have accurate F applied without changing cooldown or grade of attack","base movement cut in half","base throw distance cut in half","small , Light, unobtrusive - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudicating actions","plus 1 effectiveness to stealth actions","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Hare] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a hare.","[Legs: Hare] - Bestial legs with robust thighs and elongated tarsals for agile movement.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Skills:","Jumping F (7)","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell] (14)","Sixth Sense F [Danger] (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63(+7) points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-haregon-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-haregon-2.webp"],"aliases":["Haregon","Small"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-illithid","name":"Illithid","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Illithids are sexless entities with a humanoid body and an octopus-like head. They have four tentacles around a lamprey-like mouth. Primarily known for their intellectual skills and mind powers.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"5’ to 6’ (152–183 cm)","weight":"110–150 lbs (50–68 kg)","physique":"Illithids have a slender, elongated body that is somewhat frail in appearance. They are not heavily muscled but possess a certain grace and agility. They typically stand upright, though their movements can be fluid and almost serpentine. The head is bulbous and resembles that of an octopus, with a broad, flat top and a tentacled mouth. Their eyes are often deep-set and can vary in color, usually appearing dark or reddish. They have a penetrating gaze that can be unsettling. Surrounding their mouth are several long, flexible tentacles that they use for both feeding and grappling. They have two long, slender arms that end in three-fingered hands. The fingers are dexterous, allowing for fine manipulation. Their legs are also long and thin, with a slight bend at the knees. This structure allows for agile movement, though they are not particularly strong. Despite their seemingly frail build, illithids are surprisingly agile and can move quickly when necessary.","coloring":"Illithid skin is typically smooth and slightly slimy, with colors ranging from pale gray to bluish or greenish hues. The skin often has a faint sheen. The surface can appear somewhat rubbery, and the overall look contributes to their otherworldly presence.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70 points","Titles: Beast, Illithid","Feature:","Medium size","[Tendrils/Tentacles] - A slender, flexible limb or appendage.","[Skin: Purple/Blue/Green/Grey] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Hands: Three Fingers] - Hands have only three fingers.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Skills:","Telepathy F (21)","Sixth Sense F [Danger] (7)","Arcana (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"70 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-illithid-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-illithid-2.webp"],"aliases":["Illithid"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-kitsune","name":"Kitsune","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"A fae breed of fox that achieved a humanoid form, kitsune typically have a full fox-like appearance complete with fur but occasionally take on a human appearance accented by bestial traits (fox ears, eyes, snout, serrated teeth, claws, etc). Kitsune are separate from foxkin due to their penchant for mischief and their command of cloaking magics among other powers to facilitate their mischief. Mundane foxes occasionally evolve into kitsune.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 5’ to 6’ (152–183 cm) Female: 5’ to 6’ (152–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 120–180 lbs (54–82 kg) Female: 100–160 lbs (45–73 kg)","physique":"Kitsune are lean and agile, reflecting their fox heritage. They possess a balance of strength and grace, making them both nimble and capable in combat. The number of tails signifies their age and power, with one-tailed kitsune having a single, bushy tail that is a prominent feature. They usually have pointed fox-like ears that are expressive and sensitive to their surroundings. Kitsune have bright, intelligent eyes that can have a mystical quality, sometimes glowing or changing color based on their emotions. In their human guise, they may have hair colors that reflect their fox form or exhibit more human-like traits.","coloring":"In their fox form, they have soft, dense fur that can vary in color (often shades of red, orange, or white).","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Beast tree","Friendly with Prime tree, Fae tree","Neutral to Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63/70 points","Titles: Beast, Kitsune","Feature:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Fox] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a fox.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Tails: Multiple] (7 points per 2 tails) - Feature Skill - Creature gains additional tails whenever their character grade goes up.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Heightened Sense [Smell, Hearing] E (14)","Magic F (7)","Undetected [sense] F (14)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63/70 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-kitsune-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-kitsune-2.webp"],"aliases":["Kitsune"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-mermaid","name":"Mermaid","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"A sentient creature that lives exclusively in the sea, merfolk are one of the few denizens of the ocean. They are known to be more useful with utility magics, rarely obtaining offensive spells. As such it's more common to see merfolk with spears or martial weaponry suited to underwater combat. Though they can learn martial techniques, mermaids are generally good-spirited entities that mean no one harm.","lifespan":"125 years","height":"Male: 6’ to 7’11” (183–241 cm) Females: 5’ to 7’ (152–213 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Typically human-like, often depicted with a slender, athletic build. May have defined muscles, reflecting strength and grace, especially in the arms and shoulders. Females develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young. The tail is often long, powerful, and sleek, resembling that of a fish or dolphin. The tail extends significantly beyond the torso, contributing to the overall length of the mermaid. Often depicted with an hourglass figure for female mermaids, while male mermaids may have broader shoulders and a more muscular build. Skin is smooth and manifests in various shades, sometimes reflecting the colors of the sea (e.g., blues, greens). Hair is long and flowing, often depicted in vibrant colors or with aquatic features like seaweed or shells woven in.","coloring":"The tail is usually covered in scales, which can vary in color and pattern, providing both beauty and camouflage in water.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect the “Old Sea”, Fae tree","Friendly to Beast tree, Prime tree","Neutral to Construct tree, Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 133 points","Titles: Beast, Mermaid","Features:","Medium size","[Gills] (7) - Slits typically in the throat region that allow for breathing underwater.","[Mermaid Tail] - Instead of legs, there is only the tail end of a fish.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Direction Sense] (7) - ability to intuitively know cardinal directions regardless of indicators, allowing proper orientation in strange environments which may grant bonuses to navigational efforts","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - C (21)","Skills:","Swim Speed - D (14)","Resilient E (Water Pressure; Cold) (14)","Heightened Sense F (Hearing, Smell) (7)","Supersense F [Hydrodynamics] (7)","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Telepathy F (21)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"133 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-mermaid-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-mermaid-2.webp"],"aliases":["Mermaid"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-naga","name":"Naga","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Nagas are half human, half snake creatures that have an inborn desire to guard and protect. While young (Mundane tier), they often find employment as bodyguards and even assassins. They are exceedingly loyal once they align themselves to another in this way. Forced enslavement doesn’t always instill this same loyalty. Nagas are long-lived compared to other races in the Beast tree, so it’s no wonder they are occasionally found guarding the tombs of their former masters.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 7’ to 10’ (2.1–3.0 m) Female: 6’ to 9’ (1.8–2.7 m)","weight":"Male: 200–400 lbs (90–180 kg) Female: 150–300 lbs (68–136 kg)","physique":"Naga have a humanoid upper body, including arms, a torso, and a head. They may possess a muscular build, reflecting strength and vitality. Facial features are striking, perhaps even regal, and may include elongated ears, sharp eyes, fangs, and a forked tongue. The lower body appears as that of a serpent or snake, which can be long and flexible. This tail can vary in length, often being several times the length of the upper body. Naga are tall, with males generally larger than females. Naga often possess well-defined muscles, particularly in the arms and torso, symbolizing their strength and prowess.","coloring":"The skin of a Naga may have scales, which can be vibrant in color, reflecting their supernatural nature.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Water-themed divinity","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77 points","Titles: Beast, Naga","Feature:","Medium size","[Snake Tail] - Instead of legs, there is only the tail end of a snake.","[Fangs] - Elongated canines in the top row of teeth used to puncture flesh.","[Forked Tongue] - A tongue split into two distinct tines at the tip; this is a feature common to many species of reptiles, which smell using the tip of their tongue, and a forked tongue allows them to sense from which direction a smell is coming.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Swim Speed F (7)","Special Movement [Slithering] (Free with Snake Tail feature)","Heightened Sense [Smell] F (7)","Supersense F [Hydrodynamics] (7)","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Supersense [Thermoreception] F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapon [Snake Lower Body] F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-naga-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-naga-2.webp"],"aliases":["Naga"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-neko","name":"Neko","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"A bloodline specifically bred in the Eastern Empire by humans with an unwholesome interest in the catkin. The result was a mostly human creature with distinct feline ears, eyes and tail, variable bestial shaping to the mouth and nose, and tendency to grow longer, sturdier nails. Though the feline features are present, they may or may not be functional, as is common with the diluted bestial bloodlines.","lifespan":"105 years","height":"Male: 5'0\" to 5'7\" (152–170 cm) Female: 4'5\" to 5'2\" (135–157 cm)","weight":"Male: 140–180 lbs (64–82 kg) Female: 90–130 lbs (41–59 kg)","physique":"Neko lack the flexible spine of the Felisian, so their movements have as much grace and fluidity as a normal human body can afford. They are particularly lean when compared to either humans or felisians, having noticeably less muscle mass. The neko’s agility remains, however, allowing them to run at speed and jump. Their potential in these areas only just surpasses normal human ability. A neko’s claws are not retractable and their palms are missing typical pads, appearing human. Nekos still possess feline ears and a tail, which are their only features covered in fur. Fine motor control of these features may be greatly diminished. The form and function of the eyes remains feline.","coloring":"Something about the breeding done to create nekos appears to have allowed the eyes as well as body hair to develop nonstandard colors, such as blue or pink.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Fae tree","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42+ points","Titles: Beast, Neko","Feature:","[Ears: Cat] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a feline.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills: Heightened Sense [Hearing] F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42+ points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-neko-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-neko-2.webp"],"aliases":["Neko"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-owlbear-juvenile","name":"Owlbear (Juvenile)","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"An odd but effective union of owl and bear. Mannerisms and behavior largely resemble that of a bear: grounded, walking on all fours (can stand on hind legs), omnivorous, fast runner. Some traits are inherited from the owl half also: devouring prey whole, the ability to rotate the neck 270 degrees, and the avian style talons on the front feet. Overall size is upper range of medium but not large.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 5’ to 7’ (1.5–2.1 m) Female: 4’ to 6 ‘ (1.2–1.8 m)","weight":"Male: 300–500 lbs (136–227 kg) Female: 200–400 lbs (91–181 kg)","physique":"Adolescent owlbears have a robust and muscular build, reflecting their growth and developing strength. They are stocky, with a broad chest and strong limbs. They typically move on all fours but can stand on their hind legs, showcasing their bear-like structure. The head resembles that of an owl, featuring a round face with large, expressive eyes, a hooked beak, and prominent tufts of feathers. The head is proportionally larger compared to their body, typical of owls, giving them a distinctive appearance. Their bodies are covered in a mix of coarse fur and feathers, which provide insulation and camouflage in their natural habitat. The fur is often thicker and fluffier in colder environments. The front limbs are strong and bear-like, equipped with sharp claws for hunting and climbing. The hind limbs are muscular, allowing for powerful movement and agility when sprinting or jumping.","coloring":"The coloration can vary, typically featuring earthy tones like browns and tans, with lighter feather patterns that resemble an owl's plumage.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 91 points","Titles: Beast, Owlbear","Feature:","[Feathers and Fur] - Feathers from the head to shoulders and front arms, bear fur everywhere else.","[Eyes: Avian] - A bird's eyes are flat and fixed, fitting tightly into its skull, so a bird is unable to roll its eyes. To look around, it has to move its head.","[Telescopic Vision] (7) - The eyes of an owl are not true “eyeballs.” Their tube-shaped eyes are completely immobile, providing binocular vision which fully focuses on their prey and boosts depth perception.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Beak] - Bony projecting jaw found primarily in birds but also various reptiles and other creatures.","[Neck Mobility: 270°] (7) - Owls can rotate their necks 270 degrees.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Jump F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Resistance [Bludgeoning] (7)","Climbing F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"91 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-owlbear-juvenile-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-owlbear-juvenile-2.webp"],"aliases":["Owlbear","Owlbear (Juvenile)"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-satyr","name":"Satyr","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Satyrs are one of many creatures that appear to blend the Prime and Beast trees. Interestingly enough, this is an all male race. Some believe those who defected from the war of the races over 50 years ago became satyrs, who prefer celebration and revelry. Presently, the satyrs commonly live in forests near settlements and come out during harvest time and other occasions for making merry.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 5'0\" to 6'0\" (152–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–250 lbs (68–113 kg)","physique":"Satyrs often have a strong, muscular build, reflecting their physicality and vitality. They are typically more robust than average humans. Satyrs have the lower body of a goat, including hooves and legs covered in fur, which contributes to their animalistic appearance. The upper body is generally human-like, often muscular and athletic, with a strong chest and arms. Satyrs usually have pointed ears, prominent horns on their heads, and sometimes a beard or facial hair. Their facial expressions often convey mischief or joy. Their legs are typically covered in fur, and their skin may have a sun-kissed or rugged appearance, reflecting their connection to nature. Despite their robust build, satyrs are known for their agility and grace, allowing them to dance and move fluidly.","coloring":"Many satyrs have fur in shades of brown, ranging from light tan to deep chocolate, often with greenish hues that mimic forest foliage. Some satyrs may have patterns, such as stripes or spots, resembling those found in animals like deer or goats, adding to their wild appearance. Variants might include gray or black fur, providing a more rugged and mysterious look, especially in shadowy forest environments. Some satyrs may have lighter fur, like white or cream, which could symbolize purity or a connection to moonlight and magic. Rarely, satyrs could have vibrant or iridescent fur, incorporating colors like deep blues, purples, or even metallic shades, reflecting their magical nature.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect forest guardians","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree","Neutral to Construct Tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84 points","Titles: Beast, Satyr","Features:","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Lower Body: Goat] - The waist down is covered in fur. A stubby goat tail protrudes from the tailbone. The joints are exaggerated and the feet are replaced by hooves.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed E - (7)","Skills:","Jumping F (7)","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell] (14)","Acrobatics F (7)","Performance F [Instrument] (7)","Persuasion F (7)","Survival F (7)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-satyr-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-satyr-2.webp"],"aliases":["Satyr"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-saurian","name":"Saurian","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"An ancient race of scalekin descending from dinosaur-like creatures. They were fairly recently discovered on an island off the coast of the Second Continent. Much of the nations have yet to see a beastkin like this up close.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 6' to 7' (1.8--2.1 m) Female: 5’ 6” to 6’ 6” (1.7--2.0 m)","weight":"Male: 200--300 lbs (90--136 kg) Female: 150--250 lbs (68--113 kg)","physique":"Saurians have a strong, muscular physique, reflecting their reptilian heritage and predatory nature. They are robust and powerful. Their bodies may resemble those of large reptiles, with prominent muscles and a streamlined shape for agility and speed. Saurians usually have strong, well-defined limbs with clawed hands and feet, aiding in climbing, running, and combat. Some may exhibit a digitigrade stance, walking on their toes, which enhances agility and speed. Many saurians have elongated snouts with sharp teeth, suitable for a carnivorous diet. Males often showcase larger crests or frills, which can be used for display or intimidation. Saurians often possess long, muscular tails, which can be used for balance, communication, or even as a weapon in combat. Females may develop breasts, but they do not produce milk nor nurse their young.","coloring":"Their skin is usually covered in scales, which can vary in color and texture depending on their subspecies and environment. This provides protection and may aid in camouflage. Common colors might include greens, browns, and grays, with patterns that help them blend into their surroundings.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Larger or Stronger races, certain Avian races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 91 points","Titles: Beast, Saurial","Features:","Medium size","[Scales] - Skin is totally covered in reptilian scales.","[Ears: Reptilian] - A thin membrane located at the rear of the head.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Heightened Sense E [Sight, Smell] (14)","Climbing F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Survival F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F or Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"91 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-saurian-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-saurian-2.webp"],"aliases":["Saurial","Saurian"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-tanuki","name":"Tanuki","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"Humanoid beastkin originating from the Republic of Kuridan, who have established clans. Some Tanuki possess more animalistic features while others possess less. Thanks to their claws and enhanced senses, Tanuki beastkin excel at surviving during all hours of the night and day. They seldom reach taller than 5'8” in height.","lifespan":"72 years","height":"Male: 5'4\" to 5'8\" (162–173 cm) Female: 5'0\" to 5'6\" (152–168 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Tanuki have a strong, muscular physique. They are stocky but agile, combining strength with stealth. Their limbs are well-proportioned, allowing for a balance of power and dexterity, suitable for both climbing and running. They have a broad face with a flat nose and rounded ears, reminiscent of raccoons. This gives them an expressive appearance. Large, expressive eyes that convey curiosity and intelligence, often with a bright coloration. The fur provides warmth and protection. A long, bushy tail that aids in balance and communication. The tail may be expressive, used for signaling emotions or intentions. This race is known for its agility, capable of quick movements. They may exhibit both bipedal and quadrupedal locomotion, allowing for versatility in movement.","coloring":"Soft, dense fur that varies in color—typically shades of brown, gray, or tan, often with distinctive markings. Unique patterns or markings may be present, serving as a form of identification or cultural significance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Canine races","Friendly towards Prime tree, Beast tree, Fae tree","Neutral towards cat races, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70 points","Titles: Beast, Tanuki","Feature:","[Fur] (optional) - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Tanuki] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a raccoon dog.","[Bestial Eyes] (optional) - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Muzzle] (optional) - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] (optional) - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Special Movement F [Wall-Bouncing] (7)","Heightened Sense [Smell or Hearing] F (7)","Climbing F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Items: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"70 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-tanuki-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-tanuki-2.webp"],"aliases":["Tanuki"]},{"id":"beast-mundane-wolven","name":"Wolven","tree":"Beast","stage":"Mundane","description":"A species of humanoid canines that emerged from the east, wolven were bred to protect their human masters and help them hunt. Their instinct made hunting come naturally, and their fur made them ideal travel companions in the colder climates to the north. Unlike the fidoans, however, wolvens are far more difficult to keep on a leash. After many years under human enslavement, a seemingly instinctual pride arose in the members of the wolven race, causing them to denounce human rule. In the resulting civil war, wolven were eventually liberated and migrated to the Republic where they took leadership positions among other alphas in the Beast tree.","lifespan":"80 years","height":"Male: 6'4\" to 7'2\" (193–218 cm) Female: 5'8\" to 6'8\" (173–203 cm)","weight":"Male: 180–250 lbs (82–113 kg) Female: 120–180 lbs (54–82 kg)","physique":"A robust and athletic physique, with well-defined muscles reflecting their strength and agility. They are built for power and endurance. Their arms and legs are long and strong, allowing for both bipedal movement and agility in dynamic environments. A broad, slightly elongated head with a strong jawline, resembling that of a wolf. The muzzle is pronounced but more human-like in proportion. Large, expressive eyes that can vary in color, providing keen vision and conveying a range of emotions. They may have a reflective quality, enhancing night vision. Large, upright ears that are sensitive to sound, able to swivel to detect noises from different directions. A prominent tail that aids in balance and expression, often used for communication and signaling emotions. Despite their size, they are capable of swift, graceful movements, combining strength with agility. They may exhibit a unique gait that reflects their wolf heritage. Strong hands with dexterous fingers, allowing for tool use and manipulation. Claws may be retractable. Feet that are adapted for both running and standing, providing stability and traction.","coloring":"Thick, dense fur covering their bodies, with patterns that may vary from individual to individual. Fur colors range from grays and browns to whites and blacks.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect Alphas of the Beast tree","Friendly towards wolfkin, Canine races","Neutral towards Prime tree, Fae tree, Construct tree","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 133 points","Titles: Beast, Wolven","Feature:","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: Wolf] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a canine.","Directional Hearing (7) - Capability to precisely locate the source of sounds, which is useful for hunting and communication.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Jumping F (7)","Heightened Sense E [Hearing/Smell] (14)","Sixth Sense F [Danger] (7)","Acrobatics F (7)","Climbing F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Survival F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Conscious Expansion - may expend a 4th action in a post exclusively on a sense ability (not an attack, defense, movement action)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"133 points","images":["assets/races/beast-mundane-wolven-1.webp","assets/races/beast-mundane-wolven-2.webp"],"aliases":["Wolven"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-feles-sidh","name":"Feles-Sidh","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Feles-Sidh are an anomaly among the big cat races (cougarkin, leopardkin, tigerkin, lionkin, jaguarkin, cheetahkin, snow-leopardkin). Occasionally, when these races reproduce, the offspring is a full-blooded fae regardless of the other parent's lineage. Despite being fae, they may still take physical traits of their parents, but could also appear more human. Such offspring always have magical aptitude and, in many cases, possess supernatural senses beyond the physical. Unfortunately, it's likely their natural senses are diminished to more human levels in such cases.","lifespan":"115.5 years","height":"Refer to Lionkin, big cat races","weight":"Refer to Lionkin, big cat races","physique":"Shares cosmetic features with big cat races. Torso and face may appear more human.","coloring":"Refer to Lionkin, big cat races","historicalFigures":["Prince Orion (Ryke)"],"relations":["May learn prejudices of parent trees/races","Other beastkin likely to react \"friendly\" even if normally antagonistic/hostile"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63 points","Titles: Beast, Feles-Sidh","Feature:","Medium size","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Ears: [Big Cat]] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a [big cat].","[Eyes: Bestial] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Sixth Sense [type] F (7)","Focus F (21)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-feles-sidh-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-feles-sidh-2.webp"],"aliases":["Feles-Sidh"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-gnome","name":"Gnome","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Gnomes are among the smallest civilized races. Highly adept in their applications of magic, gnomes boast a natural resistance to charm and perception-altering effects. Their true love, however, is tinkering and inventing tediously designed mechanisms and contraptions. This love even drives some gnomes to adventure in order to observe machines and devices of ancient or foreign origins. A large demographic of gnomes can be found in Widersia.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male/Female: 3' to 4' (91.44--121.92 cm)","weight":"Male/Female: 30 to 46 lbs (13.61--20.87 kg)","physique":"Gnomes often have a sturdy, compact build that gives them a sense of solidity. They are generally not overly muscular but have a robust frame. Gnomes often have round faces with prominent cheekbones and expressive features. They may have a variety of hairstyles, often adorned with bright colors or whimsical styles. Male gnomes may have beards that are long and well-groomed.","coloring":"Skin tones can range widely, similar to humans, but often in shades that reflect their connection to nature, such as earthy tones.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct Trees, especially fellow tinkerers","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42+ points","Titles: Fae, Gnome","Feature:","Small size (+7)","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Mindshield F (7)","1 Secondary skill","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42+ points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-gnome-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-gnome-2.webp"],"aliases":["Gnome"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-halfling-hobbit","name":"Halfling/Hobbit","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Halflings are small fae preoccupied with peace, quiet, and living life to its fullest in their own simple manners. Many moved to Ryke after the war 50 years ago, finding life more leisurely and enjoying the increasingly more diverse company there. That said, halflings can be found in most any stretch of quiet land on the Second Continent.","lifespan":"180 years","height":"Male/Female: 3' to 4' (91.44--121.92 cm)","weight":"Male/Female: 30 to 46 lbs (13.61--20.87 kg)","physique":"Halflings often have a sturdy and well-proportioned build, with a slightly rounded appearance. They tend to be more robust than they look. Halflings usually have round faces with soft features and cheerful expressions. They may have curly or wavy hair, often worn long, with some male halflings sporting facial hair.","coloring":"Their skin tones can range widely, similar to humans, often with a healthy, sun-kissed appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct Trees, especially small races","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49 points","Evolves into: Lightfoot Halfling","Titles: Fae, Halfling/Hobbit","Feature:","Small Size (+7)","Stat:","Speed E (7)","28 more points in Stats","Skill:","Resilient [Fear] F (7)","Energized F (7)"],"evolvesInto":"Lightfoot Halfling","totalCost":"49 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-halfling-hobbit-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-halfling-hobbit-2.webp"],"aliases":["Halfling","Halfling/Hobbit","Hobbit"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-firbolg","name":"Firbolg","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Firbolgs are the largest demographic of fae. They tower over most humans, and their strength and keen senses make them a match for the few beastkin that can look them in the eye. Despite their intimidating presence, however, firbolg are generally calm and amicable--assuming you aren't destroying the forests they call home, that is. They are deeply in-tune with the natural world and can sense the emotions of plants and animals alike. For this reason, they tend to be suspicious of urbanized races, like humans and dwarves, when they wander into their territory.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 7' to 8' (2.13--2.44 m) Female: 6.5' to 7.5' (1.98--2.29 m)","weight":"Male: 250 to 300 lbs. (113--136 kg) Female: 180 to 240 lbs. (82--109 kg)","physique":"They possess a strong and muscular physique, reflecting their strength and physical capabilities. Their faces often have soft, gentle features, with large, expressive eyes that reflect their calm demeanor. Firbolgs may have slightly elongated ears and more pronounced noses, enhancing their connection to nature.","coloring":"Firbolgs often have earthy skin tones, such as shades of brown or green, and may have hair that resembles natural elements, like moss or leaves.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct Trees, especially nature-minded races","Neutral to Human, Dwarf, and similarly urbanized/city-dwelling races","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49 points","Titles: Fae, Firbolg","Feature:","Medium size","[Skin: Blue] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stat:","Strength E (7)","Intelligence E (7)","Vitality E (7)","Skill:","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense [Hearing] OR Heightened Sense [Smell] (7)","Nature F (7)","Empathy F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"49 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-firbolg-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-firbolg-2.webp"],"aliases":["Firbolg"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-dwarf","name":"Dwarf","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Dwarves are on the lower end of medium size. Commonly fixated on earthen bounties, dwarves are commonly owners of, or workers in, mines. When they aren't extracting precious materials from the earth, they might be adventuring for treasure, helping construct elaborate stone structures, or serving in temples of their deities, which also prize and house various riches. The only feeling that rivals a dwarf’s love of mineral wealth is their hatred for goblins and orcs.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 4'5\" to 5'0\" (135–152 cm) Female: 4'0\" to 4'8\" (122–142 cm)","weight":"Male: 180–250 lbs (82–113 kg) Female: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg)","physique":"Dwarves are short and robust, with a wide, muscular frame that emphasizes strength and durability. They have broad shoulders that contribute to their imposing presence. Dwarves often have a prominent jawline and broad forehead, giving them a rugged, sturdy appearance. Many male dwarves are known for their thick beards, which can vary in length and style, often seen as a symbol of pride and strength. Muscular arms and legs, designed for physical labor and combat, often with well-defined muscles. Their limbs are shorter in proportion to their bodies, contributing to their stocky appearance. Dwarves have large, powerful hands with thick fingers, suited for wielding tools and weapons. Their feet are broad and strong, providing stability, especially when navigating uneven terrain. Dwarves tend to have a strong, upright posture, reflecting their confidence and readiness for action. Their movements are often deliberate and powerful, emphasizing their strength rather than speed.","coloring":"The skin is typically weathered and tough, often showing signs of labor in mines or forging. Hair can vary widely, including shades of brown, black, red, and blonde, with many dwarves having thick hair and facial hair.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae, (friendly) Dragons","Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct Trees","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 21 points","Titles: Fae, Dwarf","Features: Medium size","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Artisan [Type] F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"21 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-dwarf-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-dwarf-2.webp"],"aliases":["Dwarf"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-elf","name":"Elf","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Elves come in a handful of types, but their largest demographic is the stereotypical woodland ranger sort: the common elf. If you encounter an elf, especially outside of the Fae See, it is likely one of this type. They are tall, graceful beings with pointed ears and long lifespans. Elves are deeply connected to nature, art, and magic, often embodying wisdom and a serene disposition, though they may appear aloof to other races.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5'8\" to 6'2\" (173–188 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 5'8\" (157–173 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Elves are typically characterized by a lean and graceful physique, emphasizing elegance and agility. Elves have longer limbs in proportion to their bodies, contributing to their agility and graceful movements. Their hands and feet are often slender and dexterous, well-suited for delicate tasks like crafting and archery. Elves have sharp, angular facial features, including high cheekbones and a defined jawline. A distinctive trait, their pointed ears enhance their ethereal appearance. Elven skin is typically smooth and may have a slight luminescence, reflecting their connection to nature. Elves maintain an upright and poised posture, exuding confidence and elegance. Their movements are often described as fluid and graceful, whether walking, running, or dancing.","coloring":"Hair can range from traditional colors (blonde, brown, black) to more vibrant shades (silver, green) that reflect their magical nature.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), other Elves, Gnomes","Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae","Neutral to Construct Tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 56 points","Titles: Fae, Elf","Feature:","Medium size","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Precision F - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Acrobatics F (7)","Nature F or Animal Handling F (7)","Survival F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"56 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-elf-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-elf-2.webp"],"aliases":["Elf"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-elf-lune","name":"Elf (Lune)","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Lune elves are blessed with special night vision from the moon, and as such are largely (but not exclusively) nocturnal. Their pale, at times silvery, skin easily sets them apart from other elves and the larger fae community. Lune elves stick to the shaded glades of the Fae See, but they do have a somewhat dense presence around the southern tip of Ryke. Martial and magical training are common, making hybrid weapon-catalysts typical among their equipment. The moon plays a significant role in their culture and religion.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5'8\" to 6'2\" (173–188 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 5'8\" (157–173 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Moon elves typically have a lean and graceful physique, emphasizing agility and elegance. Their limbs are typically long and slender, contributing to their agility and swift movements. Moon elves have finely shaped hands and feet, well-suited for both dexterous tasks and stealthy movements. They often possess sharp, angular facial features, with high cheekbones and a defined jawline. A distinctive trait, their pointed ears enhance their otherworldly appearance. Moon elves maintain an upright and poised posture, exuding confidence and elegance. Their movements are often graceful and fluid, reflecting their agility and connection to nature.","coloring":"Moon elves usually have very fair or luminescent skin, which may seem to glow softly in moonlight. Their hair is commonly silver, white, or light shades, often flowing and silky in texture.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Moon-related races","Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae","Neutral to Construct Tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63 points","Titles: Fae, Lune Elf","Feature:","Medium size","[Skin: Pale] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Moonvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Moonlight allows you to see in night as though it were day.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Undetected F [Sound] (14)","Acrobatics F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-elf-lune-1.webp"],"aliases":["Elf (Lune)","Lune Elf","Moon Elf"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-elf-surya","name":"Elf (Surya)","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Contrary to their lithe kin, the Surya elf is a strong specimen of tanned elf. As worshippers of the sun, it’s only fitting that they appear to be kissed by their celestial deity. They believe the sun to be an ancestral spirit, and their proof of this connection is found in their eyes. Every Suryan has between two and five pupils that can at times give their eyes a star-like appearance. This peculiar trait aids them by making them virtually immune to being blinded. Culturally, the Surya elves are divided in their weapon of choice. The magic purists refuse to use martial weaponry, while the martially inclined use what suits them.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5'10\" to 6'4\" (178–193 cm) Female: 5'4\" to 6'0\" (163–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 160–220 lbs (73–100 kg) Female: 110–170 lbs (50–77 kg)","physique":"Surya elves typically have a lean yet muscular build, emphasizing agility and strength. They are athletic and capable of quick movements. They usually have a lower body fat percentage, contributing to their toned appearance. Their muscles are well-defined, particularly in the arms and legs, reflecting their active lifestyle. Their tall stature (especially among elves) contributes to a commanding presence. They often have long limbs and fingers, which aid in dexterity and gracefulness. Surya elves typically maintain an upright and confident posture, reflecting their noble heritage. Their movements are often described as fluid and graceful, allowing them to navigate their environments with ease. They usually have sharp, angular facial features, with high cheekbones and expressive eyes that can be captivating.","coloring":"Their skin has a warm, sun-kissed glow, contributing to their overall radiant appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Sun-related races","Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae","Neutral to Construct Tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 56 points","Titles: Fae, Surya Elf","Feature:","Medium size","[Skin: Tanned] - Various shades of dark skin from constant exposure to the sun.","[Stellate Pupils] - Eyes have multiple pupillary formations resulting in a star-like shape.","[Ears: Pointy] - Short, fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [Radiant or Fire] (7)","Heightened Senses [Sight] F (7)","Resilient F [Blindness] (7)","Athletics F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"56 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-elf-surya-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-elf-surya-2.webp"],"aliases":["Elf (Surya)","Surya Elf"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-fairy","name":"Fairy","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Fairies are tiny humanoid fae that are responsible for much of the ethereal glow found in the Fae See. They hide away in groves woven together and hidden by their nature affinity and cloaking magics. Unfortunately, the insectoid wings and their enticing glow make fairies the occasional prey of insectoid beastkin and sometimes larger, malicious fae. Pixies are regarded as infantile fairies in the world of IH.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"5\" to 1' (15–30 cm)","weight":"1–5 lbs (0.5–2.3 kg)","physique":"Fairies are typically very small, often ranging from about 5 inches to 1 foot (15 to 30 cm) in height. Their petite size contributes to their delicate and whimsical appearance. Fairies generally have slender, graceful bodies that reflect their agility and lightness. They often appear fragile yet agile. Many fairies possess wings that can resemble those of butterflies, dragonflies, or other insects. These wings are often iridescent and may vary greatly in size and shape, contributing to their magical appearance. Fairies typically have enchanting, youthful faces with large, expressive eyes. Their features are often characterized by sharp cheekbones and delicate, pointed ears. Fairies are known for their graceful movements and agility, often depicted as flitting through the air or dancing lightly on the ground.","coloring":"Their skin may have a luminescent quality, often depicted in various shades, sometimes reflecting their connection to nature. Fairies have colorful hair, typically adorned with flowers and natural elements, enhancing their connection to the environment.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Nature-related races","Friendly to Fae tree, Beast tree","Neutral to Prime tree, Construct Tree, Insectoid races","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77 points","Titles: Fae, Fairy","Feature:","Tiny size (+14)","[Ears: Pointy] - Short, fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Wings] - Paired appendages capable of flight.","[Iridescent] - The above feature shows luminous colors that seem to change when seen from different angles.","Stats:","Precision - C (21)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Flight F (21)","Magic F (7)","Undetected F [Sight] (14)","1 Secondary skill","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-fairy-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-fairy-2.webp"],"aliases":["Fairy"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-faun","name":"Faun","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Fauns resemble satyrs in everything but their disposition. When war came to the Second Continent, the fauns were left to tend to the forests that survived. They are primarily healers, gentle and nurturing. While largely noncombatants, they have been known to fend off lesser monsters when they encroach or otherwise threaten the lands the faun oversees. Of the fae, fauns are the first to offer aid and direction to lost travelers regardless of race.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5'0\" to 6'0\" (152–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 120–220 lbs (54–100 kg)","physique":"Fauns generally have a more slender and graceful physique than satyrs, emphasizing agility and finesse over brute strength. They possess the lower body of a goat, including hooves and legs covered in fur, which enhances their connection to nature. The upper body is typically human-like, often with a more delicate and less muscular appearance than satyrs, reflecting their gentler nature. Fauns have pointed ears and may have small, decorative horns on their heads, along with a youthful, serene expression. Fauns are known for their agility and grace, allowing them to navigate through forests and meadows effortlessly.","coloring":"Their skin may have a natural, earthy tone, while their fur can range in color from light tan to darker browns, often blending with their surroundings.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), forest guardians","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84 points","Titles: Fae, Faun","Features:","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Goat Lower Body] - The waist down is covered in fur. A stubby goat tail protrudes from the tailbone. The joints are exaggerated and the feet are replaced by hooves.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Telepathy F (21)","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Healing F or Animal Handling F (7)","Nature F (7)","Medicine F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-faun-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-faun-2.webp"],"aliases":["Faun"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-air","name":"Air","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5'6\" to 6'0\" (168–183 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 5'8\" (157–173 cm)","weight":"Male: 130–180 lbs (59–82 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Air genasi have a more slender and graceful stature. They generally have a lean, athletic build, emphasizing agility and speed over brute strength. Their physique allows for quick, fluid movements. They may have features that reflect their elemental nature, such as slightly pointed ears or luminous eyes, giving them an ethereal appearance. Air genasi are known for their graceful movements, often appearing to float or glide rather than walk, reflecting their connection to the element of air.","coloring":"Air genasi often exhibit unique skin tones, such as pale blue, silver, or even white, reminiscent of the sky. Their hair may be wispy, flowing, or even ethereal, often in shades of light blue, white, or gray.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Sky","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84 points","Titles: Fae, Air Genasi","Feature:","[Hair: (color)] - Hair comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Air Hair] - Hair is made of visible air.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Whispersense] F (7) - Heightened Sense [Hearing] - Character can hear quiet conversations and distant sounds. Airtight seals and either character or source being submerged in liquid prevent this feature.","Stats:","Precision - C (21)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Flight F (21)","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [Air] (7)","Resilient [Suffocation] F (7)","Controlled Breathing F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-air-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-air-2.webp"],"aliases":["Air","Air Genasi"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-earth","name":"Earth","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5'8\" to 6'2\" (173–188 cm) Female: 5'4\" to 6'0\" (163–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 180–250 lbs (82–113 kg) Female: 140–220 lbs (64–100 kg)","physique":"Earth genasi generally have a sturdy, muscular build, emphasizing strength and resilience. Their physique reflects the durability associated with the earth element. Their facial features may include stone-like characteristics, such as angular jawlines or rugged appearances, reflecting their connection to earth. Earth genasi typically have a grounded way of moving, emphasizing stability and strength rather than agility, which aligns with their elemental nature.","coloring":"Earth genasi often exhibit earthy tones, such as browns, tans, or greens, with their skin resembling stone or soil. Hair may have colors like brown, gray, or even earthy shades, sometimes appearing textured like rock or moss.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Mountain","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 49 points","Titles: Fae, Earth Genasi","Features:","[Earth Hair] - Hair is made of earthy materials, like stone or moss.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Tremorsense] F (7) - Supersense - Character can sense vibration when physically touching a surface. Able to sense movement. Does not require line of sight in order to detect (narrator discretion).","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Tunneling F (7)","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [Earth] (7)","Resistance [Bludgeoning] (7)","Architecture F (7)","Climbing F (7)","Equipment: Natural Armor F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"49 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-earth-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-earth-2.webp"],"aliases":["Earth","Earth Genasi"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-fire","name":"Fire","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5'6\" to 6'1\" (168–185 cm) Female: 5'4\" to 5'9\" (163–175 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–220 lbs (68–100 kg) Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Fire genasi generally have an athletic build, emphasizing strength and agility, which is reflective of their passionate and energetic nature. They may have sharp features that convey intensity, with glowing eyes or other fiery characteristics that emphasize their elemental affiliation. Fire genasi are known for their quick and lively movements, reflecting their passionate and sometimes impulsive nature.","coloring":"Fire genasi often have skin tones that can range from deep red to orange or bronze, sometimes with a faint glow. Their hair may resemble flames, appearing in shades of red, orange, or yellow, and may even have a flickering or glowing quality.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Sun","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84 points","Titles: Fae, Fire Genasi","Feature:","[Fire Hair] - Hair resembles flames in color and ember-like glow. Not actual fire.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Thermal Vision] F (7) - Supersense - Character can see heat sources. Cool environments provide more contrast, while hot environments greatly diminish the ability to pinpoint heat sources. Cannot see heat sources through solid objects.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [Fire] (7)","Control Environment F (7)","Resistance [Fire] F (7)","Resilient F [Volcano] (7)","Energized F (7)","Acrobatic F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-fire-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-fire-2.webp"],"aliases":["Fire","Fire Genasi"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-water","name":"Water","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Male: 5'5\" to 6'0\" (165–183 cm) Female: 5'3\" to 5'8\" (160–173 cm)","weight":"Male: 140–200 lbs (64–91 kg) Female: 110–170 lbs (50–77 kg)","physique":"Water genasi generally have a lean and agile build, emphasizing fluid movements that mimic the flow of water. They may have features that evoke their aquatic nature, such as smooth skin, slightly webbed fingers, or subtle scales, enhancing their ethereal appearance. Water genasi are known for their graceful movements, often appearing to glide rather than walk, reflecting their connection to water and fluidity.","coloring":"Water genasi often possess skin tones that reflect the colors of water, such as pale blue, teal, or even sea green. Their hair may resemble sea foam or waves, often in shades of blue, green, or even white, and can appear to flow or ripple.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Ocean","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84 points","Titles: Fae, Water Genasi","Features:","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Sonar] F (7) - Supersense [Hearing] - Modified webbed ears can more easily hear nearby creatures when in water. Currents can help or hinder this feature. Only works in water.","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Swim Speed F (7)","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [Water] (7)","Resilient [Suffocation; Underwater] E (14)","Empathy F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-water-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-water-2.webp"],"aliases":["Water","Water Genasi"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-nymph","name":"Nymph","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Nymphs are fledgling nature fae that present exclusively as females with antlers. Their hair is constantly adorned with flowers and leaves, leading some to believe that these bits of foliage are actually a part of the nymph. Animals and non-monster creatures are generally friendly to nymphs and may even come to them when in distress. These maidens are of the forest and nature, but they are not yet bound to any part of the natural world. While all nymphs care for nature in their own way, some may choose to integrate into civilized society. Those who pursue their bond with nature will eventually become bound to the forest, waters, or mountains.","lifespan":"180 years","height":"Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Nymphs generally have a lean build, which allows them to move gracefully through their forest habitats. They are typically depicted with soft, natural features, embodying the beauty and vitality of nature. Their eyes may reflect the colors of the forest, such as deep greens or browns. Nymphs are known for their gentle movements, often taking their time to familiarize themselves with the natural world.","coloring":"Nymphs mostly have skin tones natural to humans, but they may also have a green tint. Their hair may have flowers or vines woven into it.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Dryads, Naiads, Nereids, Flora","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63 points","Evolves into: Dryad, Naiad, Nereid","Titles: Fae, Nymph","Features:","[Skin: (color)] - optional - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","Stats:","Strength or Speed - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Affinity [Plant] F (7)","Area Knowledge F (7)","Climbing F (7) or Swim Speed F (7)","Empathy F (7)","Nature F (7)","Perception F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Dryad, Naiad, Nereid","totalCost":"63 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-nymph-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-nymph-2.webp"],"aliases":["Nymph"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-umbral","name":"Umbral","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Umbrals arise when magic coalesces or a planar shift occurs and gives shape and sentience to the darkness. They are commonly used as minions by powerful creatures of malicious intent. Physically weaker than most other fae, shadows rely on their magical ability to survive.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 5'8\" to 6'4\" (173–193 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–220 lbs (68–100 kg) Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"They generally have a lean and agile build, emphasizing grace and stealth, which allows them to move silently through shadows. Umbrals are typically depicted with sharp, angular features that convey both beauty and a hint of danger. Their eyes might glow or reflect light in ways that enhance their enigmatic presence. They are known for their silent, graceful movements, often appearing to glide rather than walk, emphasizing their connection to the shadows.","coloring":"Umbrals often have skin tones that resemble shadows, including deep grays, blacks, or even shimmering dark hues. Their hair may vary from black to deep blue or purple, often appearing to flow like shadows.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Darkness Cardinal","Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 105 points","Titles: Fae, Umbral","Feature:","[Shadow Hair] - Hair flows and appears immaterial like shadows.","[Skin: Grayscale] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Eyes: Luminous] - Eyes appear to glow in various colors.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Night Camo] - Undetected [Sight] - While in lowlight, character can become undetectable by visual checks.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Telepathy F (21)","Magic F (7)","Affinity [Shadow] F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Undetected F [Sight] (14)","Empathy F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"105 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-umbral-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-umbral-2.webp"],"aliases":["Umbral"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-spirit","name":"Spirit","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Spirits are the life essence of a creature given form. Detaching from the physical body removes any former race titles, making the new entity a Fae Spirit. They can appear as any race, even abstract forms that may resemble the Construct tree. Reasons for why a spirit lingers widely vary, but some theorize the very nature of the world causes spirits to delay in crossing over or prevents it altogether by the interference of one or more deities.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"Any","weight":"None","physique":"Spirits often have a translucent or shimmering quality, appearing as if they are made of mist, smoke, or light. Their forms may shift and change, making them seem elusive. Spirits may have indistinct or vague facial features, sometimes appearing as shadowy outlines. When features are visible, they often convey expressions of peace, wisdom, or melancholy. If a spirit manifests clothing, it may appear flowing and ethereal, resembling robes or gowns made of light or wisps of cloud. The clothing often seems to merge with their surroundings. Spirits can vary in size, from small, delicate forms to larger, more imposing figures. Their shapes may be humanoid or completely abstract, reflecting their nature or energy. Spirits often move gracefully, gliding rather than walking, which adds to their ethereal presence. Their movement may leave a trail of light or mist behind.","coloring":"Common colors include soft whites, blues, or greens, often glowing faintly. Some spirits may take on hues that reflect their emotional state or purpose, such as deep reds for anger or muted grays for sorrow. Many spirits are surrounded by a faint glow or aura, which can vary in intensity. This aura may pulsate with energy or shimmer with colors that change in response to their emotions.","historicalFigures":["Spirit King (Fae See)"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77+ points","Titles: Fae, Spirit","Feature:","[Weightless] - Character has no physical mass.","[Hover] - optional - Character floats a few feet above solid ground. This replaces walking. Character cannot fly. Does not prevent fall damage.","[Astral Sight] F (7) - Feature Skill - Lighting doesn't affect vision. The material world appears in a monochrome color with every surface feature clearly visible as though always illuminated. It does not reveal illusions or invisibility.","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - C (21)","Skills:","Change State E (D) (42)","Limiter: Permanent","1 Secondary skill"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77+ points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-spirit-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-spirit-2.webp"],"aliases":["Spirit"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-sylph","name":"Sylph","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Fae spirits tied to the air. Usually, they live in nomadic colonies commonly referred to as “Ayrs,” that follow the direction of the wind. Upon death, it is believed a sylph’s body breaks apart and becomes air in the atmosphere. It is a common belief among sylphid that they exist to bring good deeds far and wide upon the wings of the wind.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"Male: 5'6\" to 6'2\" (168–188 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 120–180 lbs (54–82 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Sylphs often possess a slender, delicate build, emphasizing agility and lightness. Their physique is reminiscent of the fluidity of air. Sylphs typically have soft, refined features that convey a sense of beauty and tranquility. Their eyes may appear bright and reflective, often resembling the colors of the sky. Sylphs are known for their fluid, graceful movements, often appearing to glide or float rather than walk, which enhances their connection to the air.","coloring":"Sylphs may have skin that appears almost translucent or in soft, pastel hues, such as light blue, white, or pale green. Their hair often flows like wisps of air, resembling feathers or clouds, and can vary in color.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Sky","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 91 points","Evolves into: Dius Aer","Titles: Fae, Sylph","Feature:","[Air Hair] - Hair is made of visible air.","[Shimmering Visage] - The surface of the creature’s body sparkles as if by magic.","Stats:","Precision - C (21)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Flight F (21)","Magic F (7)","[Wind] Affinity F (7)","Illusion F (21)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Sixth Sense F [Weather] (7)","Resilient [Suffocation] F (7)","Area Knowledge [Area] (7)","Navigation F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Dius Aer","totalCost":"91 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-sylph-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-sylph-2.webp"],"aliases":["Sylph"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-sylvari","name":"Sylvari","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"A subspecies of Nymphs whose plant-based body is equally rooted in nature as the trees and flowers they reside over.","lifespan":"80 years","height":"Male: 6'0\" to 6'4\" (183–193 cm) Female: 5'6\" to 6'0\" (168–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Sylvari possess a lean and agile build, emphasizing elegance and fluidity in their movements. Their physique allows for both agility and strength. Their facial features are refined, with high cheekbones and expressive eyes that can reflect the colors of their environment or the seasons. They may have floral or vine-like patterns. Sylvari move with a grace that reflects their connection to the natural world, often appearing as if they flow rather than walk.","coloring":"Sylvari have skin that can vary in color, often resembling the hues of leaves and flowers, including greens, browns, and other earthy tones. Their skin may have a smooth, almost bark-like texture. Sylvari hair often resembles foliage, flowers, or vines, with colors that can range from vibrant greens to deep earth tones, enhancing their connection to nature.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Life Trees","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree","Neutral to Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 98 points","Titles: Fae, Sylvari","Features","[Plant Body] - Character has a body made out of plant-like matter, such as bark, vines and leaves. Bodily functions are supported by sap instead of blood. Their main sap vein is located where the spine is normally located, which is the core of their body and would kill them if destroyed.","[Heart's Seed] F (14 points) - An internal heart-like organ that functions like a catalyst and is rumored to house the soul.","[Plant Digestion] - Character doesn't eat food, but instead requires to take root in fertile soil to take in nutrients.","[Plant Resting] - Character doesn't need to lie down and sleep, but instead requires to stay rooted in place and meditate for longer periods to rest in order to get rid of fatigue and take in nutrients.","[Photosynthesis] - Character breathes in CO2 and breathes out O2, using photosynthesis to grow and to gain energy rather than burning calories.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Healing F (7)","Regeneration F (7)","Resilient [Critical] F (7)","Language [Flora, Fauna] (14 unless taken for free at creation)","Survival F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"98 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-sylvari-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-sylvari-2.webp"],"aliases":["Sylvari"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-yaksha","name":"Yaksha","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"The yaksha are a humanoid race that was first discovered on the Dark Continent. They claim to be descendants of former gods that have been tasked with keeping a nondescript darkness at bay. Yaksha have a special bond with the mask they wear. Despite its inhuman features, the mask is their true identity as much as the face behind it. Donning the mask–the symbol and vessel of their power–means destruction and hardship for their enemies.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male: 6'0\" to 7'0\" (183–213 cm) Female: 5'6\" to 6'6\" (168–198 cm)","weight":"Male: 180–250 lbs (82–113 kg) Female: 130–180 lbs (59–82 kg)","physique":"Yaksha (female: Yakshini) are generally tall and robust figures. They often have a strong, muscular build, reflecting their roles as guardians of treasures and nature. This physique emphasizes both strength and agility. Yakshas are usually depicted with handsome or beautiful features, symbolizing vitality and attractiveness. They may have expressive eyes and distinct facial ornaments. Yakshas are often adorned with intricate jewelry, such as necklaces, armlets, and crowns. Their clothing tends to be elaborate, reflecting their celestial or noble status. They move gracefully, embodying both power and elegance.","coloring":"Yaksha skin color can vary widely, often depicted in shades of green, gold, or earthy tones, representing their connection to nature and the earth.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Nature","Neutral to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 98 points","Titles: Fae, Yaksha","Feature:","[Luminous Tattoos] - Images etched into the skin shine under certain circumstances. Not bright enough to see in darkness.","[Skin: (color)] - optional - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Fighting Style F [weapon type] (7)","1 free tech","Magic F (7)","Affinity F [type] (7)","Heightened Sense F [Sight] (7)","Healing F (7)","Conversion F (21)","Arcana F (7)","Area Knowledge F [region] (7, free with Native path)","Perception F (7)","Item: Mask","“This, my face, will stare unflinching into the encroaching darkness, and when all other lights are blotted out, the Yaksha will stand in the gap–a luminous beacon.”","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"98 points","images":["assets/races/fae-mundane-yaksha-1.webp","assets/races/fae-mundane-yaksha-2.webp"],"aliases":["Yaksha"]},{"id":"fae-mundane-zentail","name":"Zentail","tree":"Fae","stage":"Mundane","description":"Zentail are a physically weaker, subterranean race that are well known for their administrative and tinkering skills as well as their exceptionally long lives. They are small, slender humanoids distinguished by their pale white skin, black eyes with piercing yellow-orange irises, and teeth devoid of canines (which renders them unable to properly chew meat, which they cannot digest). Due to physical deviations, their blood and muscle are an ebony black. Time spent underground has made the species sensitive to sunlight without exception–even ten minutes of exposure can be enough to leave them with a light sunburn. The Zentail derive needed nutrients from a variety of herbs grown in their subterranean caverns but also have a slow metabolism leading them to only need to eat once every three days. Zentail are exceptionally long lived due to the concoction of herbs they consume regularly, however being deprived of this mixture can cause dangerous health issues for them. The herbs they use are found wild, so typically this is not an issue. It is said that a Zentail completely deprived of the nutrients needed will fall into a coma and die within three days, this is called the \"Zentail Death Trance\". Zentail are rarely found in cities, and their unique physique requires them to wear specially tailored clothes at all times.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Any: 2’ to 4’ (60–121 cm)","weight":"Any: 25–70 lbs (11–32 kg)","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Nature","Neutral to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost:","Evolves into: Zentox","Titles: Fae, Zentail","Feature:","[Skin: Pale] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Eyes: Black/Yellow-Orange] - Eyes are completely black save for yellow-orange iris.","[Blood: Black] - Blood and viscera are black.","[Sunlight Sensitivity] - Sunlight easily burns or negatively impacts the health of this creature.","[Slow Metabolism] - Creature does not need sustenance as often.","Stats: Strength - G (Cannot Exceed)","Skills: 2 or more secondary skills"],"evolvesInto":"Zentox","totalCost":"","images":[],"aliases":["Zentail"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-dius-aer","name":"Dius Aer","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Once the wings of sylph develop, it signifies his spiritual maturity and his becoming of a dius aer. Unlike sylphid, dius aerim’s bodies are composed of photons and soundwaves. The sight of a dius aer is usually a fortunate sign of nearing spring and that the weather will be calm. When the wings of a dius aer are severed, they die, and turn into specks of light.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"Male: 5'6\" to 6'2\" (168–188 cm) Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Male: 120–180 lbs (54–82 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Sylphs often possess a slender, delicate build, emphasizing agility and lightness. Their physique is reminiscent of the fluidity of air. Sylphs typically have soft, refined features that convey a sense of beauty and tranquility. Their eyes may appear bright and reflective, often resembling the colors of the sky. Sylphs are known for their fluid, graceful movements, often appearing to glide or float rather than walk, which enhances their connection to the air.","coloring":"Sylphs may have skin that appears almost translucent or in soft, pastel hues, such as light blue, white, or pale green. Their hair often flows like wisps of air, resembling feathers or clouds, and can vary in color.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), the Sky","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Sylph","Title: Fae, Sylph, Dius Aer","Features:","[Air Hair] - Hair is made of visible air.","[Shimmering Visage] - The surface of the creature’s body sparkles as if by magic.","[Wings] - Paired appendages capable of flight. Requires Flight skill to actually fly.","Skills","Flight F","Control Environment D","Magic D","[Wind] Affinity C","Illusion F (21)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Sixth Sense F [Weather] (7)","Change State C","Resilient [Fatigue, Aging, Suffocation] D","Area Knowledge [Area] (7)","Navigation F (7)","1 Secondary skill of choice","Choose one Perk:","[Trademark Spell] - one magic ability has its cooldown permanently reduced by 1 post. Cannot be altered after becoming the Trademark Spell.","[Asset: Spirit companion] - Choose an IH Element (ex: fire, wind, water,etc). The companion serves the role of connecting the average fae to their faith in the spirit king and the elements. Ex: Worshipers of the flame Cardinal would get a flame spirit companion that occasionally chimes in with guidance or a message for character from the see faith."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-dius-aer-1.webp"],"aliases":["Dius Aer","Sylph"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-dryad","name":"Dryad","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Tree nymphs who are specifically linked to oak trees, though they can also be associated with other types of trees.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Dryads generally have a lean, athletic build, emphasizing agility and grace, which allows them to move fluidly through their forest habitats. They are typically depicted with soft, natural features, embodying the beauty and vitality of nature. Their eyes may reflect the colors of the forest, such as deep greens or browns. Dryads are known for their graceful movements, often appearing to dance or glide through their environments, reflecting their connection to trees and nature.","coloring":"Dryads often have skin tones that reflect the bark of trees, ranging from earthy browns to greens. Their hair may be leafy or resemble branches, often in shades of green, brown, or even adorned with flowers.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Flora","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Nymph","Evolves into: Oread","Titles: Fae, Dryad","Features:","[Floral Hair] - Hair resembles plantlife.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","Stats:","Strength - E","Intelligence - B","Skills:","Magic C","Affinity [Plant] C","Affinity [Entangle] C","Control Environment E","Sixth Sense D [Contamination]","Area Knowledge E","Climbing F","Empathy E","Medicine E","Nature C","Perception E","Survival D","Choose one Perk:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Trademark Spell] - one magic ability has its cooldown permanently reduced by 1 post. Cannot be altered after becoming the Trademark Spell.","[Asset: Spirit companion] - Choose an IH Element (ex: fire, wind, water,etc). The companion serves the role of connecting the average fae to their faith in the spirit king and the elements. Ex: Worshipers of the flame Cardinal would get a flame spirit companion that occasionally chimes in with guidance or a message for character from the see faith."],"evolvesInto":"Oread","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-dryad-1.webp","assets/races/fae-intermediate-dryad-2.webp"],"aliases":["Dryad"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-lightfoot-halfling","name":"Lightfoot Halfling","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Lightfoot Halflings are small fae preoccupied with exploring and travelling around the world. Their quick and alert nature has made them experts at spotting trouble and running from danger.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Male/Female: 3' to 4' (91.44--121.92 cm)","weight":"Male/Female: 30 to 46 lbs (13.61--20.87 kg)","physique":"Halflings often have a sturdy and well-proportioned build, with a slightly rounded appearance. They tend to be more robust than they look. Halflings usually have round faces with soft features and cheerful expressions. They may have curly or wavy hair, often worn long, with some male halflings sporting facial hair.","coloring":"Their skin tones can range widely, similar to humans, often with a healthy, sun-kissed appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Friendly to Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct Trees, especially small races","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Halfling","Titles: Fae, Halfling, Lightfoot Halfling","Feature: Small Size","Stat:","Intelligence - D","Speed C","Skill:","Fast D","Heightened Sense E [Hearing/Sight]","Resilient [Fear] F (7)","Energized F (7)","Lucky F"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-lightfoot-halfling-1.webp"],"aliases":["Halfling","Lightfoot Halfling"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-naiad","name":"Naiad","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Water nymphs who inhabit rivers, springs, and lakes. They are often associated with fresh water.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Naiads generally have a lean and athletic build, emphasizing grace and agility, which allows them to move effortlessly through water. Naiads are typically depicted with soft, enchanting features, representing the beauty of the natural world. Their eyes may have shades reminiscent of water, such as deep blues or greens. Naiads are known for their fluid movements, often appearing to glide or swim rather than walk, reflecting their connection to water and their aquatic lifestyle.","coloring":"Naiads often have skin tones that reflect the colors of water, such as pale blue, green, or even shimmery hues that mimic the surface of water. Their hair may resemble flowing water, often in shades of blue or green, and can appear wavy or cascading.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Water","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Nymph","Evolves into: Oread","Titles: Fae, Naiad","Features:","[Water Hair] - Hair is fluid or is constantly drenched.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Water Camo] D (42) - Undetected [Sight] - While fully submerged in water, character can become undetectable by visual checks.","Stats:","Precision - C","Intelligence - B","Speed - C","Skills:","Swim Speed D","Magic C","Affinity [Water] C","Sixth Sense E [Contamination]","Supersense E [Hydrodynamics]","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Control Environment E","Resilient [Suffocation] F","Healing F","Nature F","2 more Secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Trademark Spell] - one magic ability has its cooldown permanently reduced by 1 post. Cannot be altered after becoming the Trademark Spell.","[Asset: Spirit companion] - Choose an IH Element (ex: fire, wind, water,etc). The companion serves the role of connecting the average fae to their faith in the spirit king and the elements. Ex: Worshipers of the flame Cardinal would get a flame spirit companion that occasionally chimes in with guidance or a message for character from the see faith."],"evolvesInto":"Oread","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-naiad-1.webp","assets/races/fae-intermediate-naiad-2.webp"],"aliases":["Naiad"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-nereid","name":"Nereid","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Sea nymphs associated with the Continental Lake and oceans surrounding the Second Continent, often appearing as beautiful maidens who assist sailors.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Female: 5'2\" to 6'0\" (157–183 cm)","weight":"Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Nereids generally have a lean and athletic build, emphasizing agility and fluidity, which enhances their swimming ability. Nereids are typically depicted with soft, alluring features that embody the beauty of the ocean. Their eyes often have deep oceanic hues, such as turquoise or sea green. Nereids are known for their fluid movements, often appearing to glide or swim rather than walk, reflecting their aquatic lifestyle. Unlike naiads, however, nereids usually create locomotion in water by manipulating currents with their magic.","coloring":"Nereids often have skin tones that reflect the colors of the sea, such as pale blue, green, or shimmering silver. Their hair may resemble flowing seaweed or waves, usually in shades of blue, green, or white.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Storm fae","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Nymph","Evolves into: Oread","Titles: Fae, Nereid","Features:","[Seaweed Hair] - Hair appears as seaweed or is constantly drenched.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Water Camo] D (42) - Undetected [Sight] - While fully submerged in water, character can become undetectable by visual checks.","Stats:","Precision - C","Intelligence - B","Speed - C","Skills:","Swim Speed D","Magic C","Affinity [Water] C","Affinity [Storm] C","Sixth Sense C [Contamination]","Supersense E [Hydrodynamics]","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Control Environment E","Resilient [Suffocation] F","Nature F","2 more Secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Trademark Spell] - one magic ability has its cooldown permanently reduced by 1 post. Cannot be altered after becoming the Trademark Spell.","[Asset: Spirit companion] - Choose an IH Element (ex: fire, wind, water,etc). The companion serves the role of connecting the average fae to their faith in the spirit king and the elements. Ex: Worshipers of the flame Cardinal would get a flame spirit companion that occasionally chimes in with guidance or a message for character from the see faith."],"evolvesInto":"Oread","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-nereid-1.webp","assets/races/fae-intermediate-nereid-2.webp"],"aliases":["Nereid"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-remembrance","name":"Remembrance","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"A remembrance is a humanoid or bestial manifestation that forms in the aftermath of untimely death and suffering, commonly appearing on old battlefields. Their appearance and adornments are symbols of the suffering felt by the fallen. It is the duty of the remembrance to remember the slain and avenge them if possible. Due to the often long delay between the time of death and the spawning of the remembrance, vengeance might be exacted on next of kin or accomplices. The remembrance is not swayed by morality and may manifest after a truly evil creature was slain. After fulfilling its duty, the remembrance is called to a relevant shrine, gravesite or battlefield where it performs the Rite of Remembrance to appease the fallen and usher both the remembrance and the lingering spirits into the afterlife.","lifespan":"25 years","height":"6’ to 9’ (182–274 cm)","weight":"140–600 lbs (63.5–272.2 kg)","physique":"Remembrance physique does not always accurately reflect overall strength or durability. Their forms are often emaciated, hinting at the death that birthed them, but they are capable of withstanding heavy blows. Their eyes may be obscured or missing altogether, yet they are not blind. Though they have corporeal forms, they may have the ability to pass through solid objects. Some remembrances can move normally, at times even gracefully, while at other times they have erratic movements reminiscent of undead.","coloring":"Their skin takes on various colors of death: blackened, scorched; pale, exsanguinated; green, gangrenous. Their forms are commonly adorned with various decorations that can seem artistic at first, but symbolize the kind of death suffered.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees","Hostile to obstacles"],"requirements":["Titles: Fae, Spirit, Remembrance","Features:","[Astral Sight] F (7) - Feature Skill - Lighting doesn't affect vision. The material world appears in a monochrome color with every surface feature clearly visible as though always illuminated. It does not reveal illusions or invisibility.","Stats:","Strength or Intelligence - B","Precision - E","Vitality - C","Skills:","Special Movement F [Zen Direction]","Fighting Style C or Magic C","Blindfighter","Sixth Sense F [any]","Change State D","Resistance D [type]","3 Secondary skill"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-remembrance-1.webp","assets/races/fae-intermediate-remembrance-2.webp"],"aliases":["Remembrance","Spirit"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-vessel-cirche","name":"Vessel Cirche","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Vessel Cirche are fairies that have become vessels for some great power that was either bestowed or simply unlocked from the fairy’s own potential. Depending on the nature of this power, the fairy might take on an elder role or become a mighty warrior. Although rare and immensely dangerous, there have been cases where a Vessel came to house two different powers. In these cases, one power was awakened from within, and the other power was received from an external source.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"5\" to 1' (15–30 cm)","weight":"1–5 lbs (0.5–2.3 kg)","physique":"Fairies are typically very small, often ranging from about 5 inches to 1 foot (15 to 30 cm) in height. Their petite size contributes to their delicate and whimsical appearance. Fairies generally have slender, graceful bodies that reflect their agility and lightness. They often appear fragile yet agile. Many fairies possess wings that can resemble those of butterflies, dragonflies, or other insects. These wings are often iridescent and may vary greatly in size and shape, contributing to their magical appearance. Fairies typically have enchanting, youthful faces with large, expressive eyes. Their features are often characterized by sharp cheekbones and delicate, pointed ears. Fairies are known for their graceful movements and agility, often depicted as flitting through the air or dancing lightly on the ground.","coloring":"Their skin may have a luminescent quality, often depicted in various shades, sometimes reflecting their connection to nature. Fairies have colorful hair, typically adorned with flowers and natural elements, enhancing their connection to the environment.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Nature-related races","Friendly to Fae tree, Beast tree","Neutral to Prime tree, Construct Tree, Insectoid races","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Fairy","Titles: Fae, Fairy, Vessel Cirche","Feature:","Tiny size (+14)","[Ears: Pointy] - Short, fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Wings: Insectoid] - Paired appendages capable of flight.","[Iridescent] - The above feature shows luminous colors that seem to change when seen from different angles.","Stats:","Precision - B","Intelligence - B","Skills:","Flight E","Magic C","Undetected F [Sight] (14)","1 Secondary skill"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-intermediate-vessel-cirche-1.webp"],"aliases":["Fairy","Vessel Cirche"]},{"id":"fae-intermediate-zentox","name":"Zentox","tree":"Fae","stage":"Intermediate","description":"A Zentox is a Zentail who has, through a process of undergoing major stress and living outside of their natural environment, changed to a heartier form of life. They retain most of the physical attributes they previously had, but they will become slightly shorter, lose the sensitivity to sunlight previously possessed, and their eyes shift from the previous yellow-orange color to a darker red. Additionally, the natural weakness of the Zentail will lessen, and they can begin to build muscle. Generally, Zentox have already become skilled craftsmen, tinkerers, or administrative officials.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Any: 2’ to 4’ (60–121 cm)","weight":"Any: 25–70 lbs (11–32 kg)","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Nature","Neutral to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves into: Zentail","Titles: Fae, Zentail","Feature:","[Skin: Pale] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Eyes: Black/Red] - Eyes are completely black save for dark red iris.","[Blood Color] - Blood and viscera are black.","[Slow Metabolism] - Creature does not need sustenance as often.","Stats:","Precision - C","Intelligence - C","Skills: 2 or more secondary skills"],"evolvesInto":"Zentail","totalCost":"","images":[],"aliases":["Zentail","Zentox"]},{"id":"fae-ascended-oread","name":"Oread","tree":"Fae","stage":"Ascended","description":"Mountain nymphs who dwell in the hills and mountains, embodying the spirit of the rugged terrain.","lifespan":"240 years","height":"Female: 5'4\" to 6'2\" (163–188 cm)","weight":"Female: 120–180 lbs (54–82 kg)","physique":"Oreads generally have a muscular and robust build, emphasizing strength and endurance, which is suited for navigating rocky landscapes. They are typically depicted with strong, angular features that convey a sense of resilience and connection to nature. Despite their muscular build, oreads are known for their agility, often moving gracefully through their mountainous environments.","coloring":"Oreads often have skin tones that reflect earthy colors, such as warm browns or tans. Their hair may resemble natural elements, like flowing streams or rocky outcrops, often in shades of brown, green, or even gray.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder Fae (the Spirit King), Earth","Friendly to Prime tree, Fae tree, Beast tree, Construct tree","Hostile to Monster Tree"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Dryad, Naiad, Nereid","Titles: Fae, Oread","Features:","Choose a hair type:","[Moss Hair] - Hair grows as strands of moss. Form is flexible.","[Mineral Hair] - Hair is formed by crystalline minerals erupting from the scalp. Form is fixed.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Gemsight] F (14) - Supersense [Telescopic Vision, Magnification] - Eyes possess crystalline structures that enhance magnification, allowing them to see distant objects or detect fine detail up close.","[Earth Camo] D (42) - Undetected [Sight] - Remaining still against earthen scenery prevents detection by visual inspection.","Stats:","Strength - C","Precision - C","Intelligence - S","Vitality - C","Skills:","Magic A","Affinity [Earth] A","Sixth Sense C [Contamination]","Resistance [Bludgeoning] F","Climbing F","Nature F","4 more Secondary skills","Choose one Perk:","[Apex] - gain the title Apex. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","[Queen/King Bee] - gain the Queen/King Bee title. You are at the top of the species pecking order and considered a special existence. You are generally permitted audience with the leaders of factions and heads of state. Nations where your race is the majority tend to look to those of your grade for guidance or alliance.","Choose 1:","[Componentless Affinity] - If Trademark Spell was chosen, the Fae may now cast their trademark spell without components as if they had component less casting.","[Domain] - Gain access to a miniature world in a subspace of your own creation. May have inhabitants such as animals but nothing sentient (human level intelligence) short of rp’ing their moving into the domain."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/fae-ascended-oread-1.webp","assets/races/fae-ascended-oread-2.webp"],"aliases":["Oread"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-darkling","name":"Darkling","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Darklings are the first and weakest of monsters spawned in when too much chaos/mana concentrates in an area. Incubation time varies, but it is typically not immediate. Likely locations for darkling or other monster spawning are deep underground, in deep ocean, or deep in forests where mana congestion occurs. Creatures spawn with appropriate means to survive the environment in which they spawn (breathing underwater, darkvision in caves, etc.). Darklings are drawn to and feed off of forms of life--sentient creatures being the most potent form. Consuming enough living essence allows the darkling to evolve.","lifespan":"1 year","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2.43–4.87 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4.87 m) tall/long","weight":"Any, divide given values in half Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg) Large: 500 to 4000 lbs (2 tons)(226.79–1.81 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1.81 mt)","physique":"Darklings manifest in humanoid and bestial forms. The humanoid forms tend to be emaciated or very minimal in conveying the silhouette. The bestial forms can and tend to be more robust. Both forms come equipped with teeth and claws.","coloring":"Darklings appear as living shadows. All forms appear wispy and immaterial, but there is a solid component that can be touched or wounded.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: +42 points","Titles: Monster, Darkling","Features:","[Living Shadow] - Form is black and wispy.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength or Vitality E (7)","Precision E (7)","Skills:","Special Movement [Void Slither] (14 points) - become 2D and move along adjoining surfaces at normal movement speed.","Equipment: Natural Weapons F OR Natural Armor F (Heavy or Light)(14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"+42 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-darkling-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-darkling-2.webp"],"aliases":["Darkling"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-demon","name":"Demon","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Demons are the product of living creatures becoming corrupted by a sudden influx of dense mana. Their physical form undergoes a permanent transformation, assuming a new form that may be influenced by certain negative personality traits (e.g., greed). Demons are commonly associated with the so-called “seven deadly sins”, becoming embodiments of these concepts, but they may embody other concepts as well.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2–4 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4 m) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3 kg) Small: 8–60 lbs (3–27 kg) Medium: 61–499 lbs (27–226 kg) Large: 500–4000 lbs (2 tons)(226 kg to 1 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1 mt)","physique":"Demons may manifest forms resembling robust beasts or lean humanoids. While transforming, a physical medium black in color (some believe this to be dregs from the soul) erupts from within their form and envelopes them. This medium hardens into natural armor or natural weapons, changing color as its shape solidifies. Demons possess uncommon strength for the size of their forms, especially their humanoid forms. They are known to be exceedingly agile, scaling cliffsides with their claws or leaping giant ravines. Some even possess flying ability through physical wings or more magical means.","coloring":"Demons commonly come in obsidian black and vibrant reds, but the demon’s whimsy could see many exotic colors manifest. They may have a gaping hole or crater on the torso, or occasionally the head, believed to be the main fount from which the black medium erupted. This feature appears to be cosmetic once the form solidifies and may even shrink with time.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 35 points","Titles: Monster, Demon","Features:","[Avulsion] - Area of torn flesh on the surface of the body forming a shallow pit. Not necessarily a wound or vulnerability.","[Skin: (color)] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","1 movement skill","1 sense skill","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"35 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-demon-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-demon-2.webp"],"aliases":["Demon"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-drake","name":"Drake","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"A flightless cousin of dragons, drakes are a quadruped reptilian beast. The mundane form is about the size of a horse, which makes it suitable as a mount in some areas. Drakes can come in elemental forms, and the Greater Drakes are often mistaken for younger dragons due to their size.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 6’ to 12’ (1.8–3.7 m) Female: 5’ to 10’ (1.5–3.0 m)","weight":"Male: 100–400 lbs (45–181 kg) Female: 80–300 lbs (36–136 kg)","physique":"Drakes generally have a strong, muscular build designed for power and agility on the ground. Their physique emphasizes strength, allowing them to navigate various terrains effectively. Drakes have a broad, powerful head with sharp teeth, suitable for a carnivorous diet. They may possess distinct facial features, such as prominent horns or crests. Their limbs are well-developed, with powerful legs that provide speed and stability. They have sharp claws adapted for hunting or climbing. A long, flexible tail is common, used for balance and communication.","coloring":"Drakes are often covered in tough, scaly skin that can vary in color, typically ranging from earthy tones like greens, browns, and grays to more vibrant hues.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 126 points","Evolves into: Wyvern","Titles: Monster, Drake","Feature:","Large size (above 8 feet/500 lbs)(14)","Height: 8 to 16 feet tall/long","Weight: 500 to 4000 pounds (2 tons)","Strength:","Character can lift and carry 5x more weight. Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","Plus 1 strength effectiveness to non-attack actions","Base throw distance doubled - 60ft base distance (accurate throw*) (object that fits in hand)","Vitality: Mundane damage received is reduced by 1","Speed: Minus 1 speed effectiveness","Movement: Base movement doubled - 40ft base movement","Narrative: \"Big\", \"Heavy\", \"Obvious\" - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudication outcomes for this character","[Quadruped] - Creature has four legs.","[Scales] - Skin is totally covered in reptilian scales.","[Spines] - Any hard, pointed defensive projection or structure.","[Ears: Reptilian] - A thin membrane located at the rear of the head.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Fighting Style [Natural Weapon] F (7)","1 technique (7 point discount)","Superstrength F (14)","Heightened Sense F [Smell] (7)","Climbing F (7)","Intimidation F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Wyvern","totalCost":"126 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-drake-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-drake-2.webp"],"aliases":["Drake"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-goblin","name":"Goblin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"A monster race of a generally weaker variety. High potential for stronger variants. Low survivability. Despite this, goblins are known for their uncanny ability to hide away, repopulate, and infest a different location after being driven out.","lifespan":"50 years","height":"Male: 3’ to 4’ (0.9–1.2 m) Female: 2.5’ to 3.5’ (0.76–1.07 m)","weight":"Male: 40–70 lbs (18–32 kg) Female: 30–60 lbs (14–27 kg)","physique":"Goblins are typically small, averaging between 2.5 to 4 feet (0.76 to 1.2 meters) in height. Their stature is often hunched, contributing to a somewhat smaller appearance. Goblins usually have a lean, wiry build, emphasizing agility and speed over brute strength. They are nimble, which aids in their ability to escape danger or navigate through their environments. They typically have large, pointed ears, sharp teeth, and a broad, flat nose. Their eyes are often large and expressive, enhancing their mischievous or cunning appearance. Goblins may have sparse hair, often depicted as unkempt or wild. Goblins have relatively long arms and short legs, which contributes to their agility. Their fingers are often dexterous, allowing them to use tools or weapons effectively. Goblins usually have a hunched posture, which adds to their furtive and sneaky demeanor. This posture also allows them to move quickly and quietly. Goblins are cunning and mischievous, with a tendency towards trickery and stealth. Their physique supports these behaviors, allowing them to be effective scouts or thieves.","coloring":"Goblins often have green, gray, or brown skin, which can help them blend into their surroundings.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 126 points","Evolves into: Hobgoblin","Titles: Monster, Goblin","Feature:","Small size (+7)","Height: 2 to 4 feet tall/long","Weight: 8 to 60 pounds","Strength:","Character's lift and carry/5 . Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","Minus 1 strength action effectiveness","Base throw distance reduced by 50% - 15ft base distance (accurate throw*) (object that fits in hand)","Vitality: Mundane damage received is increased 1","Speed:","Plus 1 speed action effectiveness","Plus 1 effectiveness to stealth actions","Attack: Attacks can have accurate F applied without changing cooldown or grade of attack","Movement: Base movement reduced by 50%","Narrative: \"Small\", \"Light\", \"Unobtrusive\" - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudicating actions","[Eyes: Bestial] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - D (14)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - D (14)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Fighting Style F [weapon type] (7)","1 tech (7 point discount)","Heightened Sense E [Smell, Hearing] (14)","Undetected [Sound] (14)","Acrobatics F (7)","Climbing F (7)","Stealth F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Hobgoblin","totalCost":"126 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-goblin-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-goblin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Goblin"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-harpy","name":"Harpy","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Monsters that take the appearance of bird-like humanoids without hands. Harpies are a female race and are known for their cruel and mischievous nature.","lifespan":"120 years","height":"Female: 5’ to 7’ (1.5–2.1 m)","weight":"Female: 100–200 lbs (45–90 kg)","physique":"Harpies stand between 5 to 7 feet (1.5 to 2.1 meters) tall, with a slender, elongated body that emphasizes their agility and grace. The upper body resembles that of a woman. This includes a human-like head, arms, and torso. Harpies have large, powerful wings that are usually attached to their arms. These wings enable flight and contribute to their bird-like appearance. The wingspan can be considerable, enhancing their ability to soar. The lower body often resembles that of a bird, featuring feathers instead of human legs. Their feet have sharp talons, allowing them to grasp and attack. Harpies usually have sharp, pointed facial features, often with a beak-like mouth. Their eyes are typically large and expressive, sometimes depicted as having a fierce or predatory gaze. Feathers may cover parts of their body, particularly their arms and lower body, adding to their avian characteristics. Harpies are able to fly and navigate through the air gracefully. Their movements can be quick and erratic, fitting their mischievous and unpredictable nature. The physique of harpies reflects their roles as both beautiful and dangerous creatures. They are swift and cunning, using their agility to evade capture or to ambush their prey.","coloring":"A harpy’s plumage matches the sort of bird its avian features mimic. This allows for common earthen tones as well as exotic colorations found on jungle birds.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 91 points","Titles: Monster, Harpy","Feature:","[Feathers] - Naturally occurring plumage that covers virtually all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Wings] - Paired appendages capable of flight. Requires Flight skill to actually fly.","[Telescopic Vision] (7) - The ability to see distant objects with great clarity, similar to looking through a telescope.","[Talons] - Sharp, hooked claws of predatory avians like eagles, hawks, and owls, designed for catching prey.","Stats:","Precision - C (21)","Intelligence - E (7)","Skills:","Flight F (21)","Heightened Sense F [Vision] (7)","Sixth Sense F [Danger] (7)","Perception F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"91 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-harpy-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-harpy-2.webp"],"aliases":["Harpy"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-imp","name":"Imp","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Monsters that take the appearance of bird-like humanoids without hands. Harpies are a female race and are known for their cruel and mischievous nature.","lifespan":"50 years","height":"Male: 1.5’ to 3’ (0.45–0.9 m) Female: 1.5’ to 2.5’ (0.45–0.76 m)","weight":"Male: 10–30 lbs (4.5–13.6 kg) Female: 8–25 lbs (3.6–11.3 kg)","physique":"Imps are generally small creatures. Their small stature contributes to their agility and stealth. Imps usually have a slim, wiry build, allowing for quick movements and evasive actions. They are designed for agility rather than brute strength. Imps typically have pointed ears, sharp features, and mischievous or malevolent expressions. Many imps have small horns on their heads and a long, thin tail, which may be prehensile or used for balance. Imps usually have long, thin arms and legs, often ending in clawed fingers and toes. This makes them adept at climbing and sneaking. Some imps have small, bat-like wings, which they can use for short flights or gliding, enhancing their agility and ability to escape quickly. The physique of imps supports their roles as tricksters and mischievous beings, allowing them to navigate their environments stealthily and evade capture.","coloring":"Imp skin comes in various shades, including red, green, or gray, and may appear smooth or slightly textured. Their eyes are often large and also come in vibrant colors, adding to their otherworldly appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 126 points","Evolves into: Devil, Fiend","Titles: Monster, Imp","Feature:","[Skin: (color(s))] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Wings] - optional - Paired appendages capable of flight. Requires Flight skill to actually fly.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - D (14)","Intelligence - D (14)","Speed - D (14)","Skills:","Special Movement F [Fancy Falling] (14)","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell] (14)","Sixth Sense F [Danger or Manavision] (7)","Climbing F (7)","Deception F or Intimidation F (7)","Sleight of Hand F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Devil, Fiend","totalCost":"126 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-imp-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-imp-2.webp"],"aliases":["Imp"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-living-armor","name":"Living Armor","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"A monster race of sentient equipment. Some are dungeon sentries. Some are the source of cursed armor tales. Living armor is considered sentient, capable of independent thought, and may exhibit personality traits or motives. It can serve as a protector, guardian, or even a companion to its wearer.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2.43–4.87 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4.87 m) tall/long","weight":"Any, divide given values in half Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg) Large: 500 to 4000 lbs (2 tons)(226.79–1.81 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1.81 mt)","physique":"Living armor is typically composed of a material that resembles traditional armor (metal, leather, or a magical substance) but is animated by a life force or consciousness. This can create a flexible yet protective exterior. The size of living armor can vary widely, ranging from that of a human to larger, more imposing figures, depending on its intended purpose (e.g., a suit worn by a warrior or a stand-alone guardian). Living armor often takes on a humanoid shape, resembling a knight or warrior, but it may also have more abstract forms, depending on its origin or magical nature. Living armor is capable of movement, often mimicking the mobility of a humanoid being. It may exhibit fluid motions or more mechanical, rigid movements, depending on its design and purpose. These features can convey emotion or intent. The armor can be made of various materials, including enchanted metals, bones, or even organic components. This composition may grant it unique properties, like enhanced durability or magical abilities.","coloring":"The surface of living armor can appear smooth, like polished metal, or rugged, resembling battle-worn armor. Some variations might have intricate designs or glowing runes that hint at its magical nature. Living armor may possess facial features, such as eyes that glow or shift, adding to its sentience.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 77 points","Titles: Monster, Living Armor","Feature:","[Separable] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows major appendages and head to harmlessly separate from the torso and reattach.","[Omniswivel] (7) - allows a joint be Twisted 360 degrees without injury","Stat:","Strength- E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Fighting Style F [Weapon type] (7)","1 tech (7 point discount)","Resilience E [Fatigue (caused by hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Suffocation] (14)","Resistance F [type] (7)","Equipment: Natural Armor (light/heavy) F (14)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"77 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-living-armor-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-living-armor-2.webp"],"aliases":["Living Armor"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-nevermore","name":"Nevermore","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Nevermore are tall vaguely avian creatures with branches emerging from their heads like antlers. Ironically nicknamed \"Helpers\", nevermores make for one unforgettable encounter--assuming you survive. While their origins are unknown, survivors have reported them as having many different, inarguably useful abilities. The nature of the creature, however, is to exact a steep price for using any of its \"services\". To depart unscathed is a rarity.","lifespan":"168 years","height":"7' to 8’ (213–243 cm)","weight":"250–450 lbs (113–204 kg)","physique":"Nevermore stand tall at 7’ to 8’. Despite their height, some can move with a regal poise and elegance befitting a noble. They may or may not have a beak, but regardless all nevermore have a mouthful of carnivorous teeth. Nevermore may possess wings separate from their arms or have feathers emerging directly from their arms. Even so, not all nevermore possess the ability to fly. Their legs are thin and bony with typical avian style feet beneath them. Some nevermore possess a thin, wiry tail reminiscent of imps and fiends. Nevermore stand taller when negotiating with their next victim, but assume a hunched, more feral stance when exacting their price or attacking.","coloring":"Nevermore typically possess at minimum a mantle of plumage that adorns their shoulders, upper arms, back and chest. This plumage is commonly shades of deep purple and blue with tinges of a lavender or pink when caught in the light.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 98 points","Titles: Monster, Nevermore","Feature:","[Antlers] - Paired branched horns that grow from the creature’s skull and are periodically shed. Nevermore antlers resemble tree branches.","[Bird Head] - A head of avian design.","[Skin: Pale] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Long tongue] - A tongue long enough to be an additional arm for those coordinated enough to use it as such.","[Talons] - Sharp, hooked claws of predatory avians like eagles, hawks, and owls, designed for catching prey.","[Tail] - optional - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - D (14)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","1 Movement skill","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Smell] (7)","Healing F (7)","Intimidation F or Deception F (7)","Persuasion F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"98 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-nevermore-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-nevermore-2.webp"],"aliases":["Nevermore"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-ogre-oni","name":"Ogre/Oni","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Ogres are large, brutish creatures that enjoy feasting on passersby. Often drafted into nefarious armies during wartime, ogres are generally prized for their strength and durability. Consignment to slavery is the last thing on any ogre’s mind, however, so they hide away in tall mountains and deep forests when they can.","lifespan":"50 years","height":"Male: 8’ to 10’ (2.4 to 3.0 m) Female: 7’ to 9’ (2.1–2.7 m)","weight":"Male: 400–600 lbs (181–272 kg) Female: 300–500 lbs (136–227 kg)","physique":"Ogres are typically massive, ranging from 8 to 10 feet (2.4 to 3.0 meters) in height. Their sheer size contributes to their intimidating presence. They have a muscular and robust build, with broad shoulders and thick limbs. Ogres are usually heavily muscled, emphasizing strength and a stocky frame. They frequently have large, pronounced features, including a broad, flat nose, thick lips, and prominent brow ridges. Their eyes are often described as small and beady, adding to their monstrous look. Ogres may have large, tusk-like teeth that are visible even when their mouths are closed, enhancing their fearsome appearance. Ogres have powerful arms and legs, well-suited for physical confrontation. Their hands and feet are typically large, with thick fingers and toes that may end in claws. They tend to have a lumbering or heavy gait due to their size, but despite this, they are capable of surprising bursts of speed and agility when needed. The physique of ogres often reflects their role as brutish fighters or laborers, with a focus on raw strength and endurance. They may also be somewhat clumsy or lacking in finesse.","coloring":"Ogres often have coarse skin that can range in color from green to brown or gray, giving them an earthy appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 189 points","Titles: Monster, Ogre/Oni","Feature:","Large Size (14)","Height: 8 to 16 feet tall/long","Weight: 500 to 4000 pounds (2 tons)","Strength:","Character can lift and carry 5x more weight. Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","Plus 1 strength effectiveness to non-attack actions","Base throw distance doubled - 60ft base distance (accurate throw*) (object that fits in hand)","Vitality: Mundane damage received is reduced by 1","Speed: Minus 1 speed effectiveness","Movement: Base movement doubled - 40ft base movement","Narrative: \"Big\", \"Heavy\", \"Obvious\" - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudication outcomes for this character","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - D (14)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Special Movement F [Speedburst] (7)","Superstrength F (14)","Heightened Sense [Smell, Hearing] E (14)","Resistance F [Physical] (21)","Conversion F (21)","Intimidation F (7)","Survival F (7)","Equipment:","Natural Weapons F (14)","Natural Armor (heavy) F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"189 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-ogre-oni-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-ogre-oni-2.webp"],"aliases":["Ogre","Ogre/Oni","Oni"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-oni-ork","name":"Oni-Ork","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"A race among the fae that is more primal in nature. Prizing strength over any other trait, the orc tribes are known to be formidable in battle. Despite their reverence for strength, some orcs worship deities and are granted magical power.","lifespan":"112 years","height":"7’ to 8’ (2.13--2.44 m)","weight":"350–450 lbs (159–204 kg)","physique":"Oni-Orks stand at an impressive height of about 8 feet (2.44 meters) for males and 7 feet (2.13 meters) for females. Their towering stature emphasizes both strength and presence. They possess a massively muscular and robust build, which blends stocky strength with a toned agile physique. Oni-Orks have broad shoulders, thick limbs, and a solid core, highlighting their physical power and endurance. The skin is often tough and resilient, suitable for combat. Oni-Orks have prominent, defined features. They commonly possess a strong jawline, large, expressive eyes, and pronounced brow ridges, lending an intimidating aspect to their appearance. One distinct feature is the presence of horns. These may vary in shape and size, protruding from their foreheads and curving backward or upward. The horns are rugged and rough, resembling those of a ram or more elaborate like those of other mythical beasts, and are often a symbol of strength and dominance. Their arms and legs are powerful and muscular, with thick arms suited for wielding weapons and performing heavy labor. Hands and feet are typically large, featuring thick fingers and toes that may have slight claws for added grip. The oni-ork exhibit a confident and assertive posture, often standing tall. Their movements can be powerful and deliberate, blending the brute strength with agility, allowing them to navigate terrain with both grace and force. Physically imposing, the hybrids are capable of displaying both fierce aggression and unexpected agility. Their physique allows them to excel in combat, leveraging their strength while also being capable of strategic maneuvering in battles.","coloring":"Oni-Ork skin may vary, showing a mix of earthy tones like greenish browns, reds, or shades of gray, reflecting their orc and oni heritage.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42/49 points","Titles: Monster, Oni-Ork","Feature:","[Skin: (color(s))] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Special Movement F [Speedburst] (7)","Fighting Style F [weapon type] (7)","1 tech (7 point discount)","Superstrength F (14)","Heightened Sense [Smell, Hearing] E (14)","Sixth Sense F [Manavision] (7)","Athletics F (7)","Religion F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (7)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42/49 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-oni-ork-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-oni-ork-2.webp"],"aliases":["Oni-Ork"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-skeleton","name":"Skeleton","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Every flesh and blood creature has one but nobody starts screaming until a skeleton starts moving about without its flesh. Skeletons are as visually distinct as the races they came from: horns, teeth, and the general shape of the skull all being notable differences. Depending on the enchantments sustaining the skeleton, it may have many unusual abilities–even if they weren’t present when the creature was alive. Skeletons larger than medium require more power to enchant, so it’s common for animated skeletons to be medium or smaller.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long","weight":"Any, divide given values in half Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg)","physique":"A skeleton consists of a framework of bones, including the skull, vertebrae, ribs, limbs, and pelvis. The structure is rigid yet allows for some mobility at the joints. Skeletons typically vary in height depending on the original species, but they generally stand at an average of 5 to 6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 meters) for humanoid skeletons, reflecting the average height of a human. Skeletons are primarily composed of calcium phosphate and collagen, giving them a durable but lightweight structure. They may be enchanted or magically animated, allowing them to move as if they were alive. The skull is often prominent, with hollow eye sockets, a jaw, and various indentations for muscle attachment. The features may vary in shape, reflecting the original being. If the creature had antlers or horns, those will be visible in whole or partial condition if they were broken/rotted. The ribs form a protective cage around the chest cavity, giving the skeleton a defined torso. Wing bones may be attached to the upper back. If the creature had a tail, there may be a tail of bone extending from the base of the spine. The long bones of the arms and legs are typically straight, with joints that allow for basic movements. Skeletal hands and feet may be claw-like or bony. Skeletons typically have an upright posture, but without muscles, their movements are often jerky or mechanical, particularly if animated by magic. In narrative contexts, they may exhibit a jarring, unsettling motion. While skeletons themselves are usually devoid of personality, animated skeletons might display behaviors reflective of their creators or the spells that animate them. They may act as guardians, soldiers, or servants, often obeying commands without hesitation.","coloring":"Natural Bone Color: Pale White or Off-White: Most commonly, animated skeletons appear as a pale white or off-white, resembling freshly bleached bones. This coloration suggests a lifeless, ghostly quality. Creamy Yellow or Tan: Over time, bones can take on a creamy or yellowish hue, especially if they have aged or been exposed to elements. Magical Infusion: Glowing or Ethereal Colors: Animated skeletons might exhibit an otherworldly glow, with colors like blue, green, or purple emanating from within. This glow can signify magical energy or a curse that animates the skeleton. Iridescent or Shimmering Effects: Some animated skeletons might have a shimmering quality, where colors shift and change depending on the angle of light, indicating enchantment. Decayed or Dull Appearance: Gray or Ashen: Skeletons that have been buried or are remnants of ancient beings may appear gray or ashen, reflecting decay and age. This gives them a more sinister, undead look. Darkened Spots or Stains: Dull or dark spots may be present, indicating areas of decay, blood, or other organic materials that have stained the bones over time. Rust or Corrosion: If the skeleton is created from the remains of a body that was once heavily armored or adorned, there might be traces of rust or corrosion from metal, giving a mixed color of brown or reddish tones in certain areas. Variations by Culture: Depending on the origin of the skeleton—such as a necromancer's creation or a guardian of sacred grounds—the coloration might reflect cultural elements, like painted symbols or markings that serve a ritualistic purpose.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 98 points","Titles: Monster, Undead, Skeleton","Feature:","[Antlers] - optional - Paired branched horns that grow from the creature’s skull and are periodically shed.","[Horns] - optional - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Wings] - optional - Paired appendages capable of flight. Requires Flight skill to actually fly. Skeletal wings do not offer flight without magical assistance.","[Tail] - optional - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Speed E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Fighting Style F [weapon type] (7)","Resilient [Fatigue - doesn’t need food, water, sleep; Suffocation] E (14)","Consider also: Charmed, Disease, Fear, Paralysis, Poison, Sleep, Stun","Resistance F [Piercing] (7)","Intimidation F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"98 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-skeleton-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-skeleton-2.webp"],"aliases":["Skeleton","Undead"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-thrall","name":"Thrall","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"A newborn vampire at the bottom of their blood-soaked society. Their hunger inspires urgency and desperation when it strikes, preventing thralls from exercising much restraint. Ultimately, thralls are fodder for their superiors. If they cease to be useful, thralls are turned into ghouls to ravage an area until they perish.","lifespan":"200 years","height":"Male: 6’ to 6.5’ (1.83–1.98 m) Female: 5.5’ to 6’ (1.68–1.83 m)","weight":"Male: 160–220 lbs (73–100 kg) Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Common vampires typically have a lean and well-defined muscular build, reflecting their agility and supernatural speed. They often appear fit and agile, with an emphasis on grace rather than overwhelming bulk. Their tall stature often adds to their imposing presence. They typically have sharp, angular features with high cheekbones and defined jaws. Prominent fangs are a hallmark of vampires, extending from the canines to facilitate blood-feeding. These fangs can retract, allowing for normal speech and expression when not in use. Hair can vary widely, but it's commonly dark, sleek, and often styled dramatically. Some vampires might have flowing locks that add to their allure and mystique. Vampires are known for their graceful, fluid movements. They often exhibit a confident posture, exuding an air of sophistication and charisma. Their agility allows them to navigate their environments swiftly and silently. Physically, vampires often exude charisma and charm, using their appearance to seduce or intimidate others. Their predatory instincts can add an air of danger to their interactions, making them both alluring and threatening.","coloring":"Vampires often have pale skin, which can appear almost translucent or luminescent. This pallor enhances their ethereal, otherworldly appearance. Their eyes are often striking, sometimes appearing red, gold, or other unnatural colors, emphasizing their predatory nature.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder vampires","Hostile towards all trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 140 points","Evolves into: Dhampir","Titles: Monster, Undead, Vampire","Feature:","[Fangs] - Elongated canine teeth used to puncture flesh and draw blood.","[Blood Drinker] (7) - Creature derives nutrition from drinking the blood of other creatures.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Fighting Style F [weapon type] (7)","1 tech (7 point discount)","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell] (14)","Sixth Sense F [Danger] (7)","Regeneration F (7)","Resilient E [Fatigue - doesn’t need food, water, sleep; Suffocation] (14)","Resistance F [Slashing] (7)","Deception F (7)","Equipment: Natural Weapons F (14)","Choose one Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements."],"evolvesInto":"Dhampir","totalCost":"140 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-thrall-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-thrall-2.webp"],"aliases":["Thrall","Undead","Vampire"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-wendigo","name":"Wendigo","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"Wendigos are the manifestation of corrupted mana that is left behind in the wake of savage cannibalism or freezing to death. An unnatural chill is commonly reported in areas where a wendigo was sighted. It’s important to dispatch wendigo quickly before they feed on much, as they become increasingly bestial and develop more resistances. Due to their climate, the Republic and the Kingdom of Rotia have the most wendigo sightings, but it’s not entirely unheard of for them to manifest elsewhere.","lifespan":"200 years","height":"10’ to 15’ (3–4.5 m)","weight":"317–544 lbs (143–246 kg)","physique":"Wendigos typically range from 10 to 15 feet (3 to 4.5 meters) in height, making them towering and intimidating creatures. They appear to be extremely thin and skeletal, with their ribcage visible and skin stretched tightly over their bones. Their arms and legs are usually long and lanky, which contributes to their eerie and unnatural movement. Wendigos often have gaunt, elongated faces with pronounced cheekbones, which create a haunting, malnourished look. They typically have jagged, sharp teeth, emphasizing their predatory nature, built for ripping flesh. Wendigos move quietly and with agility, despite their size. Their movements can be described as both fluid and unsettling, reflecting their predatory instincts.","coloring":"The skin of a Wendigo is typically pale, gray, or even frostbitten, resembling that of a corpse. Occasionally, the skin may have a mottled look or appear decayed. Their eyes possess a dull glow, which adds to their supernatural presence and serves to intimidate prey. The eye color can vary, often appearing as a bright or unnatural hue.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile towards all trees"],"requirements":[],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-wendigo-1.webp","assets/races/monster-mundane-wendigo-2.webp"],"aliases":["Wendigo"]},{"id":"monster-mundane-woodland-demon","name":"Woodland Demon","tree":"Monster","stage":"Mundane","description":"First encountered in the former Light County, these malevolent entities came from the forest. Even as low-level minions, these creatures were quite sturdy, outfitted with natural weapons and armor.","lifespan":"","height":"","weight":"","physique":"","coloring":"","historicalFigures":[],"relations":[],"requirements":["Total Cost: 105 points","Titles: Monster, Woodland Demon","Feature:","[Tree Body] - Your body has the appearance and characteristics of a tree.","[Forest Camo] F (14) - Undetected [Sight] - Remaining still against forest scenery prevents detection by visual inspection.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Resistance E [Bludgeoning, Piercing] (14)","Magic E (14)","Affinity: Flora F (7)","Items:","Natural Armor F (14)","Natural Weapons F (14)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"105 points","images":["assets/races/monster-mundane-woodland-demon-1.webp"],"aliases":["Woodland Demon"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-devil-oni","name":"Devil/Oni","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Devils are the sophisticated side of the underworld. These evil creatures, typically more humanoid in shape and size, still have their sense and will use it to deadly effect in order to force their will on the world. Just as likely to slink in the shadows under some alternate identity as they are to boldly storm the city gates, devils can do it all–or so they would claim. Their natural proclivity to magic doesn’t hurt either.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Fe/Male: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long","weight":"Fe/Male: 61–499 lbs (27–226 kg)","physique":"Devils do not possess many obvious features that would give away their monstrous heritage. Any oddities they do have are easily passed off as a trait of the accepted race trees (Prime, Beast, Fae, Construct). More powerful devils may possess a clearly unnatural form, but they have mastered magics to maintain a normal form when in public.","coloring":"Devil eyes are usually the first sign of their monstrous nature. Sigils or flames can be seen burning from within their retina when they aren’t cloaked.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Imp","Titles: Monster, Devil/Oni","Feature:","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Eyes: Brand] - Eye possesses a mark or distinct fiery appearance that reveals devilish lineage.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Wings] - optional - paired appendages capable of flight.","Stats:","Strength - E","Precision - D","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Speed - C","Skills:","Special Movement F [Fancy Falling]","Magic C","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell]","Sixth Sense F [Danger or Manavision]","Alternate Identity F","Climbing F","Deception F","Sleight of Hand F","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-devil-oni-1.webp","assets/races/monster-intermediate-devil-oni-2.webp"],"aliases":["Devil","Devil/Oni","Oni"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-fiend-oni","name":"Fiend/Oni","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Fiends are wild creatures ascended from the bowels of the underworld. Usually manifesting as ideas given form, fiends embody things such as the seven deadly sins or more abstract concepts like malevolence, malignancy, decay, and destruction. Intellect varies wildly but most run on bestial instinct. Magic does not come naturally to them, but it can be granted if they find favor with a powerful demonlord.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 6’ to 10’ (1.8–3 m) Female: 5’ to 9’ (1.5–2.7 m)","weight":"Male: 200–600 lbs (91–272 kg) Female: 150–500 lbs (68–227 kg)","physique":"Fiends can range in size from medium to large, typically standing between 5 to 10 feet (1.5 to 3 meters) tall. Many fiends are depicted with strong, muscular builds that emphasize their physical strength and combat prowess. They often have striking features, including glowing eyes or unusual shapes, enhancing their menacing appearance. Many fiends possess horns, claws, tails, or other distinctive appendages that reflect their supernatural origins. Fiends typically have powerful arms and legs, designed for combat and agility. Clawed hands and feet are common features, aiding in both attack and defense. Some fiends may have long, flexible tails that can be used as weapons or for balance. Many fiends have natural armor, such as tough scales or a hardened hide, providing them with added protection in battle. Fiends often embody traits such as cunning, aggression, and a sense of superiority, which can influence their posture and movements. They may exude an aura of intimidation.","coloring":"Their physique often reflects their role as formidable adversaries. Fiends have skin that is tough and comes in various colors, including red, black, green, or even metallic tones, depending on their type.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Imp","Titles: Monster, Fiend/Oni","Feature:","[Horns] - Paired permanent extensions of the creature’s skull that are often curved and pointed.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","Stats:","Strength - B","Precision - D","Intelligence - D","Vitality - E","Speed - D","Skills:","Jumping E","Special Movement F [Fancy Falling]","Fighting Style C [weapon type]","4 unique techs","Superstrength D","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell]","Sixth Sense F [Danger or Manavision]","Resistance [Mundane] E","Climbing F","Intimidation F","Sleight","Survival F","Equipment: Natural Weapons D","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-fiend-oni-1.webp","assets/races/monster-intermediate-fiend-oni-2.webp"],"aliases":["Fiend","Fiend/Oni","Oni"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-hobgoblin","name":"Hobgoblin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Despite typically being associated with goblinoids, they are closer to humans in capabilities despite their ugly appearance and innately dark hearts.","lifespan":"75 years","height":"Male: 5.5’ to 6’ (1.68–1.83 m) Female: 5’ to 5.5’ (1.52–1.68 m)","weight":"Male: 150–200 lbs (68–91 kg) Female: 100–150 lbs (45–68 kg)","physique":"Hobgoblins are typically depicted with a stocky, muscular build. They are more robust than regular goblins, reflecting their training and military lifestyle. Hobgoblins usually stand between 5 to 6 feet tall (1.52 to 1.83 meters), making them taller than average goblins but still shorter than many other humanoid races. Hobgoblins have distinctive facial features, including a broad forehead, prominent brow, and pointed ears. Their noses are often somewhat flat or broad. They have long limbs that provide agility and strength, aiding them in combat. Their hands and feet are usually larger, capable of wielding weapons effectively. Hobgoblins have a confident and aggressive posture, often embodying the traits of disciplined soldiers. Their movements are usually quick and purposeful, reflecting their training and martial discipline. They often wear medium to heavy armor, which enhances their sturdy appearance. Their armor is typically practical and functional, reflecting their military background, adorned with symbols of their clan or status.","coloring":"Their skin tones can vary, commonly ranging from shades of green to brown or gray, and on occasion red. This helps them blend into their environments, especially in rugged terrain. They typically have sharp, piercing eyes that can be unsettling, often displaying colors like yellow or red, contributing to their menacing appearance.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Goblin","Titles: Monster, Hobgoblin","Feature:","[Skin: (color(s))] - Skin comes in certain nonstandard colors.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","Stats:","Strength - B","Precision - D","Intelligence - D","Speed - D","Skills:","Fast F","Fighting Style C [weapon type]","4 unique techs (7 point discount each)","Heightened Sense E [Smell, Hearing]","Undetected [Sound]","Acrobatics F","Climbing F","Stealth F","Equipment: Natural Weapons F","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-hobgoblin-1.webp","assets/races/monster-intermediate-hobgoblin-2.webp"],"aliases":["Hobgoblin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-airkin","name":"Airkin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"N/A","weight":"N/A","physique":"Airkin are composed of air and wind, making them insubstantial and intangible. They can move and shift freely, often appearing as swirling winds, breezes, or clouds. While they lack a solid form, airkin can sometimes manifest in shapes that are more recognizable, such as whirlwinds, spirals of air, or faint humanoid figures. These shapes might be more of an impression than a solid body. Airkin are highly mobile and can fly at great speeds. They can traverse the battlefield with ease, often evading attacks due to their elusive nature. Although they lack a physical body, airkin can interact with the environment to some extent. They might create gusts of wind, whirlwinds, or storms, influencing their surroundings without a traditional physical form. Because of their insubstantiality, airkin are often resistant or immune to non-magical attacks, making them challenging opponents to engage in physical combat.","coloring":"Translucent unless it kicks up debris (largely dust), liquid, or smoke which typically spread throughout the elemental’s form revealing it.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Airkin","Features:","[Air Camo] F (14) - Undetected [Sight] - Creature is invisible while motionless. Can still be heard. If above loose dirt, debris, liquid, or smoke, this feature fails.","[Hover] - Character floats a few feet above solid ground. This replaces walking. Character cannot fly. Does not prevent fall damage.","Stats:","Precision - C","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Speed - C","Skills:","Flight F","Affinity [Air] D","Magic C","Componentless Casting D","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Change State F(E)","Limiter: Permanent","Resistance [physical] D","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-airkin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Airkin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-earthkin","name":"Earthkin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"8’ to 12’ (2.4–3.7 m)","weight":"1,000–4,000 lbs (450–1814 kg)","physique":"Earthkin are solid, durable beings made of rock, clay, soil, or other earthy materials. Their form is often reminiscent of statues, golems, or large figures made from the natural elements of the earth. Their appearance can vary widely, but they often have a rugged, uneven surface, with features resembling stones or boulders. Some might display characteristics like moss, crystals, or minerals embedded in their bodies. They are generally large, towering creatures, often much taller and bulkier than a human. Their size enhances their imposing presence and strength in combat. While earthkin are solid, they are capable of moving with surprising agility for their size. They can traverse rocky terrain easily and may even meld into the ground or manipulate earth as part of their actions. Earthkin are adept at close combat, using their physical presence to crush or batter foes. They may also possess abilities to manipulate earth and stone, using their environment to their advantage.","coloring":"Earthkin can be composed of different types of earth materials, such as mud, rock, or granite, which can influence their durability and abilities. For instance, a muddy source kin may appear more fluid in movement compared to one made of solid stone.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Earthkin","Features:","Large size","Height: 8 to 16 feet tall/long","Weight: 500 to 4000 pounds (2 tons)","Strength:","Character can lift and carry 5x more weight. Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","Plus 1 strength effectiveness to non-attack actions","Base throw distance doubled - 60ft base distance (accurate throw*) (object that fits in hand)","Vitality: Mundane damage received is reduced by 1","Speed: Minus 1 speed effectiveness","Movement: Base movement doubled - 40ft base movement","Narrative: \"Big\", \"Heavy\", \"Obvious\" - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudication outcomes for this character","[Earth Camo] F (14) - Undetected [Sight] - Remaining still against earthen scenery prevents detection by visual inspection.","Stats:","Strength - C","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Skills:","Special Movement F [Earth Walk]","Superstrength D","Affinity D [Earth]","Magic C","Componentless Casting D or Natural Catalyst D","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Resistance [Physical] D","Equipment:","Natural Armor D","Natural Weapons D","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-earthkin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Earthkin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-firekin","name":"Firekin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"N/A","weight":"N/A","physique":"Firekin are primarily composed of flame and heat. Their physical form often resembles a swirling mass of fire or a humanoid figure made entirely of flame. Their shapes can be fluid and shifting, similar to a flame dancing in the wind. Some may resemble a humanoid figure or a large flame, with features that are vaguely recognizable but always composed of fire. While firekin have a physical appearance, they may also possess an intangible quality. The flames may flicker, and they can move or dissipate easily, giving them an elusive nature. Firekin can vary in size but are often large creatures, capable of towering over normal beings. They may take on different dimensions based on the amount of fire they embody. They are incredibly mobile and can move through the air or ground with the elegance of fire spreading. Their speed and ability to phase through things enhance their combat effectiveness. Firekin often have the ability to create flames, project fireballs, or engulf foes in flames. Their physical form allows them to deal fire damage upon contact, adding to their danger.","coloring":"They exude a brilliant glow, with colors ranging from deep oranges and reds to bright yellows.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Firekin","Feature:","[Aura: Fire] D (21) - Affinity [Aura] - An ever-present heat surrounds you, damaging all that get close.","[Bright] (7) - Creature’s body sheds bright light in all directions.","Stats:","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Skills:","Special Movement F [Fire Walk]","[Fire Walk] - Creature can move along the top of lava and fire without harm.","Affinity D [Fire]","Magic C","Componentless Casting C or Natural Catalyst C","Sixth Sense F [Cold]","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Change State F(E)","Limiter: Permanent","Resistance D [Fire]","Resilient [heat] F","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-firekin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Firekin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-icekin","name":"Icekin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"6’ to 12’ (1.8 to 3.7 m)","weight":"800–2,000 lbs (364–907 kg)","physique":"Icekin typically range from 6 to 12 feet (1.8 to 3.7 meters) in height, but their size can vary. They generally have a solid, angular build, resembling crystalline structures or frosty figures. Their forms can appear jagged, reflecting the nature of ice. Their surfaces may resemble frozen water or crystal, giving them a stunning and formidable presence. Their features can be both humanoid and abstract, with aspects that mimic sharp ice formations or icy fog. Their mouths can appear as cracks or fissures that emit cold air, further enhancing their chilling aura. Icekin move by gliding or moving fluidly, as if sliding over surfaces of ice. This gives them an elegant yet eerie presence, allowing them to traverse battlefields quickly. Their bodies can be covered in frost or snow, and they might create a trail of ice or frost wherever they move. This adds to their elemental theme and emphasizes their connection to cold and winter.","coloring":"Icekin usually have a translucent or bluish hue, often shimmering as light interacts with their icy bodies. If they possess facial features, they may have hollow sockets for eyes that glow with a cold blue light.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Icekin","Feature: [Aura: Cold] D (21) - Affinity: Aura - An ever-present chill surrounds you, damaging all that touch you.","Stats:","Strength - C","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Skills:","Special Movement F [Ice Walk]","[Ice Walk] - Character is able to move across ice normally.","Magic C","Affinity: Aura D","Affinity D [Ice]","Componentless Casting D or Natural Catalyst D","Control Environment F","Sixth Sense F [Heat]","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Resistance E [Physical]","Resilient F [Cold]","Ability: Frost Walk [Affinity F (Ice); Special Movement F (Ice Walk)] - Character is able to produce ice at its feet to walk or glide over surfaces.","Items:","Natural Armor D","Natural Weapons D","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-icekin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Icekin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-shadowkin","name":"Shadowkin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"5’ to 10’ (1.5–3 m)","weight":"N/A","physique":"Shadowkin typically range from 5 to 10 feet (1.5 to 3 meters) in height, though they may shift in size and shape depending on their environment and intentions. They are often depicted as having an undefined or amorphous shape, making them appear fluid and ever-changing. Their form may seem to blend into the surrounding shadows, making it difficult to perceive their true dimensions. When given form, they can appear somewhat skeletal or with elongated limbs, enhancing their spectral and haunting attributes. Shadowkin are usually represented as dark silhouettes or pure darkness. Their bodies may lack solid features, resembling wisps of smoke or shadow that flicker and swirl. They move with grace and stealth, often gliding silently through the air. Their ability to flow through shadows makes them adept at evading detection and surprising foes. Shadowkin have powers related to darkness, such as the ability to create areas of darkness, manipulate shadows, or even merge with them to become invisible. These abilities enhance their unpredictable and formidable nature.","coloring":"Shadowkin may have glowing eyes or faint outlines that provide a contrast against the darkness, creating an ominous presence. Their \"skin\" can appear as swirling darkness or shifting shadows, devoid of physical substance. This can make them seem intangible, allowing them to pass through solid objects or disappear into darkness.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Shadowkin","Feature:","[Shadow Camo] F (14) - Undetected [Sight] - Creature is invisible while motionless in shadow. Can still be heard.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","[Hover] - Character floats a few feet above solid ground. This replaces walking. Character cannot fly. Does not prevent fall damage.","Stats:","Precision - C","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Speed - C","Skills:","Special Movement [Shadow Walk]","[Shadow Walk] - creature has the ability to meld into and move through shadow.","Teleport D","Affinity D [Darkness]","Magic C","Componentless Casting D","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Change State F(E)","Limiter: Permanent","Resistance [physical] D","Intermediate Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on the narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-shadowkin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Shadowkin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-waterkin","name":"Waterkin","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed","height":"5’ to 10’ (1.5–3.0 m)","weight":"500–1,500 lbs (227–680 kg)","physique":"Waterkin typically range from 5 to 10 feet (1.5 to 3 meters), but their form can shift significantly depending on their surroundings and the amount of water they contain. Waterkin lack a fixed form, often appearing as swirling masses of water or fluid shapes. They can stretch, compress, and flow seamlessly, embodying the adaptability of water. When resembling a humanoid figure, they may have smooth, flowing bodies that seem to ripple and change, mimicking the movement of water. Waterkin may have features like waves or streams flowing down their bodies, and they can appear to be constantly in motion. These elementals move fluidly, often gliding or flowing rather than walking. They can merge with bodies of water, dive into liquid, or create waves as they move. Their agility allows them to change shape quickly, making them able to avoid attacks or traverse terrain effortlessly. Waterkin have powers related to water manipulation, such as creating tidal waves, forming rain, or enveloping enemies in water. They can also regenerate using the water available in their surroundings.","coloring":"Waterkin are semi-transparent, with hues ranging from deep blue to crystal clear. This can give them a mesmerizing, almost ethereal look that reflects light beautifully. The \"skin\" of a waterkin resembles that of water, appearing smooth and reflective. The surface may shimmer as if catching light, and their bodies can appear to ripple like water in a breeze.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Monster, Waterkin","Features: [Water Camo] F (14) - Undetected [Sight] - While fully submerged in water, character can become undetectable by visual checks.","Stats:","Intelligence - B","Vitality - C","Speed - C","Skills:","Swim Speed D","Affinity C [Water]","Magic C","Componentless Casting D","Sixth Sense F [Manavision]","Supersense C [Hydrodynamics]","[Hydrodynamics] - Creature can detect and interpret disturbances in water caused by other moving objects or currents.","Change State F(E)","Limiter: Permanent","Regeneration D","Resistance D [Water]","Resilient E [Underwater; Suffocation]","Elasticity D"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-waterkin-1.webp"],"aliases":["Waterkin"]},{"id":"monster-intermediate-wyvern","name":"Wyvern","tree":"Monster","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Wyverns are formidable creatures with strong wings and elementally charged breath. Often used as mounts or guards for large or important locations. They are at home in wide open spaces with plenty of room to fly around.","lifespan":"200 years","height":"Male: 10’ to 15’ (3–4.6 m) Female: 8’ to 12’ (2.4–3.7 m)","weight":"Male: 300–600 lbs (136–272 kg) Female: 250–500 lbs (113–227 kg)","physique":"Wyverns typically measure between 10 to 15 feet (3 to 4.6 meters) from snout to tail. Their wingspan can be quite extensive, often reaching 20 to 30 feet (6 to 9 meters), allowing for powerful flight. Wyverns have a lean, muscular build that emphasizes agility and speed. Their bodies are designed for flight, with strong muscles supporting their wings. They have a narrow, elongated head with sharp teeth and a pronounced jaw, as well as often having horns or crests. Wyverns have two powerful forelimbs that double as wings. The structure of these limbs is adapted for both flying and grasping prey. Their hind limbs are strong and often end in sharp claws, aiding in hunting and climbing. Wyverns possess long, flexible tails that can be used for balance during flight and as a weapon in combat. Wyverns are aerial hunters, using their speed and agility to catch prey. Their physique supports this predatory lifestyle.","coloring":"Wyverns are covered in tough, protective scales that can vary in color, often seen in shades of green, brown, or metallic hues.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Hostile to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves From: Drake","Titles: Monster, Drake, Wyvern","Feature:","Large size (above 8 feet/500 lbs)","Height: 8 to 16 feet tall/long","Weight: 500 to 4000 pounds (2 tons)","Strength:","Character can lift and carry 5x more weight. Stacks with [Super Strength] skill.","Plus 1 strength effectiveness to non-attack actions","Base throw distance doubled - 60ft base distance (accurate throw*) (object that fits in hand)","Vitality: Mundane damage received is reduced by 1","Speed: Minus 1 speed effectiveness","Movement: Base movement doubled - 40ft base movement","Narrative: \"Big\", \"Heavy\", \"Obvious\" - things narrator should keep in mind when adjudication outcomes for this character","[Quadruped] - Creature has four legs.","[Scales] - Skin is totally covered in reptilian scales.","[Wings] - paired appendages capable of flight.","[Spines] - Any hard, pointed defensive projection or structure.","[Ears: Reptilian] - A thin membrane located at the rear of the head.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Breath Weapon (Type)] - The ability to exhale or project an elementally charged breath or discharge from the mouth. Element must be selected upon acquisition.","[Darkvision] F - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - B","Precision - B","Intelligence - C","Speed - C","Vitality - C","Skills:","Fast E","Flight E","Fighting Style C [Natural Weapon]","Tech: Range F","Tech: Area F","Superstrength C","Magic D","Heightened Sense D [Smell]","Resistance D [element]","Climbing F","Intimidation D","Stealth E","Items: Natural Weapons C","Perks:","Perk 1: [Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Perk 2: Choose 1:","[Menace] - an aura of fear emanates from the creature at all times that makes lower grade creatures take a -1 effectiveness on attacks against monster or monster allies.","[Rank and File Asset F] - All monsters below the grade of this character are compelled to follow their orders. Alternate to Leadership but only applies to npc monsters. This grants a handful of followers as a narrative asset during rp (they do NOT count as minions and number, usefulness, and presence ultimately depends on narrator)."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/monster-intermediate-wyvern-1.webp","assets/races/monster-intermediate-wyvern-2.webp"],"aliases":["Drake","Wyvern"]},{"id":"construct-mundane-golem","name":"Golem","tree":"Construct","stage":"Mundane","description":"Typically inorganic constructs with humanoid bodies that vary in material, size, purpose, and place of origin. Despite their physical differences, all golems possess a common innate desire to serve their creator. Currently, the densest golem populations are found in places like the Otenzian Empire (East) and Widersia, both of which have established histories of construct innovation. Rumor has it that golems were first created by infusing living souls into inorganic bodies.","lifespan":"Non-sentient constructs persist as long as maintenance is performed. Sentient constructs last up to 120 years","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2.43–4.87 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4.87 m) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg) Large: 500 to 4000 lbs (2 tons)(226.79–1.81 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1.81 mt)","physique":"Golems are humanoid in the vaguest sense. Their bipedal frames are bulky and cumbersome. Generally stocky and muscular, designed for strength and durability rather than agility. Clay Golems typically have a smooth, earthy appearance, often resembling humanoid shapes. They might be slightly flexible but can harden over time. Stone Golems usually have a rugged, solid physique, resembling large, muscular humanoids made from various types of stone (granite, marble, etc.). Metal Golems are often sleek and shiny, made from various metals. They can appear more mechanical and may have articulated joints.","coloring":"Golems take earthy tones from the materials they are made from. Their eyes and various parts of their bodies might glow as a result of the magic core powering them. The core is typically blue but can manifest other colors.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 35 points","Evolves into: Guardian Golem","Titles: Construct, Golem","Features:","Stats: Strength or Vitality E (7)","Skills:","Resilient E [Fatigue (caused by Hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Aging] (14)","Equipment:","Natural Weapons F (14) or Natural Armor F (Heavy or Light)(14)"],"evolvesInto":"Guardian Golem","totalCost":"35 points","images":["assets/races/construct-mundane-golem-1.webp","assets/races/construct-mundane-golem-2.webp"],"aliases":["Golem"]},{"id":"construct-mundane-fabriken","name":"Fabriken","tree":"Construct","stage":"Mundane","description":"First discovered in the northwestern desert of the Ororoot Empire (West), the Fabriken people are a race of \"animated\" cloth. Unlike living dolls and living armor, the animation of the cloth is false. The true body of a fabriken is a magical particulate, not unlike soot in appearance, that must inhabit a shell or membrane of some kind in order for it to take a functional form. Being that the inhabitable objects and materials vary so much, fabrikens can take many different forms from humanoids to spindly legged forms akin to crustaceans.","lifespan":"Non-sentient constructs persist as long as maintenance is performed. Sentient constructs last up to 120 years","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2.43–4.87 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4.87 m) tall/long","weight":"Any, divide given values in half Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg) Large: 500 to 4000 lbs (2 tons)(226.79–1.81 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1.81 mt)","physique":"The Fabriken, when at rest, appear as shapeless mounds or clouds of soot, often shifting in color from deep black to dark gray while shimmering slightly due to their magical nature. In this form, they are only capable of slinking along the ground like a caterpillar. Their texture has a soft, airy quality, resembling clumps of bubbles or foam. The Fabriken can extend thin, wispy tendrils that can sense their environment but lack significant strength. These tendrils are used for manipulation of small objects or interacting with their surroundings. The tendrils can dissolve and reform quickly, allowing the Fabriken to adapt to various situations by extending or retracting as needed. Fabriken utilize various materials for their shells—these could include natural items like leaves, shells, or crystals; crafted items like clothing, armor, or bowls; or even more complex constructs. Each Fabriken can customize its shell, which influences its personal aesthetic and functions. For instance, a bowl may allow for easy movement while clothing offers more dexterity. Fabriken can alter their shape more dramatically when occupying a shell, taking on various forms (e.g., animals, humanoids) for a limited time based on their environment or need.","coloring":"The particulate comprising fabriken shifts from deep black to dark gray while also shimmering slightly under lighting. Regardless of what form a fabriken is in, they always manifest two yellow eyes that can vary in size. Some speculate these might be related to the fabriken’s core.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 112+ points","Titles: Construct, Fabriken","Feature: [Amorphous] (7) - Your body has no set form.","Stats:","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Sixth Sense F [Manavision] (7)","Supersense F [Tremorsense] (7)","Regeneration F (7)","Resilient E [Fatigue - doesn’t need food, water, sleep; Suffocation] (14)","Change State F (21)","Elasticity F (14)","2 Secondary skills","Choose 1 Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Self Made - Constructs may perform creation and upgrade of natural equipment for constructs when using appropriate Masterwork Maker skills."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"112+ points","images":["assets/races/construct-mundane-fabriken-1.webp","assets/races/construct-mundane-fabriken-2.webp"],"aliases":["Fabriken"]},{"id":"construct-mundane-living-doll","name":"Living Doll","tree":"Construct","stage":"Mundane","description":"Living dolls are animated by a mana core similar to normal constructs, but, unlike normal constructs, the core in these dolls forms spontaneously. Also unlike normal constructs is the living doll’s inability to be controlled through typical commands. There are rumors of a being that pities the dolls and imbues this false life upon them.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg)","physique":"Living dolls are often crafted from a variety of materials, such as porcelain, wood, fabric, or even magical constructs. Their bodies may resemble traditional dolls with stiff joints. A porcelain doll might have a smooth, glossy finish, while a cloth doll could have a soft, textured surface. The materials chosen can affect both their aesthetic and how they interact with the environment. Living dolls frequently have large, expressive eyes that can appear glassy or painted. These eyes may convey emotions or have a supernatural glow. Their mouths are often small and stylized, sometimes capable of movement to express emotions or speak, depending on the magical or mechanical nature of the doll. Living dolls generally have jointed limbs that allow for movement, though their range may be limited compared to more complex beings. They might have a charmingly stiff or exaggerated quality to their movements. Their hands can vary from simple paws to delicate, articulated fingers, allowing them to grasp or manipulate objects with a doll-like grip. Living dolls may have a variety of hairstyles and materials for hair, including wigs made from various fibers or real hair. Hairstyles can range from elaborate and styled to simple and tidy. While primarily static or limited in movement, many living dolls may possess the ability to move, often in a jerky or exaggerated manner, which can add to their otherworldly charm. Occasionally, living dolls–particularly those from Widersia–can animate gracefully, exhibiting a range of movements that can evoke emotions or tell stories.","coloring":"Living dolls have an appearance that can be uncannily close to humans. Closer inspection reveals them to be constructs. Some may have softly glowing eyes, commonly in blue the color of mana. They are often adorned in unique, ornate clothing reminiscent of the time period or aesthetic they represent, which adds to their character. This clothing can be intricate, with layers, lace, and other decorative elements.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 70+ points","Evolves into: Possessed Doll","Titles: Construct, Living Doll","Feature:","[Form: (material type)] - Body is made of inorganics.","[Separable] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows major appendages and head to harmlessly separate from the torso and reattach.","[Replaceable Parts] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows them to swap their parts at will.","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Resilient [Fatigue (caused by hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Suffocation] E (14)","Choose 3:","Acrobatics F (7)","Culture F (7)","Domestic Arts F (7)","Etiquette F (7)","Gaming F (7)","History F (7)","Law F (7)","Medicine F (7)","Nature F (7)","Navigation F (7)","Performance F [type] (7)","Visual Arts F (7)","Choose 1 Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Self Made - Constructs may perform creation and upgrade of natural equipment for constructs when using appropriate Masterwork Maker skills."],"evolvesInto":"Possessed Doll","totalCost":"70+ points","images":["assets/races/construct-mundane-living-doll-1.webp","assets/races/construct-mundane-living-doll-2.webp"],"aliases":["Living Doll"]},{"id":"construct-mundane-pawn","name":"Pawn","tree":"Construct","stage":"Mundane","description":"Pawns are part of a larger community of constructs known collectively as Rooks, with pawns being one of the mundane iterations. Pawns are humanoid bipeds that commonly resemble lightly armored foot soldiers. Internally, they have metal plating layered over a part mechanical, part magical \"nervous system\". Pawns were created and modified to accomplish various tasks, but their main function was to serve as guardians and war machines for the ancient civilization of the Talbot. Talbots mostly lived in and around present-day Widersia, but smaller populations migrated across the southern half of the continent. Some Rooks have been found in Talbot ruins or buried under old battlefields.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"6’ to 8’ (1.8–2.4 m)","weight":"400–800 lbs (180–360 kg)","physique":"Pawns have a variety of designs resembling lightly armored foot soldiers, often incorporating intricate engravings or glowing runes that reflect their individual functions or lineage. Their bodies are generally leaner in design for agility. Their joints function similarly to those of organic beings. The internal structure combines metal wiring and magical energy conduits, giving them an ability to react and move with surprising agility. The \"heart\" or \"core\" functions as both a power source and a central processing unit, imbued with magical energy. Pawns can be periodically updated or modified with new magical enhancements or mechanical parts, allowing them to adapt to new challenges. Pawns may have the ability to self-repair minor damage using available materials or magical energy, giving them resilience in long battles. Skilled Pawns could be adept at crafting or enhancing equipment, whether it be their own or for others.","coloring":"Their plating can come in different colors or finishes (e.g., polished silver, darkened bronze, or glowing blue) based on their specific roles or the magical resources used in their creation.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 84+ points","Titles: Construct, Pawn","Features:","[Thaumaturgic Neural Network] F (7) - Mindshield - brain made with magical and mechanical components","Lacks sense of smell, taste","[Visual Sensors] - 1 to 8 Visual sensors (eyes) with light interface for visual code communication","Stats:","Strength or Precision E (7)","Intelligence E (7)","Vitality D (14)","Skills:","Appraisal F (7, free for isekai)","Fighting Style F or Magic F (7)","Resilient [Fatigue - doesn’t need food, water, sleep; Suffocation] E (14)","Athletics F (7) or Acrobatics F (7)","2 Secondary skills","Items: Natural Armor F (light/heavy) (14)","Choose 1 Perk:","Born For This - get 7pt discount on a skill you chose for your Mundane requirements.","Self Made - Constructs may perform creation and upgrade of natural equipment for constructs when using appropriate Masterwork Maker skills."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"84+ points","images":["assets/races/construct-mundane-pawn-1.webp","assets/races/construct-mundane-pawn-2.webp"],"aliases":["Pawn"]},{"id":"construct-intermediate-guardian-golem","name":"Guardian Golem","tree":"Construct","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Guardian golems are more common in dungeons outside of Ryke. They can take many shapes but are commonly humanoid. Those found in dungeons bear an appearance that is a product of ancient cultures. The Otenzian Empire (East) has manufactured guardian golems for various locations within their domain. These golems reflect the Empire’s culture.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"8’ to 12’ (2.4–3.7 m)","weight":"1,000–2,500 lbs (450–1,130 kg)","physique":"Mid-tier golems have a solid and durable physique, often resembling heightened humanoid forms or more massive constructs. Their frames are thick and bulky, designed for strength and resilience. They may be crafted from various materials, including: Stone: Giving them a sturdy, rugged appearance, with visible textures and jagged edges. Clay: Offering a smoother surface, often with the ability to reshape or contour slightly. Metal: Constructed from iron or bronze, lending a polished or heavily armored look. Golems typically possess large, powerful limbs, allowing for heavy lifting and powerful strikes. Their arms and legs may be blocky or humanoid in shape, equipped for combat or labor. While not as agile as smaller constructs, mid-tier golems can still move with surprising grace for their size, often able to cover ground quickly when necessary. Mid-tier golems usually lack detailed facial features. Instead, they might have a simplistic visage, such as eye slots or a carved face, displaying an imposing or stoic expression. Internally, a mid-tier golem contains a magical core or heart that powers its movements and functions. This core could glow with a soft light, reflecting the type of magic sustaining it. Although not truly organic, they could have a network of magical conduits resembling a nervous system, allowing them to respond to commands or stimuli.","coloring":"Some versions may feature glowing runes or eyes, indicating their magical essence or serving as indicators of their functional state.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Golem","Titles: Construct, Golem, Guardian Golem","Features:","Large size","[360° Vision] - ability to see in all directions simultaneously, preventing surprise while active.","Stats:","Strength - C","Intelligence - C","Vitality - B","Skills:","Fighting Style D or Magic D","Superstrength D","Duration Reduction D","Resilient C [Fatigue (caused by Hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Aging; Fear; Prone]","Resistance D [Physical]","Nullify E [Type]","Equipment:","Natural Weapons D","Natural Armor D (Heavy or Light)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/construct-intermediate-guardian-golem-1.webp","assets/races/construct-intermediate-guardian-golem-2.webp"],"aliases":["Golem","Guardian Golem"]},{"id":"construct-intermediate-possessed-doll","name":"Possessed Doll","tree":"Construct","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Living dolls eventually become “possessed” when the soul inside begins to more intimately merge with the synthetic shell. This is referred to as ‘soul saturation’. Once this process begins, the inorganics housing the soul begin to take on a more lifelike appearance, such as the body surface appearing flush with blood despite lacking any. Despite the change in appearance, the inorganics remain unchanged structurally. Unlike actual flesh, or even the original state of the now saturated inorganics, a doll that becomes soul-saturated is surprisingly more resistant to physical damage. Possessed dolls are largely found in the Grand Duchy, due to ongoing study into soul saturation.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg)","physique":"The surface of the possessed doll’s body starts to resemble that of living flesh, with an increased softness and warmth. The previously rigid finish of materials like porcelain or vinyl begins to take on a smoother, more supple appearance. The color of its exterior shifts to include subtle shades of pink, tan, or peach, resembling natural skin tones with more realistic undertones, including potential freckles or blush. As it grows more lifelike, the possessed doll’s movements become fluid and graceful, mimicking the organic ease of human actions. Instead of jerky or mechanical movement, it would exhibit smooth transitions, bending and twisting more naturally. Although it lacks lungs, the possessed doll displays a rhythmic rise and fall in its chest area, creating an illusion of breathing tied to its magical essence, contributing to its growing sense of vitality. Tiny magical pulses create the sensation of a heartbeat, producing gentle thumps or vibrations felt in the chest area. Soft glowing areas beneath the surface flash in sync with these “heartbeats.” The sensation of palpitations may also be linked to its emotional state, causing changes in intensity or rhythm in response to feelings or interactions. The face may begin to reflect emotions more vividly. Subtle muscle movements could create expressions like smiles, frowns, or squints, transforming static features into dynamic expressions. The eyes exhibit depth and emotion, with irises that dilate or shift colors in response to emotional stimuli. The internal magic core begins to mimic the function of a heart, circulating magical energy throughout the body, serving as a symbol of life. Though devoid of blood, the magical core creates a sensation akin to flowing energy through the limbs, adding to the realism of its movement and interactions. The hair begins to exhibit movement, responding to changes in temperature or emotional states, resembling the natural flow of hair rather than simply being static or styled. Overall, edges and joints appear less rigid; transitions between parts of the body smooth out, providing an impression of continuity that resembles a living being rather than a construct.","coloring":"Mana can be seen glowing beneath the body’s surface, circulating through the body like blood. The default blue glow in the eyes may change color, granting more individuality like natural eye color.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Living Doll","Evolves into: Awakened Doll","Titles: Construct, Living Doll, Possessed Doll","Feature:","[Form: (material type)] - Body is made of inorganics.","[Separable] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows major appendages and head to harmlessly separate from the torso and reattach.","[Replaceable Parts] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows them to swap their parts at will.","Stats:","Strength - E","Precision - E","Intelligence - C","Vitality - B","Speed - E","Skills:","Resilient [Fatigue (caused by hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Suffocation] E","Hardening C","Resistance F [Physical]","Alchemy F","4 total Secondary skills","Equipment:","Natural Weapons F","Natural Armor F (Light or Heavy)","Perks:","[Evolved] - gain the title evolved. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others of your racial tree.","Choose 1:","[Vitality upgrade] - receive Resistance [Physical] F or upgrade the same by one grade for free","Special Movement F [Fall to Pieces] (14 points) - your body can disassemble as part of an action in order to navigate various obstacles and attacks. While disassembled or in the process of disassembling, you can still move."],"evolvesInto":"Awakened Doll","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/construct-intermediate-possessed-doll-1.webp","assets/races/construct-intermediate-possessed-doll-2.webp"],"aliases":["Living Doll","Possessed Doll"]},{"id":"construct-ascended-awakened-doll","name":"Awakened Doll","tree":"Construct","stage":"Ascended","description":"When soul saturation reaches 100%, the possessed doll is considered to have evolved into an awakened doll. Features continue to become increasingly lifelike. The body runs on mana circulated by a core, much like a heart pumping blood. The shell of the body is now seamless; all joints, hinges, gears, and other machinations are covered by a membrane that bends and folds like flesh. The face is fully capable of emoting, and the eyes may even blink periodically (though having no need to). The body as a whole, as well as certain features like nails and hair, may start growing over time similar to the organic counterpart. In addition to the nigh indistinguishable lifelike appearance, the doll now gains control of the soul saturation process that morphed its inanimate body. Transmutation powers are now able to be harnessed and used to augment the self and surroundings. The number of known awakened dolls can be counted on one hand. Some say there used to be more, but there is no trace of them in current memory.","lifespan":"","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg)","physique":"The exterior of the Awakened Doll has transformed into a flawless surface that resembles human skin, smooth and supple. All internal machinery, including joints and gears, is now hidden beneath a membrane-like layer, allowing for natural movement. The facial structure perfectly emulates human characteristics, with defined cheekbones, a soft jawline, and a mouth that can express a full range of emotions. Subtle variations in skin tone hint at warmth and vitality. The eyes are now vividly colored and capable of blinking, reflecting a spectrum of emotions. The eyes appear to have depth, resembling the way real eyes capture light, enhancing their realism. The breathing is now distinctly rhythmic and organic, with a chest that expands and contracts in a lifelike manner, despite retaining its magical essence. The glow of the mana core is visible through the skin, pulsing gently in sync with the artificial heartbeat. Hair may now grow and be styled, appearing playful and lively, while nails can also grow, appearing naturally manicured. The doll exhibits fluid and expressive movements, utilizing gestures and postures that resonate with its emotional state. The Awakened Doll can consciously control the soul saturation process, allowing it to manipulate its own features and magical abilities. This newfound agency may lead to further enhancements in appearance and functionality. The doll can utilize transmutation abilities to affect its environment, altering objects, reshaping materials, or creating temporary enhancements for itself or allies. The Awakened Doll’s powers may extend beyond self-augmentation; they can change surroundings to either facilitate protection, create advantages in combat, or manipulate pathways and structures.","coloring":"Mana can be seen glowing beneath the body’s surface, circulating through the body like blood. The eyes may also radiate soft light or change shade in response to feelings, giving them a captivating quality.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Possessed Doll","Titles: Construct, Living Doll, Possessed Doll","Feature:","[Form: (material type)] - Body is made of inorganics.","[Separable] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows major appendages and head to harmlessly separate from the torso and reattach.","[Replaceable Parts] (7) - Unique functionality of a construct that allows them to swap their parts at will.","Stats:","Strength - C","Precision - C","Intelligence - A","Vitality - S","Speed - C","Skills:","Transmutation E","Regeneration E","Resilient [Fatigue (caused by hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Suffocation] E","Hardening A","Resistance D [Physical]","Alchemy C","6 total Secondary skills","Equipment:","Natural Weapons E","Natural Armor E (Light or Heavy)","Perks:","[Apex] - gain the title Apex. Something about your physiology or aura identifies to others you are of a higher species than your peers. Gain a +1 to social exchanges with others. Can stack with evolved title bonus if speaking with members of their own tree.","[Singularity] - character gains a level of existence and self awareness that makes their status of being alive unquestioned and acknowledged by the world. Character can no longer be belittled or looked down on for being a construct.","Choose 1:","[Automaton Genesis] - gain the ability to impart your essence into an inanimate object and generate a single construct life. Cannot be larger than size Large. Construct must follow rules of D-grade Companion skill. Can only have one construct made in this way at a time.","[Automaton Army] - gain the ability to manipulate constructs within 100 feet of you. Constructs higher than D-grade resist. Mind Shield D counters this perk. Can combo with PCs to override resistance. Narrator discretion."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/construct-ascended-awakened-doll-1.webp","assets/races/construct-ascended-awakened-doll-2.webp"],"aliases":["Awakened Doll","Living Doll","Possessed Doll"]},{"id":"hybrid-mundane-half-elf","name":"Half-Elf","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Mundane","description":"The product of an elf and human reproducing, half-elves are often torn between the respective worlds of their parents. The chaotic and adventurous spirit of the humans clashes with the loyal devotion the elves have towards nature. One constant among half-elves is that they are usually educated. Whether they put their knowledge to use in politics or as part of an adventuring party is anyone's guess. Half-elves are not new, but the demographic has seen a marked increase in the past 50 years since the War of the Races, particularly in Ryke and Widersia.","lifespan":"180 years","height":"Men: 5' 5\" to 6' 3\" (165.1--190.5 cm) Women: 5' 3\" to 6' 1\" (160.02--185.42 cm)","weight":"Male: 114–220 lbs (51.71–99.79 kg) Female: 107–202 lb (48.53–91.63 kg)","physique":"Half-elves tend to have a lean and athletic build, combining the gracefulness of elves with the sturdiness of humans. This often results in a physique that is agile and adaptable. They tend to age more slowly than humans but faster than elves, often appearing youthful for much of their lives.","coloring":"Skin tones can vary widely, reflecting their human ancestry, ranging from fair to tan to darker shades. Hair color and texture can also vary, with half-elves often having a mix of human and elven characteristics, such as straight or wavy hair in various natural colors. Half-elves typically have pointed ears, though not as pronounced as those of full elves.","historicalFigures":["Count Hadi Sadek (Ryke)"],"relations":["Friendly towards Fae and Prime trees","Neutral towards Construct and Beast trees","Hostile towards Monster tree"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 42 points","Titles: Prime, Fae, Hybrid, Half-Elf","Feature:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","[Ears: Pointy] - Normal fleshy ears that come to a point at the top.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Magic F (7)","Educated F (7)","Perk:","[Born For These] - get one 7pt discount per racial tree of which you are a part. Each discount must be used on purchases made for mundane racial requirements of each parent tree."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"42 points","images":["assets/races/hybrid-mundane-half-elf-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-mundane-half-elf-2.webp"],"aliases":["Half-Elf"]},{"id":"hybrid-mundane-augur","name":"Augur","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Mundane","description":"Augurs, or augs, were a test group of humans enhanced with orichalcum or mithril modifications in an effort to surpass the human condition. Orichalcum subjects needed far less maintenance and repair, but the utility of the mithril subjects made upkeep costs tolerable. Augers were first made in the Grand Duchy of Roran where magitech research enabled the creation of cybernetics. Healing magic was good enough to reduce rejection and allow grafting synthetics to body parts. It also enabled a level of crafting that would work with the body rather than crude and imperfect parts more common for the time period. Regular body parts were frail and not particularly customizable. Augs are sturdy, superior in functionality, and designer chic. Even those weaker in magic could suddenly pull off feats of magic and power with augs. However in modern times, augs are a costly thing, and the quality of augs and their installations varies greatly. When war is off, their usefulness wanes. Augs were used alongside fullers in the Separation War that split the duchy from the Ororoot Empire (West). Since those days, augs are possible to find in Widersia and the Otenzian Empire (East). Steam and clockwork augs and half golem augs from the Otenzian Empire are not as pristine or top-of-the-line, but they are functional and typically superior to the average person.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"6’ to 8’ (1.8–2.4 m)","weight":"400–800 lbs (180–360 kg)","physique":"Augmenters have human bodies with obvious mechanized attachments. Their bodies are usually lean and muscular. As a rule, there is more organic body than inorganic.","coloring":"Mechanical parts, particularly the eyes or weapon attachments, may glow from mana power sources.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Titles: Prime, Construct, Hybrid, Augur","Feature:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","Purchases from the Augment list go in this section of the character sheet","Stats:","Track Sentience here","C-grade character","Skills:","(Prime) Choose one:","2 magic skills/affinities","2 martial skills/techniques","2 secondary skills","(Construct) Requirements:","One (1) defensive skill","Two (2) secondary skills","Perk:","[Born For These] - get one 7pt discount per racial tree of which you are a part. Each discount must be used on purchases made for mundane racial requirements of each parent tree."],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/hybrid-mundane-augur-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-mundane-augur-2.webp"],"aliases":["Augur"]},{"id":"hybrid-mundane-cyborg","name":"Cyborg","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Mundane","description":"Cyborgs are organic beings that have received mechanical replacements for organs and limbs in order to resume normal life. Where augurs are organic beings specifically enhanced with combat-capable attachments, cyborgs may be ordinary noncombatants that just needed a new hand or leg. Generally speaking, cyborgs are fairly common since magical healing isn’t always available or affordable, but they tend to be more common as one gets closer to the major dealers in such attachments: the Grand Duchy and Widersia.","lifespan":"Refer to racial tree of organic race","height":"Any Tiny: Under 2' (61 cm) tall/long Small: 2' to 4' (61–122 cm) feet tall/long Medium: 4'1\" to 7'11\" (124–241 cm) tall/long Large: 8' to 16' (2.43–4.87 m) tall/long Huge: Over 16' (4.87 m) tall/long","weight":"Any Tiny: Under 8 lbs (3.62 kg) Small: 8 to 60 lbs (3.62–27.21 kg) Medium: 61 to 499 lbs (27.66–226.34 kg) Large: 500 to 4000 lbs (2 tons)(226.79–1.81 mt) Huge: Over 4000 lbs (2 tons)(1.81 mt)","physique":"Cyborgs typically range from 5.5 to 7.5 feet (1.7 to 2.3 meters), depending on their origin and design. Their height may be slightly enhanced through mechanical legs or other body modifications. The physique often maintains a generally human form, with muscle tone that may be enhanced through mechanical augmentation. The body can appear more athletic or robust due to cybernetic enhancements. Features may resemble origin race, but specific augmentations can create variations, such as broader shoulders or reinforced limbs. Cyborgs might have a combination of organic skin and synthetic coverings. Parts of the body could be exposed metal, showing circuitry or intricate designs beneath a transparent layer. Where mechanical parts connect with organic flesh, the transition is typically smooth, minimizing visual disruption. Arms and legs may feature various enhancements that provide increased strength, precision, or capabilities (e.g., enhanced grip, weapon integration). These limbs might be bulkier or more stylized than typical appendages. Joints may be reinforced with mechanical components, allowing for greater range of motion or enhanced durability. The face retains origin race characteristics but may include features like an enhanced visual interface or mechanical parts (e.g., augmented eyes or built-in communication devices). Cybernetic enhancements might give the eyes a distinct appearance, such as glowing pupils, multi-colored lenses, or the ability to change focus or zoom. The internal structure combines organic organs with mechanical components, such as a heart or power source that could be synthetic. Depending on the extent of the mechanical enhancements, cyborgs can weigh between 150 to 300 lbs (approximately 68 to 136 kg), with heavily augmented individuals being on the heavier side due to metal components. The overall look tends to have a sleek, advanced aesthetic, often featuring visible technological designs, glowing elements, and a combination of matte and shiny surfaces. Cyborgs may have individualized styles based on their personality or purpose, with features that reflect their unique enhancements.","coloring":"Mechanical parts, particularly the eyes or weapon attachments, may glow from mana power sources.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 63 points","Titles: (Prime or Beast or Fae), Construct, Hybrid, Cyborg","Features:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","[Mechanical Parts] - Creature possesses inorganic body parts.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Precision - E (7)","Intelligence - E (7)","Vitality - E (7)","Skills:","Resilient F [type] (7)","Artisan [Tinkerer] F (7)","Athletics F (7)","Equipment: Natural Armor F or Natural Weapons F (14)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"63 points","images":["assets/races/hybrid-mundane-cyborg-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-mundane-cyborg-2.webp"],"aliases":["(Prime or Beast or Fae)","Cyborg"]},{"id":"hybrid-mundane-felinite","name":"Felinite","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Mundane","description":"Felinites are feline hybrids that possess transformation abilities that allow them to transition between bestial and humanoid forms. Their features are a mishmash of breeds from the Felis genus. Their back paws are patterned after the black footed cat. Their front paws (or arms and hands in humanoid form) bear the pattern of a jungle cat. The face and ears resemble the Chinese mountain cat. Finally, their tail is that of the European wild cat. In the world of IH, felinites are categorized under the ‘Animora’ family, which consists of Fae born from the souls of dead animals. The rebirth is credited to nearby concentrations of mana. In the case of Felinites, they are born from the souls of dead animals of the ‘Felis’ genus.","lifespan":"82.5 years","height":"Male: 13” to 16” (33–41 cm) Female: 10” to 14” (25–36 cm)","weight":"Male: 12–15 lbs (5.4–6.8 kg) Female: 8–12 lbs (3.6–5.4 kg)","physique":"Small-sized feline, similar in stature to a small domestic cat but more robust and muscular. Sleek yet sturdy build, allowing for agility and strength. The physique combines the elongated limbs of the jungle cat with the stocky robustness of the Chinese mountain cat, resulting in a well-balanced and powerful form. The head is broad with a slightly rounded shape, featuring pronounced cheekbones. It exhibits a strong jaw structure, giving the felinite a confident and intelligent appearance. Medium to large ears, pointed with tufted tips reminiscent of the Chinese mountain cat, providing excellent hearing abilities. Thick and medium-length coat that is soft to the touch, with a mix of colors ranging from tawny to grayish-brown. Long and bushy tail, usually adorned with dark rings or a darker tip, aiding in balance and communication. The tail's expressive movements contribute to their social interaction. Strong and agile legs, designed for both climbing and running. The paws are larger than typical cats, equipped with retractable claws adapted for grip on varying terrains. The felinite is known for its playful yet stealthy nature, blending the playful curiosity of the jungle cat with the cautious intelligence of the European wild cat. It is a versatile hunter, able to adapt to diverse habitats and environments.","coloring":"The fur features subtle stripes or spots, aiding in camouflage within various environments. The underbelly is lighter, providing contrast and further enhancing its natural disguise.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 112 points","Titles: Fae, Beast, Hybrid, Felinite","Features:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","[Fur] - Naturally occurring body hair that covers part or all exterior surfaces of the body.","[Luminous] - Some or all of the above feature glows softly.","[Eyes: Bestial] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Ears: Cat] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a cat.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Retractable] (7) - Concealment skill - The above feature can be withdrawn into the creatures form to hide it from view.","Stats:","Strength - E (7)","Intelligence - D (14)","Vitality - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Skills:","Fast F (7)","Magic F (7)","Heightened Senses E [Smell/Hearing] (14)","Transformation F (28)","All points must be spent before upgrading","Languages [Sylvan, Woodland Animal] (0)","Climbing F (7)"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"112 points","images":["assets/races/hybrid-mundane-felinite-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-mundane-felinite-2.webp"],"aliases":["Felinite"]},{"id":"hybrid-mundane-glacial-fox","name":"Glacial Fox","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Mundane","description":"A rarely seen construct race that appears as a fox made of ice. It is known they were created, but the creator remains unknown. Glacial foxes behave mostly how a normal fox would, but they display an intimate understanding of the frozen world. Some revere them as a kind of guardian spirit that leads the lost traveler to the border of their icy domain. Others say they are merely tricksters that would just as soon bury you in the snow as lead you to safety.","lifespan":"Immortal, can still be destroyed in combat","height":"36” long, not including tail 15” at shoulder","weight":"60.7 lbs (27.5 kg)","physique":"The body of a Glacial Fox appears slightly bulkier than a typical fox, with defined musculature to suggest strength while maintaining an elegant, streamlined shape. The ice appears slightly translucent, reflecting light and creating a sparkling effect, akin to frozen water catching the sun. The coat resembles soft, delicate ice crystals or frost instead of traditional fur, giving it a shimmering, ethereal quality. Similar to typical foxes, the ears are large and pointed, perhaps with a crystalline structure that resembles icy spires. The eyes are bright and glowing, with hues ranging from icy blue to deep azure, conveying emotions and intelligence. The nose would be darker and more defined, with a mouth that retains a certain warmth, allowing for expressive facial movements. The legs are sturdy yet graceful, with ice-like coloration and shimmering effects that reflect movement. The paws display a unique adaptation for gripping snowy or icy surfaces, perhaps with small ice “claws” that enhance grip without causing harm. The tail is long and bushy, flowing behind the fox and resembling a plume of snow or ice, possibly with a hint of frosty sparkle. While primarily resembling a traditional fox in terms of movement and agility, this living ice entity may exhibit gentle luminescence when active or during emotional states, creating an enchanting spectacle.","coloring":"The color of the fur varies from pure white to bluish or crystal-like hues, depending on environmental conditions and the type of ice.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Total Cost: 133 points","Titles: Beast, Construct, Hybrid, Glacial Fox","Feature:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","[Quadruped] - Creature has four legs.","[Ears: Fox] - Bestial ears shaped like those of a fox.","[Bestial Eyes] - Typically no or very little white showing. Pupil shape falls into one of three main types: horizontally elongated, circular, or vertically elongated.","[Muzzle] - The mouth and nose region on bestial races that extends out from the face.","[Serrated Teeth] - Sharp or jagged teeth perfect for tearing flesh.","[Claws] - Sturdy, usually pointed, nails that grow out from bestial digits.","[Tail] - An extra appendage typically formed by an elongated tailbone extending from the base of the spine.","[Ice Body] - The character's body is composed entirely of unmelting, magically infused ice.","[Rime Hide] F (14) - Natural Armor - Body is made of magically enhanced ice that acts as armor.","[Core] F (14) - Natural Catalyst - The character's core allows them to conduct magical abilities.","Stats:","Intelligence - E (7)","Speed - E (7)","Vitality - D (14)","Skills:","Special Movement F [Ice Walk] (7)","[Ice Walk] - Character is able to move across ice normally.","Affinity F [Ice] (7)","Control Environment F (7)","Magic F (7)","Heightened Sense F [Hearing] (7)","Sixth Sense F [Heat] (7)","Sixth Sense F [Manavision] (7)","Resilient [Fatigue (caused by hunger, thirst, lack of sleep); Arctic] E (14)","Resistance F [Cold] (7)","Equipment: Natural Armor F"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"133 points","images":["assets/races/hybrid-mundane-glacial-fox-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-mundane-glacial-fox-2.webp"],"aliases":["Glacial Fox"]},{"id":"hybrid-intermediate-dhampir","name":"Dhampir","tree":"Hybrid","stage":"Intermediate","description":"Occasionally, when a vampire thrall feeds on fae blood, they diverge from the main vampire evolutionary tree and become a vampire hybrid known as a dhampir. The fae influence seems to quell the insatiable hunger of the thrall and grants them some composure. Additionally, they become able to walk in the daylight. These changes are beneficial for the thrall, which is exactly why the mainline vampires don’t take kindly to it. Dhampirs are usually persecuted by their peers and elders.","lifespan":"100 years","height":"Male: 5'10\" to 6'2\" (178–188 cm) Female: 5'4\" to 5'10\" (163–178 cm)","weight":"Male: 150–230 lbs (68–104 kg) Female: 110–180 lbs (50–82 kg)","physique":"Dhampirs possess a lean, athletic physique, resulting from agility and strength from their vampiric lineage. They have defined muscles and a well-proportioned, agile frame. Their movements tend to be fluid and graceful, reflecting both human athleticism and vampiric agility. They have angular or sharp facial features, such as high cheekbones and defined jawlines, giving them a striking appearance. Hair may be worn long, flowing, or styled in ways that highlight their dual nature, possibly reflecting both practicality and aesthetics. Dhampirs generally have longer limbs in proportion to their bodies, contributing to their speed and agility. Their hands have finesse, capable of both delicate movements and powerful actions, reflecting their hybrid skills. Dhampirs often exude a certain charisma or allure, making them captivating figures. This quality can be enhanced by their confident body language and expressive demeanor. Their mixed heritage grants them resilience against certain attacks and supernatural effects, contributing to a robust overall appearance.","coloring":"Dhampirs often have a complexion that reflects their vampiric side, typically pale but can also exhibit a warm tan or olive hue, particularly if they have spent time in the sun. Some dhampirs might display faint, mystical markings or veins that hint at their supernatural heritage. Their eyes can be more vibrant and reflective, possibly exhibiting unusual colors (like amber, deep red, or striking blue) that hint at their vampiric lineage. Hair color can vary widely, from dark shades (deep black or brown) to lighter tones (blonde or red), often with a glossy quality that can appear almost unnatural.","historicalFigures":["N/A"],"relations":["Respect elder vampires","Neutral to all Trees"],"requirements":["Evolves from: Thrall","Titles: Monster, Thrall, Fae, Hybrid, Dhampir","Feature:","[Mixed Race] (7) - Allows the purchase of one additional racial tree title.","[Fangs] - Elongated canine teeth used to puncture flesh and draw blood.","[Blood Drinker] (7) - Creature derives nutrition from drinking the blood of other creatures.","[Darkvision] F (7) - Feature Skill - Eyes adapted to using every bit of light present to see in natural darkness when otherwise you couldn't. Everything is rendered grayscale.","Stats:","Strength - D","Intelligence - B","Vitality - D","Speed - D","Skills:","Fast E","Fighting Style C [weapon type]","4 techs","Magic C","Heightened Sense E [Hearing, Smell]","Sixth Sense E [Danger]","Regeneration E","Resilient E [Fatigue - doesn’t need food, water, sleep; Suffocation]","Resistance E [Slashing]","Deception F","Equipment: Natural Weapons F"],"evolvesInto":"","totalCost":"","images":["assets/races/hybrid-intermediate-dhampir-1.webp","assets/races/hybrid-intermediate-dhampir-2.webp"],"aliases":["Dhampir","Thrall"]}];
